},
	[26600]={ language="Kroward discovered the FRB-265411 signal (fast radio burst signal) that appears every 28 days and lasted for a year. Kroward speculates it might be information from an extraterrestrial civilization, so after discussions, decided to respond to the FRB-265411 signal."
},
	[26601]={ language="In the Tashkomir Grand Canyon, Kroward began constructing the 【Lorimer Signal Tower】 to respond to the FRB-265411 signal. The 【Lorimer Signal Tower】 sent out a beam carrying human DNA information and telecommunications signals about the stage of human civilization, and is awaiting a response."
},
	[26602]={ language="Due to Shogger's invasion, Earth's basic scientific research has come to a halt."
},
	[26603]={ language="Lawton Institute of Bionic Mechanics (L.I.B.M) developed the first generation of humanoid military combat robots (Resister combat robot), abbreviated as R.C.R. However, due to energy constraints and an outdated command system, the combat efficiency of R.C.R is not high, only able to complete basic tasks."
},
	[26604]={ language="Rumor has it that the Joshburg government secretly trained a combat unit—F.S.C.F, but little is known about the unit's information."
},
	[26605]={ language="The leading woman at Leistance Security Bureau is a Legendary AIMBS named Zeila. Zeila's unyielding spirit constantly provides a Morale Boost to all Leistance staff. Her personal plaque is currently housed in the Leistance Heroes Memorial."
},
	[26606]={ language="Originally the Joshburg National Guard, after the Anchor Crisis, traditional forces from two other countries were gradually incorporated, changing it to the Resistance Army, mainly used to combat Shogger and Fission Forms, as well as various related cleanup and support tasks."
},
	[26607]={ language="After the Anchor Crisis broke out, Joshburg used his diplomatic skills to convince Liboseir and Kroward to jointly establish the Lord Federation, sharing technology and resources to jointly resist Shogger."
},
	[26608]={ language="The Lord Federation Independent Armed Forces, established after the Anchor Crisis, is mainly composed of special forces from three countries of the Lord Federation. They have a higher combat capability compared to the Resistance Headquarters, often acting as a support unit for the Leistance Campaign teams. The unit is equipped with a new generation of bionic mechanical arms, featuring high Campaign capabilities and self-repair abilities."
},
	[26609]={ language="The independent organization formed after the Anchor Crisis was established by Alice Laboratory, Lawton Institute of Bionic Mechanics, and 84laboratory. It's for Enhance, centrally dispatching all AIMBS Operators, with several combat teams under the Security Bureau."
},
	[26610]={ language="This project is a gene optimization initiative secretly launched by Shawn Bio Technology, aimed at enhancing human intelligence and abilities, curing diseases, and extending human lifespan. However, the project was quietly halted halfway, and no one knows the exact reason to this day."
},
	[26611]={ language="Anima Crystals are an Energy substance refined from Anima Crystal ores, with visible Energy streaks flowing on the surface. Initially, they appeared in veins near anchors, and later, Anima Crystal conversion technology was discovered. This allows Anima Crystals to be directly converted into objects. Additionally, because Anima Crystal ores are also a high concentration of Energy, they were later developed into an energy source."
},
	[26612]={ language="Anima Crystal is a derivative of Primal Crystal combined with local elements, mainly used for regular Shogger Energy restoration. It contains more impurities and the purity of the Energy it holds is relatively low."
},
	[26613]={ language="Currently, there are very few known Primal Crystals ores in the world. What everyone knows is that in Anchor Space, you can find Primal Crystals ores, but it's extremely difficult to obtain them."
},
	[26614]={ language="The fundamental structure of the Anima Crystal is the Metatron cube lattice. It's a mystical crystal containing cosmic Energy. With the current human mastery of crystal energy extraction technology, only fire, electric, and ice elements can be extracted."
},
	[26615]={ language="Taino Star"
},
	[26616]={ language="Stellar Crystal"
},
	[26617]={ language="Skyborne Barriers"
},
	[26618]={ language="Eternal Night"
},
	[26619]={ language="Shogger"
},
	[26620]={ language="Void Particles"
},
	[26621]={ language="Leistance Security Bureau"
},
	[26622]={ language="Star Council"
},
	[26623]={ language="Anchor Space"
},
	[26624]={ language="Operator (AIMBS)"
},
	[26625]={ language="Linker"
},
	[26626]={ language="Crystal Weapon"
},
	[26627]={ language="Contamination"
},
	[26628]={ language="Void Expanse"
},
	[26629]={ language="Mutant"
},
	[26630]={ language="Coordinator"
},
	[26631]={ language="The terrestrial planet inhabited by humans experienced an interdimensional invasion war called the [Shogger War] a century ago, and has now recovered."
},
	[26632]={ language="Mysterious crystal-like minerals spread across Taino Star, which have a slow self-growth ability. Named Stellar Crystal due to their starry reflection-like colors, under certain conditions, they can trigger supernatural phenomena that current scientific theories can't explain, based on the mental will of the user."
},
	[26633]={ language="The array barriers, composed of 7,200 artificial satellites in geosynchronous orbit around the Taino Star, serve to dynamically obscure Taino Star's cosmic coordinates on a dimensional level, preventing Shogger from executing precise spatial invasions. They are controlled through 18 ground bases and 72 subsidiary bases."
},
	[26634]={ language="The global phenomenon brought about by Skyborne Barriers manifests as overall low visibility on Taino Star. Simply put, once Skyborne Barriers are launched, Taino Star no longer experiences [daytime] and is forever in night."
},
	[26635]={ language="A type of alien cosmic creature that remains not fully understood by the Taino people. It possesses multiple tribe forms, sharing consciousness and spirit through a catalyst called [Shogger Network.] The group structure is similar to an ANT-like society."
},
	[26636]={ language="The visual effect is of dispersing black particles or smoke. When living organisms come into contact with a certain concentration of Void Particles, they become contaminated and turn into Mutants. This process is mostly irreversible."
},
	[26637]={ language="The campaign organization without borders established by the Star Council during the Shogger War, specializes in handling Shogger and related incidents caused by Shogger."
},
	[26638]={ language="The superior organization of Leistance, aimed at gathering resources and forces from around the world to collectively resist Shogger."
},
	[26639]={ language="The passage through which Shogger descended to Taino Star. It's filled with a lot of Void Particles, and only power related to crystals can effectively interfere with targets within the anchor."
},
	[26640]={ language="A remodeled superhuman with superpowers and various abilities, possesses extra resistance to Shogger, is a new generation warrior capable of surviving Anchor Space."
},
	[26641]={ language="Leistance's special battle units primarily serve as psychological anchors for Operators, taking on the side effects when Operators use their abilities and significantly Enhancing the Operators' Campaign capabilities."
},
	[26642]={ language="The standardized armor of Operators. Has been customized based on each Operator's specific abilities."
},
	[26643]={ language="Contamination is an abnormal phenomenon that causes changes in life forms, often accompanied by Crystal accidents. Small amounts of contamination can be cleaned up, but once it surpasses a certain critical point, contamination erupts, and the life form is completely distorted and irreversible."
},
	[26644]={ language="Void Expanse refers to areas contaminated by contamination. The formation of Void Expanse is accompanied by anchors appearing and a large-scale Shogger invasion. After prolonged contamination, the natural environment changes, with the surface covered in masses of black crystals and Void Particles concentration too high for ordinary humans to enter."
},
	[26645]={ language="Life forms altered by contamination are generally called Mutants. Mutants usually lack intelligence, are highly aggressive, and are attracted to sound and light. They seem to have their own evolution system, with higher-level Mutants possessing abilities similar to Operators and appearing even more bizarre."
},
	[26646]={ language="In recent decades, the sudden appearance of unique Mutants has been denied by major powers, who are trying to cover up and eliminate them."
},
	[26647]={ language="Garden Journal"
},
	[26648]={ language="When midnight lanterns bloom in golden splendor, I bid thee join this radiant festival's surrender."
},
	[26701]={ language="Here is the Operator's current Battery skills (activation consumes some Battery). The skill icon will display its skill level and skill positioning. Unlocked skills require reaching the corresponding star level to unlock."
},
	[26702]={ language="Here is the Operator's current Energy Burst (activation consumes Energy ). The skill icon will display its skill level and skill positioning. Unlocked skills require reaching the corresponding star level to unlock."
},
	[26703]={ language="Tap here to edit the skill positions of the same type. During auto battle, skills are released from left to right in sequence."
},
	[26704]={ language="Breakthrough can comprehensively improve an Operator's basic attributes and increase the Operator's level cap."
},
	[26705]={ language="Breakthrough skills add extra effects to active skills. Corresponding breakthrough skills can be unlocked through Operator breakthrough."
},
	[26706]={ language="Missions are mainly divided into Daily Missions and Weekly Missions. Daily Missions reset at 5 AM every day, and Weekly Missions reset at 5 AM every Monday."
},
	[26707]={ language="Completing various Daily Missions accumulates Activity Points. Upon reaching specific Activity Tiers, you can claim corresponding Tiered Rewards."
},
	[26708]={ language="Tap here to view the buffs you've obtained (you'll need to find clues to obtain buffs within the story)."
},
	[26709]={ language="Full Chapter Exploration (100%) requires clearing all level in the current chapter."
},
	[26710]={ language="Current Level Debuffs can be viewed here. You need to adjust the Operator lineup according to the abnormal environment."
},
	[26711]={ language="After clearing any level, the difficulty of the level for the rest of the week cannot be changed again."
},
	[26712]={ language="Current Obtained Buffs can be viewed here. You can get matrices by clearing the level."
},
	[26713]={ language="Multiple Bosses appear every Monday at 5:00 AM based on the Linker's level. When multiple Bosses appear, an Operator can only participate in the Challenge of one Boss."
},
	[26714]={ language="Defeating Bosses under specified conditions grants stars. Accumulating certain stars unlock level rewards."
},
	[26715]={ language="Challenge attempt resets at 5 AM every day. Attempts are only consumed upon successful defeat of a Boss."
},
	[26716]={ language="This is the restart button. Tapping it will reset the current maze (the treasure chest rewards will not reset)."
},
	[26717]={ language="You can view the current debuff of this level here. Linker needs to adjust the Operator lineup according to the abnormal environment."
},
	[26718]={ language="Here you can see the obtained buff that you can get after defeating monsters."
},
	[26719]={ language="Here is the number of remaining treasure chests in the maze."
},
	[26720]={ language="When you can't find Alicia, click here to quickly locate Alicia's position."
},
	[26721]={ language="Tap here to view the current status of Operators in the squad."
},
	[26722]={ language="There are 4 challenge attempts available each day, and you can choose your favorite Operator information to collect."
},
	[26723]={ language="Each season of Arena lasts 30 days.When the season countdown reaches 0,all players' points will be reset according to certain rules and the season Settlement Rewards will be distributed via in-game mail."
},
	[26724]={ language="Rewards are divided into daily rewards and season rewards. Daily rewards are sent via in-game email based on the current rank of Linker at 5:00 AM every day."
},
	[26725]={ language="Arena defense lineup is initially set to the player's current attack lineup. Tap to enter the defense lineup editing interface to change Operators and formation."
},
	[26726]={ language="Points can be earned by pairing up and defeating other Linkers, and the higher the points, the higher the rank."
},
	[26727]={ language="Arena offers 3 free Challenge attempts each day. After these 3 attempts, each additional Challenge requires the use of 1 Arena Ticket, which can be obtained through the regular exchange."
},
	[26728]={ language="The Arena attack queue is initially set to the player's current attack queue. Tap to enter the attack queue editing interface to change the Operator and formation."
},
	[26729]={ language="The event lasts for 30 days, don't forget to claim your target rewards before it ends."
},
	[26730]={ language="Participating in activities can help achieve various activity goals, so remember to claim them."
},
	[26731]={ language="There are all sorts of goods in the night market, but you need Unlimited Coins to exchange for them."
},
	[26732]={ language="The Unlimited Ranking is the Honor Roll of Sub-Story, although there's no reward for reaching first place."
},
	[26733]={ language="Tap here to view the loot currently in possession (loot can be obtained by clearing normal level)"
},
	[26734]={ language="Tap here to reset the current level's Challenge progress. Meanwhile, the level Boss will be randomly generated, and any acquired loot will also be reset."
},
	[26735]={ language="Operator Ascension mainly enhances the Operator's basic attributes and the damage coefficient of regular attacks. Ascension materials can be obtained from the Anima collection stage."
},
	[26736]={ language="The abnormal environment buff not only gives all enemies in this level an additional boost but also weakens the operation ability of our Operators."
},
	[26737]={ language="Matrix buffs mainly enhance our Operators' operation abilities (choosing wisely and having the right matrix is key to clear the stage). Matrices will also reset after resetting a stage."
},
	[26738]={ language="This section shows the cumulative activity of Missions. When the cumulative activity for the day reaches different stages, you can tap the corresponding stage to claim different rewards."
},
	[26739]={ language="You can check the key points for clearing each level here."
},
	[26740]={ language="Special types of level cannot change action configurations."
},
	[26741]={ language="Subconscious Deepseek has 5 stages, each with 5 difficulty level. Each level has different enemy Feature. Understanding the enemy's Feature is the key to successfully passing the challenge."
},
	[26742]={ language="You can directly enter Arena supplies from here, and use the Arena License to purchase many rare items."
},
	[26743]={ language="Arena attack queue is initially set as the player's current Story team. Tap to enter the attack queue editing interface to change Operators and formation."
},
	[26744]={ language="The Gift Workshop can produce various gifts that different Operators like."
},
	[26745]={ language="The Model encapsulation workshop can produce Models of different qualities."
},
	[26746]={ language="Tap here to view the currently produced materials."
},
	[26747]={ language="The material production workshop can produce various Operator growth materials."
},
	[26748]={ language="The Research Support Workshop can produce supplies for the research center."
},
	[26749]={ language="Here are the mandatory requirements for dispatch. Operators in the dispatch squad must meet the following requirements."
},
	[26750]={ language="Here is the time required for dispatch."
},
	[26751]={ language="Here is our lineup selection area, where you can choose suitable Operators for operation based on the Tutorial opponents."
},
	[26752]={ language="Here is Tutorial opponent's lineup and formation."
},
	[26753]={ language="Here is the current Tutorial prompt information for the Tutorial level. Using the key information in it can help you complete the Tutorial faster."
},
	[26754]={ language="Here is the place to prepare for Operator, and you need to read tips and information to make a reasonable choice in using Operator."
},
	[26755]={ language="Here is the difficulty switch button for the current Boss. Tap to view and switch between different difficulties."
},
	[26756]={ language="Here is the number of stars needed until the next reward."
},
	[26757]={ language="Here is the conditions required to obtain different stars."
},
	[26758]={ language="Here is the current Abyssal Resonance effects that Operators will experience in the battle environment."
},
	[26759]={ language="Here is the list of Operators locked to the current leader. Locked Operators can only be used to Challenge this Boss in the current cycle."
},
	[26760]={ language="You get a certain number of Challenge attempts daily. Clearing the Tutorial mode doesn't use up Challenge attempts, and completing a Challenge doesn't lock an Operator."
},
	[26761]={ language="This section shows the reward reset time. Tap to redeem to directly jump to the Store."
},
	[26762]={ language="Here is the list of Bosses. Tap to switch between different Bosses for a Challenge."
},
	[26763]={ language="Constructing and upgrading buildings require production robots in Base. They can also be used to speed up Resource production. Once used up, their availability automatically recovers over time."
},
	[26764]={ language="The number on the left is the total Electric Power consumed by all buildings, and the number on the right is the total Electric Power provided by all power Models. The total Electric Power required for upgrading and constructing buildings cannot exceed the total Electric Power."
},
	[26765]={ language="Titanium Materials are essential for constructing and upgrading buildings and can be produced by building a Refine factory."
},
	[26766]={ language="After tapping to open the Overview interface, you can quickly view and edit the Operator's stationing status in each building."
},
	[26767]={ language="Tap to enter build mode, where you can construct and upgrade buildings."
},
	[26768]={ language="Here is the Electric Power provided by the inspected Model."
},
	[26769]={ language="Here is the number of power Model charging robots produced per hour."
},
	[26770]={ language="Tap here to open the Operator stationing interface. Operators specializing in Motivation Model related Base skills can accelerate robot charging."
},
	[26771]={ language="Here are the parameters related to dispatch.Tap the Operator dispatch icon to enter the Operator dispatch interface."
},
	[26772]={ language="Tap here to open the Operator stationing interface. Operators with skills related to Dispatch Dock can reduce the time for dispatch recovery attempts."
},
	[26773]={ language="Here is the production progress of Titanium Materials. When the Depot is full, production cannot continue. Tap the robot icon at the top right to consume production robots and speed up production."
},
	[26774]={ language="Tap here to access the Operator stationing interface. Operators with Base skills related to the Refine plant can reduce the processing time of Titanium Materials."
},
	[26775]={ language="Here is the production progress of the Operation EXP Report. When the Depot is full, production cannot proceed. Tap the robot icon in the upper right corner to use production robots to speed up production."
},
	[26776]={ language="Tap here to open the Operator stationing interface. Operators with skills related to the Tutorial Model Base can reduce the processing time for Operation EXP Report."
},
	[26777]={ language="Here is the current production progress of processing materials. Tap the plus sign to enter the material processing selection interface."
},
	[26778]={ language="Tap here to open the Operator stationing interface. Operators with Production Line-related Base skills can reduce processing time for different materials."
},
	[26779]={ language="Here is the comfort level of Dorm. Arranging different furniture can increase comfort, and upgrading Dorm level can increase the comfort limit."
},
	[26780]={ language="This shows the fatigue recovery rate of Operators in the dormitory. The higher the comfort, the faster the recovery rate of fatigue."
},
	[26781]={ language="The decor store sells a variety of furniture."
},
	[26782]={ language="Tap [Decorate] to enter the Dorm decoration mode."
},
	[26783]={ language="Tap here to open the Operator stationing interface. Operators with Base skills related to dorms can reduce the fatigue recovery time of Operators."
},
	[26784]={ language="Tap to switch different material production tabs. Upgrading the production line level can unlock more material categories."
},
	[26785]={ language="The far left shows the target production materials, while the right side displays the materials and time needed to produce one unit of the target material."
},
	[26786]={ language="Every time you level up in the Battle Record, you can unlock the corresponding level rewards. Tap to enter and view the rewards."
},
	[26787]={ language="4 missions will be reset every 15 days. Completing different missions can earn a large amount of experience in the Battle Record."
},
	[26788]={ language="Increase the level of the Battle Record to earn corresponding talent points. Talent points can be used to activate talent skills, reducing exploration difficulty."
},
	[26789]={ language="The funding from the Secret Line allows you to view the total investment amount handed to the mysterious merchant during the exploration and the corresponding unlocked Store privileges."
},
	[26790]={ language="You can view all collected and uncollected items in the showroom. Collecting a certain number of items allows you to receive generous collection rewards."
},
	[26791]={ language="You can view all the recorded endings in the Collection Room. Unlocking the corresponding plots allows you to receive generous collection rewards."
},
	[26792]={ language="Only SSR quality Model can be Remodelled. The materials consumed for Remodel are Models of the same set type."
},
	[26793]={ language="Choose to consume the same Sigil to increase Refine level."
},
	[26794]={ language="Tap here to open the Operator stationing interface. Operators with skills related to Heart of Flame can increase the production efficiency of other facilities."
},
	[26795]={ language="Here is the start or end time of the event. Tap the Ranking to view the corresponding ranking reward information."
},
	[26796]={ language="Here is the current Boss round. After completing one round of Boss challenges, a new round will begin, and the attributes of the Boss will also increase."
},
	[26797]={ language="Here is the remaining Challenge attempts for the day. When run out, they'll reset at 5 AM the next day."
},
	[26798]={ language="Tap here to view the battle records of Linker within Union for this event."
},
	[26799]={ language="There are a total of 3 war zones, each corresponding to 3 districts."
},
	[26800]={ language="The disturbance index will change based on the overall level of players in the room. Each district must meet the minimum promotion points standard and be in the top 10 of the ranking to be eligible for promotion."
},
	[26801]={ language="Once you select a difficulty this week, it can't be changed. You must clear the previous difficulty first to unlock difficulties beyond 4."
},
	[26802]={ language="You can only claim HP bonuses for different stages once a week."
},
	[26803]={ language="Challenge attempts increase once daily at 5 AM and reset to 1 on Monday at 5 AM."
},
	[26804]={ language="All difficulties are shown here. Once a challenge is completed, the next difficulty will be automatically selected."
},
	[26805]={ language="Here is the total cumulative damage for all difficulty level."
},
	[26806]={ language="Reach a certain amount of total accumulated damage to unlock the corresponding damage rewards."
},
	[26807]={ language="The Challenge attempts reset every day at 5 AM. The highest difficulty can be challenged infinitely, and the record will be the accumulated damage from the highest attempt. (The Boss's HP resets each battle and cannot be killed.)"
},
	[26809]={ language="Only the Union Leader can use Auto-Deploy. When activated, it will assign members to vacant facilities in descending order of their level. (Land Sentinels cannot be auto-deployed.)"
},
	[26810]={ language="Tap to view Union's past match records in the Land Clash."
},
	[26811]={ language="Tap outside the event period to view facility deployment status. During the event, tap to view facility damage status."
},
	[26812]={ language="Tap to set up 2 defense teams. Both teams must be configured before members can be assigned to facilities. Once the event starts, defense teams and Operator stats will be locked (adjustable only during match settlement phases)."
},
	[26813]={ language="Tap to set up 2 attack teams. Attack teams can be freely adjusted during the event. Match results are determined by the outcome of two battles:(Victory conditions: 2 wins, or 1 win & 1 draw. Results in 120 damage to enemy facility and 120 Processing Power reward. Defeat conditions: 2 losses, or 1 loss & 1 draw. Draw conditions: 2 draws, or 1 win & 1 loss. Results in 60 damage to enemy facility and 60 Processing Power reward.)"
},
	[26814]={ language="The Energy Hub can only be attacked when any Energy Base's HP is ≤50%. Destroying facilities grants bonus Processing Power (Energy Hub: 3000; Energy Base: 1200; Energy Pylon: 300)"
},
	[26815]={ language="Land Sentinels can only defend and cannot be used for attack. (They can be auto-deployed.)"
},
