	[43110]={ language="Whenever Electrofury's HP drops by 20%, it leaves the battlefield and summons three different monsters. Defeat them, and Electrofury reappears.\nWhen Electrofury reappears, if its current attribute is countered by the attribute of its last appearance, Electrofury will gain a [30% damage reduction] effect.\nWhen Electrofury reappears, if its current attribute counters the attribute of its last appearance, Electrofury will gain a [30% increased damage] effect."
},
	[43111]={ language="When Electrofury's HP drops below 40%, it enters the next phase, and in this phase, Electrofury will no longer change its attribute.\nIf Electrofury is Ice-attribute, it will gain an Ice Shield every 2 turns. While the shield is active, attackers' attack will be reduced by 20% for 2 turns.\nIf Electrofury is Fire-attribute, each attack will additionally deal 5% of its own attack as Fire damage. This effect can stack up to 10 layers and cannot be dispelled.\nIf Electrofury is Electric-attribute, each attack has a 15% chance to stun one target for 2 turns."
},
	[43112]={ language="When Electrofury's HP drops below 20%, it enters the final phase. At this point, Electrofury gains all the abilities from the previous phase's attributes and additionally increases its attack by 20%."
},
	[43113]={ language="Dean·Lancelots enters, wielding the legendary sword Lancelots in battle."
},
	[43114]={ language="When Dean's HP drops below 70%, he will show a mutated form, using mutant claws to attack enemy units randomly.\nAt the same time, the Legendary Sword Lancelots will awaken as an independent battle unit to assist Dean in battle. When Dean dies, the Legendary Sword Lancelots will also die simultaneously.\nIn this stage, on every odd-numbered turn, Dean will apply the [Enhance Metal] defense effect to himself, covering himself with special metal. At this point, Dean receives 20% physical DMG reduction but takes 20% more electric damage."
},
	[43115]={ language="When Dean's HP drops below 30%, he enters the final stage, during which Dean will once again wield the legendary sword Lancelots for the battle, boosting attack by 25% and CRIT Rate by 30%.\nIn this stage, Dean will always be in the [Enhance Metal] state, reducing physical DMG by 30%, but taking 30% more electric damage.\nMeanwhile, Dean will turn the entire battlefield into a sword graveyard and summon three monsters onto the field. When each monster is defeated individually, it will Revive after three turns; if all three monsters are defeated simultaneously, they cannot Revive and will deal damage equal to 15% of Dean's Max HP.\nWhen Dean dies, all monsters on the field will also die simultaneously."
},
