	[47010]={ language="Real Name: Bartianta\nIdentity: Burksomi dispatched communication personnel\nInterests: Collecting various first-place trophies"
},
	[47011]={ language="Initial Data"
},
	[47012]={ language="Reward"
},
	[47101]={ language="Confidential Before Opening"
},
	[47102]={ language="Stay Tuned"
},
	[47103]={ language="[Stand up, Bartianta. Just being my daughter, and you can't handle this?]\n[There's no time for hesitation on the battlefield.]\n[Tutorial task not complete, it's not break time yet.]\n[Yes, mother!]\n[Continue.]\n[Yes!]\n\nIn the AIMBS Operator exclusive Tutorial room, the woman's stern voice kept ringing out, mixed with the girl's responses and heavy panting.\n\nSometimes passersby at the Tutorial room heard these sounds, stopped for a moment, then shook their heads helplessly and walked away.\n\nThis is daily life at the Burksomi AIMBS Operator Tutorial base. After all, she's a well-known AIMBS instructor, and people are used to it.\n\nBartianta has almost no impression of [mother,] mostly hearsay from others describing her. Her mother, the AIMBS Operator from Burksomi, is like a bloom in the harsh northern winter—bright, resilient, and a figure of admiration and worship. But in her own memory, the most common question her mother asks is:\n\n[Did you complete today's Tutorial task?]\n\nThe hero against Shogger, one of Burksomi's strongest AIMBS Operators, now the Chief Instructor of Burksomi AIMBS Operators... Her child should be just as outstanding.\n\nBartianta herself believed this too, as the daughter of that person, and the daughter of an AIMBS Operator. To live up to the identity, she'd demanded of herself the highest standards from a young age. Even if others saw it as a nearly cruel Tutorial, she'd silently achieve the best results.\n\nMost believed this mother's education was overly harsh, but in the eyes of AIMBS Operators, such strict Tutorials and interactions are perfectly normal.\n\nOne day, her mother asked, [Bartianta, why do you want to become an AIMBS Operator?]\n\n[Because you're an excellent AIMBS Operator, and I want to be excellent like you.]\n\n[Is that the only reason?]\n\n[Do I need another reason?]\n\nHearing her mother's question, Bartianta felt a bit puzzled.\n\n[Bartianta, maybe you don't understand yet, but I can tell you, I don't want to be your goal.] Different from her usual stern Tutorial tone, the mother's voice became gently soft, [You don't have a goal yet, this way you are destined not to achieve true strength.]\n\n[True strength? What is true strength?]\n[Bartianta, the answer needs to be found by yourself.]\n\nSince then, Bartianta asked many strong individuals what true strength was, but each had a different answer, and she never got one that satisfied her.\nWhat is the [true strength] her mother talked about... Even today, Bartianta is pondering in the Tutorial."
},
	[47104]={ language="Information One: [Though she often seems aloof, as long as you don't provoke her, she won't bother you. In a way, she's kind of 'easygoing'... I guess.]\n\nInformation Two: When filming a promo, the photographer suggested she not keep a straight face and to smile, but the preview was too shocking, so the footage was scrapped.\n\nInformation Three: [Incredibly strong battle skills, you can trust her with your back.]"
},
	[47105]={ language="1. Composite Energy Bow: The core structure is the energy ring. Be careful to protect it during use, and if damaged, it's advised to buy a new one.\n\n2. AIMBS Squad Badge: The badge of Bartianta's squad, symbolizing Burksomi's strongest AIMBS squad with the Chief Instructor's autograph on the back.\n\n3. Tutorial Student Medal: First-place medal for the Burksomi AIMBS reserves' Tutorial student competition, shaped like Burksomi's iconic animal—a soaring eagle.\n\n4. Quiver: A backup to prevent running out of Energy during battles, needs regular replenishment.\n\n5. Schedule: Made by Bartianta herself, strictly executed daily, with Tutorial times precise to the second.\n\n6. Energy Ring Care Device: Though Bartianta thinks anything besides Tutorial is a waste of time, she chooses to personally maintain the Energy Bow."
},
	[47106]={ language="Information One: A tutorial fanatic, always either at the tutorial venue or on the way there.\n\nInformation Two: [Tactics don't exist for her. In the face of overwhelming strength, tactics don't really matter, right?]\n\nInformation Three: [Even if it's something she's not interested in, as long as you tell her it's competitive, she'll definitely participate and get first place. She's surprisingly straightforward in that sense.]"
},
	[47107]={ language="On September 1, XXXX, I started studying at the military academy... There is no doubt that I am ranked first in the S-rank entrance examination.\n…\nOn June 1, XXXX, I participated in the AIMBS Operator reserve Tutorial selection today.\nOn June 2, XXXX, selection ended. Even without seeing the results, I know I'm first place. I saw my mother during the award ceremony. Was she smiling? Because I came first?\n…\nOn April 24, XXXX, more classmates have been challenging me lately, which is slightly affecting my Tutorial. But... sparring can be considered a form of Tutorial too, as long as they're not those overconfident guys.\n…\nOn May 21, XXXX, I encountered a senior opponent, and ended in a draw... I admitted he was strong. After asking him for advice, he said that feeling strong is about the overwhelming victory over opponents... Is true strength about that kind of undisputed victory? I see.\n…\nOn July 30, XXXX, I ran into a group of strange people claiming to be my fan club. What is a fan club? Why don't they use their time to focus on their Tutorial instead? Please don't make weird noises when I am in Tutorial. After I said that, they got even more excited. Truly a bunch of odd people. I think I'll find a different place for Tutorial tomorrow.\n…\nOn March 24, XXXX, nothing special happened, spent the whole day in Tutorial.\n…\nOn April 6, XXXX, I got bumped into in the hallway at noon, felt quite novel... not a big deal, the other person apologized and handed me a stack of dessert coupons. I might take a few minutes tomorrow to use them... shouldn't affect Tutorial. Thanks to this classmate.\n…\n On May 8, XXXX, received a competition invitation, the other person left without explaining what it was about... Oh well, whatever the competition is, I won't lose to anyone.\nOn May 9, XXXX, I got first place in a black market cooking competition... Boring.\n…\nOn September 10, XXXX, found a satisfactory Tutorial partner. Briefly asked her what she thought true strength was. She mentioned that someone truly strong, like myself, who is first in everything, is what she aspires to be, which is why she wants to be my partner...\nEven if you say that, it won't reduce the Tutorial volume.\nTrue strength... is it always being first?\nBut even after achieving so many firsts, isn't mother still unsatisfied?\nShe hasn't smiled at me for a long time... Am I not doing enough?\n…\nOn June 30, XXXX, graduated and joined the AIMBS forces. As expected.\nOn July 8, XXXX, first mission perfectly completed... The victory banquet was lavish, but mother didn't attend.\n…\nOn December 30, XXXX, I was forced to shoot a promotional video. I don't like it, but it's an order.\n…\nOn August 1, XXXX, participated in a multinational joint Shogger Campaign Arena. Other AIMBS Operators are formidable, but I'll be stronger. I will be first again in this event.\nOn August 3, XXXX... lost the finals to [Sparkle-Wing] from Selevie, this time the first place... wasn't me.\n——From Bartianta's personal journals."
},
	[47108]={ language="Information One: Actually has a secret hobby of collecting colored contact lenses, never mentioned it to anyone—including mom.\n\nInformation Two: Won the first place medal in a dark cuisine competition."
},
	[47109]={ language="August 5, 2123, cloudy.\nThere are more voices discussing me at the AIMBS Operator base of Burksomi.\nI know what they're saying.\n[Even Bartianta will fail one day?]\n [The Chief Instructor must be very disappointed, right?]\n[Seems like Bartianta isn't the strongest after all.]\n[The myth of being number one has been broken.]\n[Is there someone stronger than Bartianta?]\nThese kinds of comments have been constant these days, and they can be heard even in the Tutorial area.\nUnfortunately, my mother isn't as disappointed as they imagine.\nI believe she doesn't care about the outcome of this competition and hasn't shown disappointment in my failure; I've always been unable to understand her.\n[Although strong, you seem confused inside,] was Sparkle-Wing's final comment to me when the competition ended.\nAm I confused inside? I'm very clear about my goal, which is to be number one.\nI don't know how Sparkle-Wing saw confusion in me, but I feel I must see her again.\n————\n...At the end of the competition, due to my overconfidence in my own strength and underestimating the opponent, disregarding teammates' suggestions and acting hastily, the Burksomi team failed to win the championship, for which I feel deeply guilty.\nBecause I failed to consider teamwork, treating the competition as a personal showcase and neglecting my teammates' tactical support, leading to the loss, I am willing to take full responsibility for this failure. I request that my teammates' ranks and rights be kept intact, and the punishment be directed solely at me.\n…\nBased on the report content above, I hereby apply to join the Burksomi dispatch team to Leistance and request the officer's approval. I will submit a detailed application separately.\nFrom: Bartianta.\n————————\nReply to Bartianta:\nApplication approved.\n(Encrypted message) My daughter, I hope that through this experience, you can learn in Leistance what true strength means. I am always proud of you."
},
	[47110]={ language="Information One: She has no particular preference besides Tutorial, but someone saw her visiting the same dessert shop for several days in a row. After the news spread, [Bartianta's favorite] desserts quickly sold out.\n\nInformation Two: Bartianta doesn't care about anyone besides Sparkle-Wing. Ever since she came to Leistance and reunited with Sparkle-Wing, Bartianta has always looked for opportunities to compete with Sparkle-Wing. Interestingly, despite Bartianta's efforts, they have never faced each other in an official match till now."
},
	[47111]={ language="Real Name: Grinloffin\nIdentity: Zulu Mercenary Group's leader\nInterests: Nature, Hunting, Combat, Extreme Sports Related"
},
	[47112]={ language="The [Reservation] was once a broad term, usually used to refer to settlements around Selevie that retained some of their original appearance. In these settlements, residents did not rely on modern technology, they lived simple lives and had unique tribal cultures. They were often located in specific areas within Selevie's ecological zones but were not subject to the control of city-states and had some autonomy. However, as the environment around Selevie further deteriorated over time, such settlements gradually declined, leaving only one representative behind. From then on, [Reservation] became the exclusive term for this tribe.\n\nThis group has distinctive physical Feature: white hair, golden eyes, and dark skin. They enjoy using various animal bones and horns as unique decorations. The people of the reservation possess innate strength and tenacity, with extreme physical prowess. Relying on their understanding of nature and their combat skills, they can maintain a stable life even in the perilous surroundings of Selevie. They have a unique way of developing Stellar Crystals that can be effectively used in combat to enhance warriors' defensive abilities.\n\nThe tribal belief of the reservation combines nature worship and ancestor worship. They personify nature, emphasizing reverence and admiration towards it as well as tribal cohesion, following the seasons and showing respect for living things. The reservation's totem is a mighty bull-like creature. In the tribe, people with certain status wear unique horn ornaments to symbolize their identity and faith.\n\nThis sole surviving primitive settlement was wiped out in an unexpected Shogger invasion in this century, with only a few residents escaping unharmed. They accepted help from the Selevie government, left the ruins of their homeland, and resettled in the city. Regrettably, those magnificent and mysterious civilizations may never reappear in the world again.\n\nOr perhaps the survivors will Reignite their belief and pass on the cultural flame once more."
},
	[47113]={ language="Information One: Really likes to use her shield as a skateboard, and often goes out for a ride during her free time. Most of the time, she goes alone; maybe only those she's very close with can share these moments with her.\n\nInformation Two: Very hardworking, the kind who can endure hardships, seemingly with endless energy. Almost no one has ever seen her show fatigue.\n\nInformation Three: Thinks things through comprehensively and has a natural protective instinct for those younger or more timid. She's always very patient with them."
},
	[47114]={ language="1. Solar Explosion Shield: It can create an energy light shield to defend against damage; it's more like a hoverboard than a skateboard. Maybe a bit avant-garde, but it's Grinloffin's favorite [vehicle.]\n\n2. Crystal Tri-Blade Spear: A long and agile weapon, good at blocking and thrusting. Its considerable weight signifies its power.\n\n3. Horn Decoration: Seems to be a tribal decorative piece. Looks a bit worn, is it an old item from childhood?\n\n4. A gift with profound meaning. Wear it, and you can chase the wind."
},
	[47115]={ language="Information One: No sense of distance with familiar people, likes to put arms around others.\n\nInformation Two: Really good at singing and dancing, doesn't mind performing if in the mood, but there are few opportunities.\n\nInformation Three: Usually seems carefree, but is very perceptive in situations requiring emotional intelligence."
},
	[47116]={ language="Even though the threat of eternal night has long loomed over this planet, for now, those who have experienced the fall of an entire race are still an absolute minority. Overnight, being forced to part from loved ones, the familiar order of life disrupted, and previous understandings uprooted—this is a wound that's hard to heal for anyone.\n\nNot many people know where Grinloffin comes from. She's bold in style but meticulous in thought and always takes a cautious approach when mentioning her homeland. Instead of straightforward storytelling, she hopes the stories of the Reservation stay within oral traditions and for this civilization to truly regain its vitality. Zulu Mercenary Group was established by her after she decided to leave Selevie. Initially, they were a small group of mercenaries living together for survival. Gradually, under Grinloffin's leadership, they became almost like a mobile museum of Reservation civilization. Like any Reservation people, they worship nature, wear horn ornaments, and unite under the same totem. But notably, they aren't connected by blood; their current lifestyle is their own choice.\n\nThis clearly resembles Grinloffin's own tribe. Her personal charm plays an undeniable role in this. She's eager to care for the vulnerable and tirelessly lends a hand to those in need, often without calculating the cost. The Leistance Security Bureau agents who've worked with her invariably have received her help, whether big or small, whether public or private—even down to offering candy when someone's feeling down. Her passion for this cause seems innate, reminding one of large herbivores closely guarding their own herds during migration.\n\nUnlike the usual stereotypes of tribal dwellers, she is well-versed in the workings of modern Technology and knows how to survive in a city. It is said that Grinloffin survived the disaster that wiped out the Reservation because she wasn't in the tribe at the time but was in the city of Selevie. Regarding this part of her life, she remains tight-lipped but doesn't seem to believe her past [rebellion] can be labeled wrong. Indeed, looking back futilely at the past won't benefit the future.\n\nSome think she's avoiding something, while others believe she's already shown enough bravery."
},
	[47117]={ language="Information One: Really afraid of not making it in time—like not making it back to the Reservation swallowed by disaster from the city.\n\nInformation Two: Even though she felt lost when she first started leaving Selevie, she unconsciously began to embrace the people she met along the way, eventually using her charisma to move them, turning them into her [family.]"
},
	[47118]={ language="...\n\nYou mean Antilope? I've seen her! I've seen her.\n\nUzyanta is a mixed bag, and the border is even more so. Let me tell you, our place isn't as bad as they say outside; there's good money to be made—just easy to lose your life too.\n\nThat's not really a flaw, right? Isn't everywhere like this nowadays?\n\nThree years ago, there was a new mercenary group named Zulu that entered the city. Strange, isn't it? Right, that's what I thought too. I had never heard of them, seemed like some dialect, sounded quite funny at first. The leader of this mercenary group was a young woman, quite tall. I'd never seen someone with those Feature before: white hair, golden eyes, and dark skin. They all wore strange accessories, looking like cattle skulls. Honestly, too primitive, kind of uncivilized, somewhat frightening.\n\nDon't doubt it, you'd get goosebumps seeing them. You said you're a journalist, should be well-informed. Do you know where they're from?\n\n…\n\nOn the day they settled in town, many people went out to watch the spectacle, the streets were packed. The woman was at the very front of the group, carrying a massive Energy shield about as tall as a person in one hand and holding a golden spear in the other, not even glancing at the surrounding Ravend.\n\n...Tsk tsk, I bet the bigwigs in the city wouldn't be able to lift those two things. No wonder the mercenaries listened to her, kind of like obediently following orders.\n\nA lot of people here rely on Crystals for a living, anyone could see the stuff in her hands was nothing ordinary. But with the swarms of mercenaries coming and going daily, they didn't stand out much. Yet within three days, without landing a single order, they clashed with the local thugs.\n\nApparently, it was just because someone shoved a kid and knocked over his half-filled milk jug.\n\nStuff like this—what's the big deal? This stuff happens every day. If they want to deal with it, where would they start? You think they're just idle, don't you? Yeah, exactly.\n\nBut they won the fight. The leading woman was especially strong; many saw it. Standing on her shield, she suddenly jumped up into the sky, with golden light illuminating half the city like under a spotlight.\n\nImagine the mess those thugs must have been in after tangling with them.\n\nThat girl was Grinloffin. Yeah, Antilope. Antilope might be her alias, everyone calls her that anyway.\n\nBack then, I thought, strong people tend to have bad tempers, it's normal. But this was not a smart move. Being a hero doesn't mean you should choose the wrong place, right? As they say, knowing when to act is smart; otherwise, you're a fool.\n\nMany people bet on when they'd leave, either driven out or left voluntarily because they couldn't stand it. Playing a good guy in a place like this just makes you unpopular and likely to be excluded. But look, three years have passed, and they're still in Uzyanta, even helping people. Old, young, women and children, whatever the problem, they'd help without even charging.n\nTell me, is this really good deeds being rewarded? Could such a thing still happen in this world?\n\n…\n\n——[Uzyanta Memoir 2123: Oral Histories of Twenty People] Chapter 12"
},
	[47119]={ language="Information One: Her math is really bad, but she's surprisingly good at writing poetry—her style has a raw feel to it, like the gentle whispers of the jungle or the exuberant singing on the prairie.\n\nInformation Two: She doesn't want to go back to Selevie, nor does she want to stay in one place for long.\n\nInformation Three: She's actually afraid of thunder; it feels like the embodiment of some disaster, but she never shows it."
},
	[47120]={ language="Real Name: Lilira Nightingale\nIdentity: Operator of Lissugen Branch of Leistance\nInterests: Writing diaries, collecting small animal Puppets"
},
	[47121]={ language="[Such a pity, so young and yet...]\n[I heard she was born with it from her mother's body...]\n[Is it Void Particles Infection? I heard the director personally treated her...]\n[She's so weak, can this child really survive?]\n[Mutation is terrifying, isn't it...]\n…\n\nSince she could remember, Lilira constantly heard these words.\n\nTo most people, she was an unfortunate girl, infected by Void Particles even before birth because her mother was attacked by Shogger, leaving her weak and needing long-term treatment after birth.\n\nHer childhood was filled with pale walls and the pungent smell of medicine; during every treatment, she'd hear these comments.\n\nHer dad said she was just [sick,] and if she cooperated with the treatment, she would soon get better. She firmly believed this.\n\nLilira was considerate and didn't cause trouble for her dad, obediently cooperating with the treatment at the hospital. While other HPy kids were attending school and making friends, Lilira's companions were only books and Puppets, her sole friends during childhood.\n\nInitially, Lilira didn't know what [death] really meant.\n\nYoung children have a vague understanding of life and death; she only noticed some patients never returned one day. But when she witnessed death firsthand, the instinctive fear of it overcame her reason.\n\nShe gradually realized death is painful.\n\nFor a long time, she was so scared she couldn't sleep; during treatments, she fearfully asked her dad if she would [die] too.\n\n[Lilira, death is something everyone will face, it's just a matter of time,] her dad, not great at comforting, gently stroked Lilira's head. [Death is inevitable; it'll come. What doctors and I can do is to make sure Lilira sees it a little later, giving you more time to do what you want.]\n\n[What I want to do?]\n\nLilira looked at her dad, confused, still young at the time, not knowing what she could do living long-term in the hospital. She saw patients deemed incurable due to severe Void Particles contamination, and the pain and tears of those who lost loved ones, images deeply ingrained in her mind.\n\nLater, as she gradually got used to facing death, she realized surviving was already lucky enough. While contemplating her luck, she thought about her dad's words:\n\nThe time wrested from death, during which she could do something.\n\nShe looked at other patients in the ward, forming a vague idea.\n\nShe wanted to do something for them."
},
	[47122]={ language="Information One: If a patient doesn't cooperate with treatment, Lilira can become very scary—[How scary? Why don't you try and find out?] according to an anonymous patient.\n\nInformation Two: Publicly expresses a great fear of bugs, but it's said her favorite pillow is a two-meter-long caterpillar.\n\nInformation Three: Previously had HP issues and a strictly controlled diet. Now that restrictions are lifted, she loves extremely spicy food, though she can't handle much. She finds it painful yet immensely enjoyable each time she eats it."
},
	[47123]={ language="1. Nursing Book: [AIMBS Emergency Guide for the Injured] (Joshburg Southern Publishing, Seventh Edition, Third Printing)\n\n2. Healer Notes: These notes detail the physical conditions and treatment plans of squad members.\n\n3. Energy Battery: Beta 3 exclusive energy battery, for emergency use on the battlefield.\n\n4. Diary: Lilira's diary, each entry includes adorable illustrations.\n\n5. Kitty Puppet: A white cat puppet, a gift given to Lilira by the other squad members, with hidden messages inside for Lilira."
},
	[47124]={ language="Information One: She doesn't dare to play with the plush puppet she bought because she's not good at crafts and worried about accidentally breaking it, which would be a hassle.\n\nInformation Two: Her favorite animal is a cat, and she calls herself Miss Kitty in front of kids at the hospital.\n\nInformation Three: The cat ear accessory on her head seems like it hasn't changed, but actually, it's a different one every day. She just bought many pairs that look identical."
},
	[47125]={ language="March 7, XXXX, Dad said I'm getting better, so I don't have to stay in the special ward anymore—I can go out and move around. I'm so happy! I got a new Puppet from Mom and Dad. Tomorrow's my first time leaving this ward; I wonder what will happen? (Miss Kitty's smiley face)\nMarch 8, XXXX, Dad's not here today. I asked Nurse Sister if I could help take care of the patients with her, and she agreed, as long as I don't act alone. I'm so happy she agreed! I'm still young, not as skilled as my dad, but I can do something—I believe I can.\nMarch 9, XXXX, There's no nurse outfit in my size, but Owl Nurse Sister gave me a cute nurse hat. From today, I'm a nurse too! Go Miss Kitty!(Clenched cat paw)\nMarch 10, XXXX, Today's work... documenting each little animal's medication types and amounts, purifying the air in the ward, room inspections... Wow, a nurse's work is busier and harder than I imagined, but Miss Kitty will do her best!\n…\nMarch 19, XXXX, I'm familiar with everyone in the ward now. Even though I can only do basic care and record-keeping, it's great to be helpful. (A big smiling face)\nMarch 20, XXXX, I heard more little animals got Cursed by the witch. We got a lot of new patients today... I'm not afraid of Infection and mutation anymore. I really hope these little animals can get better like I did.\n…\nApril 15, XXXX, Brother Bear in bed three is getting worse. I overheard the nurses saying he might not make it till the end of the month... How did it come to this?\nWhat will happen to Brother Bear? What can I do for him? (I wrote down many plans, then crossed them out)\nApril 16, XXXX, I saw Brother Bear's family visiting him today. Although they couldn't make direct contact, Brother Bear looked happy. After his parents left, he wanted to give me the toys and snacks they brought. But I don't want them—I just want Brother Bear to live.\nApril 17, XXXX, Owl Nurse Sister wasn't here today. Brother Bear said he wanted a drink, but the nurse said drinks are forbidden. He looked so pitiful... Will he die if he doesn't drink? Okay... just a sip. (A tiny cat paw indicating [a little])\nIt was the first time I saw Brother Bear smile so happily.\nYou'll live well, right?\nApril 18, XXXX, The nurse found out about the drink, and both Miss Kitty and Brother Bear got scolded... Boohoo. (Crying face)\n(A stern owl picture) [Lilira, our job is to meet the patients' needs, but not everything is allowed. Sick little animals are fragile; we must strictly follow the doctor's orders. Disobedient animals will be closely monitored.]\nMiss Kitty remembered: no more secretly allowing Brother Bear drinks. He has to take his medicine to get better.\n…\nApril 29, XXXX, Played games with Brother Bear. He seems to be improving and cooperated well with the treatment today.\nHe'll definitely get better.\nMay 30, XXXX, Brother Bear didn't wake up. (A big tear stain here)\n…\nOctober 29, XXXX, Today is Miss Kitty's last day at the hospital. I'll miss everyone so much.\nBut I'll come back someday. Saying 'hope to see you all again' at a hospital might sound odd, right? So, everyone, stay well. Miss Kitty hopes by the time I return, there won't be any sick little animals here~ (Smiling face)\n—Lilira's Fourth Journal (Top Secret)"
},
	[47126]={ language="Information One: The medical notes have some illustrations drawn by the person, and some ramblings that have been crossed out.\n\nInformation Two: Has been rated as [the most charming girl in Joshburg Medical School], but she is unaware of this."
},
	[47127]={ language="Dear Miss Loral:\nHope this finds you well.\nLong time no see, how have you been lately?\n\nPlease forgive me for contacting you this way. I heard from dad about your upcoming retirement, and I'm thrilled for you. I'm sorry I can't rush to the hospital to celebrate with you, please understand.\n\nLately, I can't help but recall the times when I was in the hospital. I still remember the first time I met you. I was scared because of the treatment, and my parents weren't around. You comforted and helped me when I was most lost and helpless. Even now, I remember how your warm hands held mine and told me not to be afraid.\n\nIt's a bit embarrassing to say, but some things I can only write down, so I'm not at a loss for words when I see you. My biggest memory of you from childhood is your busy figure in the ward. You even remembered every patient's name and condition, giving them care and help. I must say, a big reason I chose to become a doctor was the encouragement and courage I got from you.\n\nI don't know if my dad told you, but I've graduated from medical school and am now interning at Leistance Security Bureau. I've successfully passed the AIMBS interview and become a Healer Operator with the Project D-Blood. My parents respect my choice, but I know they're worried and don't want me to go to dangerous battlefields. However, this is my well-thought-out decision, so please don't worry about me. I'll take good care of myself.\n\nOnce I get through this busy period, I'll bring some local specialties to visit you. I hope you won't mind (Laugh).\n\nFrom: Lilira·Nightingale (Miss Kitty from the ward)"
},
	[47128]={ language="Information One: On days off, she volunteers at the hospital and is particularly fond of dressing up as animals to tell stories to kids.\n\nInformation Two: Lilira can only draw small animals; drawing people and other things is an absolute disaster, but she is extremely confident in this area."
},
	[47129]={ language="Real Name: Lorila \nIdentity: Special Manager of AIMBS at Leistance Security Bureau\nInterests: Making sandbags, which are actually her cat scratchers"
},
	[47130]={ language="This is the downtown slum of the city, adults call it [Back Street.]\n\nFor some reason, our family moved here. My room has a window that faces a dim alley.\n\nMost of the time I sit in my wheelchair by the window, watching those stray cats that appear from nowhere in the alley.\n\nThat's when I first saw her.\n\nBut she ran too fast, and I couldn't quite tell if it was a cat or a person.\n\n…\nI saw her again today. She looks younger than me, with only a piece of tattered cloth. Is she homeless and wandering?\n…\nToday she's injured, crouching in a corner licking the back of her hand. I threw some medicine and bandages through the window at her. She seemed startled and quickly disappeared, not seen for several days.\n…\nToday she returned, playing happily with the stray cats. I watched as she punched through a trash can. I wasn't hungry for the food my mom brought, so I threw the meat out of the window.\nI saw her look up in my direction, and quickly ate the food before running away.\n…\nEvery day afterward, I saved my food for her.\nI don't know if she remembers me, but she shows up at a fixed time every day. I really want to talk to her, but I can't.\n…\nMy HP keeps deteriorating. Mom seems to have discovered that I've been giving all my food to those cats, and she had someone weld the window shut. I can't open the window anymore.\n…\nToday mom is on the phone with the police complaining about the stray cats outside keeping her up at night.\n…\nPolice cars and cleaning trucks came in, and I saw them with cages in their hands.\nAfter that, I never saw stray cats in the alley again.\n…\nShe returned today, wandering the alley.\nIs she looking for companions?\n…\nSaw a cleaner today placing food there, but she ran away.\n…\nThe cleaner came again today, and she didn't hide. I can't hear their conversation, and only in the brightest time of day can I see twisted letters on the ground through the window crack.\nLorila.\nIs that her name?\n…\nToday the alley was noisy. The cleaner who frequently appeared here was robbed by a group of ruffians. They injured the cleaner; she didn't escape and fought them. The ruffians ran away, and the cleaner lay there, not moving.\nWhen mom came into the room, I wrote this down and showed it to her.\n…\nSoon mom called the police. She later told me the cleaner had died.\nAnd that child, I saw them capture her and take her away.\n…\nWhere will they take her? No one will tell me even if I ask, right?\nI really hope she survives."
},
	[47131]={ language="Information One: Although the situation has improved, when groggy, she still can't tell if she's a human or a cat.\n\nInformation Two: She uses sandbags as a scratching post, so they need to be replaced often. If don't provide her with materials in time, she'll start scratching door panels or precision instruments.\n\nInformation Three: For a long time, she'd end her sentences with a [meow], but that's been corrected now."
},
	[47132]={ language="1. Sandbag: It's actually used as a scratching post for the cat, with some strange text that only Lorila can understand.\n\n2. Cat-shaped Long Pillow: Lorila rolls the pillow into a circle while sleeping and lies inside it.\n\n3. Colorful Markers: Lorila uses them to mark his own belongings."
},
	[47133]={ language="Information One: An absolute nocturnal creature, her attending physician once tried to help adjust her schedule but almost ended up with a nervous breakdown, so the treatment plan was stopped.\n\nInformation Two: [Though she's really cute, she's also quite dangerous. If you want to approach her, it's best to have some snacks on hand.]\n\nInformation Three: She writes strange symbols on all her belongings, which she claims are the language of cats."
},
	[47134]={ language="Today was my first day working at the city's underground arena. They gave me what they called an [easy] job—taking care of the important [fighters.]\n\nBefore coming here, I'd heard a bit about the fighters. It's said they're illegally remodeled AIMBS Operators. Wealthy men enjoy watching the maddened AIMBS Operators fight, and the Boss here profits from this bizarre hobby. Not that it concerns me much; if I wasn't broke, I wouldn't be working in a place like this.\n\nThe manager took me to where they [keep] these illegal AIMBS Operators.\n\n[You'll be responsible for her], he handed me a set of keys and reminded me, [You're new here, right? A word of advice: she's dangerous. When feeding her, don't get too close.]\n\n…\nSoon, it was time for the first feeding.\nSome barely cooked meat was placed at the feed spot by the gate. In a blink, she devoured the whole plate, not leaving a morsel behind.\nI recalled what they called her—\nWildcat.\n…\nToday she went berserk, injured, blood pouring from her arm. Wildcat is wild as ever, not letting the doctor near to treat her madness.\nThey asked me, the caretaker, to soothe her. What a joke? I don't want to die.\nI had to obey them for money. Maybe because she knew I fed her, she didn't harm me.\n…\nWildcat seemed to be talking in her sleep, waking me up.\nIt sounded like she was calling a name, Lorila.\n…\nI heard those wealthy men shouting like crazy again. She probably won again.\nThey gave her a better room and served food we can't afford because she's now a cash cow here. Even I, just delivering her meals, moved to a better place.\n…\nShe stayed the same, never spoke a word, nearly killed opponents in battle, AIMBS being precious. Boss would stop the fight by shocking her collar.\nBut this time, the shock didn't work.\nWhen I heard chaos, she had defeated everyone in the arena. The Boss, who looked down on everyone, lay there like a dead dog, unclear if he's alive.\nI found the collar keys on the Boss, called her, and unlocked her shackles.\nShe glanced at me; I thought she'd kill me, but she walked away.\n…\n[That's all I know. As for why she didn't harm me... I don't know. Do you have any other questions?]\n[No, thanks for your cooperation.]\n…\n[That child is called Lorila.]"
},
	[47135]={ language="Information One: Despite multiple warnings not to damage the drones flying around the base, quite a few drones have still met with disaster.\n\nInformation Two: Has no specific food preference and can eat anything, but has a deep hatred for chili peppers."
},
	[47136]={ language="When they brought that child back, I couldn't even imagine what had happened to her.\n\nAnyone who saw her at first glance would think her condition was too terrible.\n\nMaybe the way she was brought back was a bit rough, and she had a strong stress reaction. I gave her a sedative so I could examine her.\n\nMuscle tissue torn in multiple places, severe arm fracture (who did this?), malnutrition, multiple organ tissue damage...\n\nSo cruel, really, places like the arena just shouldn't exist.\n\nI applied to be her attending physician.\n\n…\nHer condition is worse than I imagined. After more than half a month of treatment, she finally adapted to her current environment, but she still displays extreme mistrust and aggression towards strangers, except for me. She injured quite a few people during this time, and no one dares to approach her closely anymore.\n…\nTotally unable to communicate, almost no language ability, it's impossible to carry out psychological treatment like this.\nBut my efforts have started to show some results.\nThis kid's name is Lorila, who gave her this name?\n…\nHer physical injuries have mostly healed, but she doesn't like the bandages on her arm. Several times she tore them off when I wasn't paying attention, and it just keeps going like this.\n…\nShe's starting to resist examinations, need to figure something out.\n…\nToday, some careless subordinate made a mistake, setting off an alarm and triggering her mania. She not only failed to recognize me but also wrecked the whole room.\nIf possible, I wouldn't want to use sedatives again, but there's no choice, she needs to calm down.\n…\nThe arm injury worsened, and they've designed armor for her arm, but she's still not used to being restrained, though the armor can't be taken off now, right? At least this way she can move freely without hurting anyone.\n…\nBroke three surveillance drones.\nIs she treating them like toys?\n…\n[Feeling energetic today too, Lorila. How are you?]\nShe snatched the fish snack from my hand, retreated to a corner, and nibbled at it. After finishing, she licked her lips and looked at me, saying:\n[Mm].\nLooks like I've found a way to communicate with her.\n…\nShe finally knows she's human, not a cat, her cognitive disorder has eased, and her mania hasn't acted up for a long time. Although it can't be fully treated, everything is turning for the better.\n…\nI really hope she can consider this place her new home. I believe one day she'll open her heart to someone."
},
	[47137]={ language="Information One: Very strong, easily goes berserk during battle, can't distinguish friend from foe, requires a high level of Linker.\n\nInformation Two: Uses some strange metaphors to express feelings."
},
	[47138]={ language="Real Name: Clarence Constantine\nIdentity: Star Knight of Vilatria\nInterests: Reading novels and eating, especially enjoys knight novels and snacks."
},
	[47139]={ language="How much do you know about [Stellar Knights]?\n\nIsn't that the internal military organization of Vilatria? What are you bringing this up for?\n\nAfter all, a [Star Knight] will be here tomorrow to negotiate with us, right? Might as well do some homework on it.\n\nThe data says they have a very... traditional structure. Apart from [Companion Star Knights] handling daily duties, there's also a group of [Star Knights] who can use the power of the Stellar Crystal. They seem to have abilities almost like the AIMBS Operator.\n\nWithout D-Blood technology, they can still do what AIMBS Operators can?\n\nThat's Vilatria's most core secret, right? Honestly, I'm really curious about this country. The idea that knights, doctrines, and faith can encompass an entire nation feels like they're completely different from today's world.\n\nIndeed... What about that Star Knight coming to discuss with us? Is there any info on her?\n\nLet me check... Her code name is [Flicker], Real Name Clarence Constantine, and she's the sixth in the Stellar Knights.\n\nFlicker... refers to the sun? Using something that has [disappeared] as a code name?\n\nYeah, that's how the Information described her—[The golden glow she emits in battle... is just like the sun. No Shogger or Mutant can stand up to that beam of light!]\n\nIs she really that powerful... This is getting me more and more curious.\n\n—Chat amongst Leistance employees while waiting to meet for business exchange with Vilatria."
},
	[47140]={ language="Information One: In her spare time, she eagerly buries herself in books, but if you observe closely, you'll find she's actually reading popular novels about knights.\n\nInformation Two: Although born into nobility, Clarence never puts on airs and is approachable, which is why other lower-ranked knights are happy to interact with her.\n\nInformation Three: No one has ever seen Clarence relaxing; she seems to have endless energy, doing everything herself, making people wonder if she's a perpetual motion machine."
},
	[47141]={ language="1. [The Black Iron Throne]: It's a knight-themed novel, with signs of repeated reading and notes on the pages.\n\n2. An Old Photograph: It's a family photo of the Constantine family, featuring Clarence with his late elder siblings and parents.\n\n3. A Relatively New Photo: A picture of Clarence just after becoming a Star Knight.\n\n4. [Family Admonition]: The Constantine family's admonition, with notes left by the elder siblings, given to Clarence by his father."
},
	[47142]={ language="Information One: Clarence is one of the most popular Star Knights in Vilatria, beloved by children who feel she's like the sunlight piercing through Vilatria's darkness, enveloping this star-blessed land.\n\nInformation Two: Clarence always carries a photo with her elder sister and brother, and uses them as his role models.\n\nInformation Three: She rarely sleeps in and maintains a very HPy routine."
},
	[47143]={ language="[The Celestial Star guided him and his people to the ultimate land, where he led them to establish Vilatria, a nation blessed by the stars.] \n—— [Vilatria Chronicles, Volume One] \n\nAs one of Vilatria's seven Guard families, the Constantine family, where Flicker belongs, shares the same historical dimension as the founding of Vilatria—ever since the first Pope led the ancestors to establish the nation, the Constantine family has been the backbone actively participating on various fronts—it's safe to say that the Constantine family and the other six families are the foundation stones of Vilatria's creation. \n\nHowever, these are all events recorded in books now buried in the past. Time has changed many things claimed to be unchanging, even for Vilatria, which worships the so-called [Eternal Celestial Star.] The current reality differs significantly from what's recorded in the books: only three of the seven Guard families remain, and their status among the populace is far less stable than that of the Starcall Abbey... Among them, the Constantine family is the weakest. If Miss Clarence hadn't become a Star Knight, the Constantine family might have faded like those vanished Guard families and only existed in books. \n\nI don't know if Miss Clarence willingly became [Flicker], but anyone who's met her knows that [Flicker] is a perfect adherent to the Stellar Knights' ethos. She's strong, loyal, fights against evil, and has a great sense of justice, appearing wherever her country and people need her—she's fully embraced the identity of [Flicker]. Correspondingly, has she become indifferent to her origins from the Constantine family? The current head of the Constantine family seems to have mixed feelings about Clarence becoming a Star Knight—however... this is ultimately a family matter of the Constantines. We, as outsiders, cannot interfere or know the inside story. \n\nAt least for now, the [Flicker] knight is doing well to protect Vilatria. The public loves her, respects her, and needs her—she is Vilatria's [shield,] and that is undeniable. \n\n—— Notes from the Religious Advisor stationed at Leistance Vilatria"
},
	[47144]={ language="Information One: When interrupted while absorbed in a knight novel, she will show a very interesting expression.\n\nInformation Two: She has learned noble etiquette well and even has a gown, but due to a busy work schedule, there's no chance for her to wear it."
},
	[47145]={ language="——Private letter from Vilatria City Post.\n\nDear Aunt Linmer:\n\nI apologize for not writing to you for a while. Before heading out on this mission, I wanted to send you this letter and hope you understand.\n\nHow is your HP? As winter approaches, please keep warm. If there's not enough fuel for the Crystal heater, I'll send more to Mr. Mitch at the Depot, so you don't need to go to the market. Even though your legs have just recovered, frequent movement in this chilled weather might affect your recovery.\n\nI've received the cured meat and pickles you sent. It's the familiar taste; indeed, you know my preferences best—thank you so much. By the way, the books your child wants to read have been packed by the mail staff. They are selected by me and my friends, and she will definitely not feel lonely this winter.\n\nSome medicines for father have also been sent home. Please remind him to use them under your or Mr. Mitch's name, without mentioning me. If he knows they're from me, he'll throw them into the river outside the estate again.\n\nRegarding your suggestion, after careful consideration, I've decided to deal with the Missions of the knights first and discuss with you this matter next spring. As you mentioned, Vilatria has been unstable lately, and the Constantine family indeed needs to consider future issues. If father is unwilling, it should be my responsibility as a descendant of the Constantine family, which has never changed.\n\nTime is tight, and I can't share more about my life in the city and the knights' order. I hope father, you, Mr. Mitch, and everyone else at the estate stay Happy.\n\n——Clarence Constantine"
},
	[47146]={ language="Information One: The shield in her arsenal was once shattered, but was successfully reforged under her personal supervision.\n\nInformation Two: Clarence's family is actually very wealthy, but she doesn't know how to use money or manage finances, leading colleagues to mistakenly think she might be very poor."
},
	[47147]={ language="Real Name: Franbyn Blackbell\nIdentity: Deputy Captain of the [Glory] affiliated with Joshburg Navy.\nInterests: Researching drones."
},
	[47148]={ language="The surname Blackbell is quite prominent in the Joshburg military. Since the establishment of Joshburg, they have been developing alongside Joshburg's air forces. Over half of the air force commanders have come from the Blackbell family, making it fair to say that the Blackbell family is a cradle for air force commanders.\n\nBorn into such a family, Franbyn was expected to achieve great things from a young age. Her father, an air force commander, groomed her to be the next air force commander rather than giving her a typical childhood. For her 12th birthday, she received a unique present as she was personally [sent] by her father to the Air Force Command Academy and instructed the instructors to give her [special care], doubling both her academic workload and tutorial sessions.\n\nFew know what Franbyn's inner thoughts were during her time at the academy, but she ultimately graduated at the top of her class.\n\nDue to her family's background and Franbyn's outstanding performance, she was supposed to directly join Joshburg's first air squadron and become part of the air force. But on the day new officers were to report, Franbyn didn't show up, nor could anyone reach her.\n\nFranbyn's father, Lieutenant General Jector, the current Joshburg air force commander, realized something was wrong. Concerned about the possibility of an accident, he deployed a large team to search for her but found nothing. That was until his daughter returned to the Blackbell residence dressed in a navy uniform.\n\n[I haven't had any accidents, nor am I running away from home. I'm just doing what I want to do.]"
},
	[47149]={ language="Information One: Extremely responsible, treasures her companions, you can confidently entrust your back to her.\n\nInformation Two: Hates birds trapped in cages, especially canaries, she feels they lack selfhood and are content with being imprisoned by fate.\n\nInformation Three: Very popular in the navy, voted [Joshburg's Most Beautiful Navy Miss] for three consecutive years, but Franbyn is indifferent to this."
},
	[47150]={ language="1. Frozen Vegetable Pack: Occasionally there are unforeseen situations on the ship where supplies are unavailable. At times like these, Franbyn relies on frozen vegetable packs to keep up her nutrition.\n\n2. Craft Wine: The brewer has a deep understanding of wine, and this wine tastes great, but it's best not to drink too much. Franbyn usually drinks a few glasses alone when she's dealing with insomnia or feeling down.\n\n3. Drone: Though it's meant to be her personal Crystal weapon and a part of the Navy's new campaign equipment, Franbyn likes to treat it as her toy and enjoys playing and studying it in her spare time.\n\n4. M58 Fishing Rod: The champion prize from the 40th [Glory] fishing contest was the first reward Franbyn received from fishing. Her colleagues say she was born to be a great angler."
},
	[47151]={ language="Information One: Takes great care of their uniform, unwilling to let it get a speck of dust.\n\nInformation Two: Often stands on the deck in the dead of night, enjoying the breeze with a few drinks.\n\nInformation Three: A landlubber, currently learning to swim."
},
	[47152]={ language="Franbyn joining the navy caused confusion and dissatisfaction among many in her family, especially her father, Lieutenant General Jackett, the Air Force Commander.\n\nUnlike in the Air Force, the Blackbell name is not highly regarded in the Joshburg Navy—reasons for this are complex, though at the core, it's about uneven Resource distribution. As a prestigious Air Force family, the Blackbell family has worked hard to protect Air Force interests, inevitably harming or infringing on other military branches' interests.\n\nJackett couldn't understand why his daughter, whom he had trained, chose the navy over the Air Force, thinking she was ruining her future. Yet Franbyn, facing her always authoritative father, surprisingly did not yield. She firmly expressed her determination to become a naval campaign member, stating it was a well-considered decision—to no longer live under the family's protection or the so-called [good, right, and beneficial] path arranged for her.\n\nA severe argument broke out between father and daughter. Though tensions eased with other family members' mediation, Jackett still disagreed with Franbyn's choice. However, he understood his daughter's personality—Franbyn might seem easygoing, but she was more stubborn than a mule. Once she decided on something, no one could change her mind.\n\nConsidering his options, Jackett decided to approach it through the military. He spoke to the captain of Franbyn's fleet, highlighting his relationship with Franbyn and hoping they could release her. However, the captain stated they would respect the soldier's will, emphasizing, [There is only 'Tern' in the Sea Hawk Fleet, no Franbyn Blackbell.]"
},
	[47153]={ language="Information One: During the recruitment test for the Joshburg Navy test, was admitted with top marks.\n\nInformation Two: Every time arriving at a new place, always buys postcards with local Feature."
},
	[47154]={ language="■■, ■■, ■■■■, weather: Sunny\n\nToday marks the fiftieth day of officially becoming a member of the Sea Hawk Fleet, and the twentieth day of the closed tutorial.\n\nMy body has completely adapted, and the Navy's campaign tutorial intensity is just like that. The tutorial indicators have all reached excellent standards, but there's still room for improvement. Next, I need to consider how to keep improving.\n\nFrier called again, but I still didn't answer. That's the 17th call. Next time… I'll answer it next time.\n\nI really don't know what to talk about with the family.\n\n[[Mom]sent things again, I don't get it... Does she think this can improve our relationship?\n\n[The wife of the Air Force Commander exercising privilege, sending things to her stepdaughter in the Navy Fleet closed tutorial,] I'm sure these rumors have spread by now.\n\nThis just makes the divide between the Navy and Air Force bigger.\n\nThe old man surely knows this too, why doesn't he stop it? Whatever. His strictness always targets me.\n\nSince I've escaped the cage, I shouldn't think about these things anymore.\n\nTern, there's no way out for you.\n\nYou can only return as a fleet leader, otherwise, you'll never have a proper conversation with him in this lifetime."
},
	[47155]={ language="Information One: Rumor has it she dyed her hair red during her student days and even ran away from home—she's a rebellious girl.\n\nInformation Two: She has a half-sister, but Flampe is not close to her."
},
	[47156]={ language="Real Name: Lansenie\nIdentity: Security head of [Moonlight Kiss] bar\nInterests: None"
},
	[47157]={ language="The security head at [Moonlight Kiss] bar, Marceline, always sits in the shadows, quietly watching the bustling Ravend. Sometimes, she won't say a word all day, just keeps a stern face, and won't move unless necessary.\n\nIf a guest is new, they'd probably think she's cool or hard to deal with, but regulars know she just isn't good at talking—but being hard to deal with is true too.\n\nOnce, some female patrons, after leaving the bar, were harassed by passing thugs. The noise caught Marceline's attention, and many didn't even see how she got to the scene—she emerged from the shadows like a sudden apparition, and in just a few moves, took down those thugs, ending the fight in mere seconds.\n\nThe rescued female patrons were evidently a bit drunk, and to express their gratitude, they took turns hugging Marceline. As a result... according to witnesses, Marceline turned as red as a ripe shrimp from head to toe, and it was the bar owner Grenache who helped her, saving Marceline, who was too nervous to know what to do with her hands and feet.\n\nShe must be shy, right? Regulars say this about her, as if they completely forget how intimidating she is when she acts. But she only takes action against those not following the rules. If you're not causing trouble, there's naturally no reason to be afraid of her, right?"
},
	[47158]={ language="Information One: She's easily shy and often mistaken for being aloof, but her ears turn bright red.\n\nInformation Two: Lansenie rarely talks about her past. Whenever asked, she either responds with [I don't remember] or stays silent.\n\nInformation Three: She hardly sleeps—or rather, she never sleeps when others are around."
},
	[47159]={ language="1. Scythe: One of the main sources of security in Moonlight Kiss. As long as you don't do anything dangerous, it's just a beautiful decoration.\n\n2. Brown-covered Notebook: It has symbols only Lansnie can understand, but judging by the smiley faces, it's probably about good things.\n\n3. Black-covered Notebook: It's just filled with names, and you get the feeling you really don't want to end up on that list...\n\n4. Flowers: Lansnie loves all kinds of flowers, especially ones given by colleagues and guests."
},
	[47160]={ language="Information One: Often gets teased by Truce, and the only reaction is blushing. This hasn't improved so far, and Truce clearly isn't tired of it yet.\n\nInformation Two: Sometimes, her way of speaking seems disordered, but it's not just a lack of willingness to speak; it comes from past experiences.\n\nInformation Three: Strictly follows an unspoken principle of equivalent exchange. Even if you give her a leaf, she'll quietly give you a flower in return."
},
	[47161]={ language="Are you curious about how Lansenie came to us and how she became the head of security under the boss lady?\n\nWell, that was quite some time ago...\n\nI remember it was raining that night when the boss lady suddenly came back, carrying a girl covered in blood. She herself was injured too. Honestly, we were all shocked, but she didn't care about her own injuries and only told us that this girl was her lifesaver and we needed to find a doctor immediately—\n\nWe didn't know much, so we called a doctor. After checking the girl, the doctor just shook his head—he said the young girl's body seemed to have undergone multiple biological experiments or some type of Remodel. I was listening nearby but didn't understand.\n\nThe doctor and the boss lady talked quite a lot, but I can't remember exactly what they said. Anyway, it seemed like if forced treatment was carried out, it might not be successful. If left alone, relying on some strange self-healing ability, she might just recover on her own.\n\nAfter saying this, the doctor left some medicine and went off. The Boss lady listened to his advice and had us move the girl to a safe spot, clean her up, and take care of her.\n\nTwo months later, the girl finally woke up. She was very weak, hard to communicate with, and extremely aggressive, making us all reluctant to approach her.\n\nIn the end, the boss lady worked her magic. After spending some time alone with the girl, she managed to calm her down, and we learned that her name is Lansenie.\n\nHonestly, I don't know where Lansenie came from or why she behaves like this, but she's been doing well here, and that's all that matters.\n\n—An old employee from [Moonlight Kiss] bar"
},
	[47162]={ language="Information One: Always seems to be daydreaming, so there's always someone trying to scare her. Some of these people get discovered right away, while others need to go for psychological counseling.\n\nInformation Two: Likes the feeling of having trust around—preferably without needing to talk."
},
	[47163]={ language="All the Information here is yet to be confirmed—\n\nThere is reportedly a secret biological laboratory in the northern part of Uzyanta.\n\nThey have been running a gene remodel project named [Σ] for many years, initiated by unknown entities and led by unknown individuals. The only thing confirmed is—this project doesn't limit its subjects to animals.\n\nIn Uzyanta's black market, anything can be bought with money, known to all, and human trafficking is quite commonplace here.\n\nRumors say the Σ project has bought many children from the black market, using them as test subjects in the laboratory.\n\nMany speculate that the ultimate goal of the Σ project is to create super soldiers like the AIMBS Operator, a product of the Project D-Blood. The effectiveness of this, however, remains unknown.\n\nAlthough, several years ago, there were reports of test subjects escaping from the biological laboratory. The authenticity of this news is highly questionable since an uncontrolled human weapon would undoubtedly be conspicuous. Yet, Uzyanta has never reported anything related to this incident, and the laboratory has never openly sought the escaped subject. Soon, this Information was deemed a false rumor and quickly forgotten.\n\nThe forces behind this biological laboratory are very powerful, hence, although many disapprove of their actions, no one has dared to trouble them. Some say they have created a considerable armed force through the gene Remodel project, explaining why anyone with such ideas has been quietly eliminated by this team. In short, provoking them is not advisable. Uzyanta's gray forces usually keep their distance from this laboratory, avoiding discussion."
},
	[47164]={ language="Information One: It's best not to joke about [certain] things with her, like hating someone, wishing them bad luck, or hoping something happens to them. These risky remarks can lead to misunderstandings and negative consequences.\n\nInformation Two: When dealing with social situations, she takes a bit longer to respond, but when handling bar missions, she acts quickly—almost as if the former requires thought, and the latter is just instinct."
},
	[47174]={ language="Real Name: Adenie\nIdentity: Contracted Operator of Leistance Security Bureau\nInterests: Stargazing, gardening, making dried flowers"
},
	[47175]={ language="Vilatria is a theocracy with a strict hierarchy, ranked from top to bottom as: distinguished families, regular nobility, knights, commoners, and outcasts. The social mobility between these classes is extremely limited. For commoners and outcasts, rising to the rank of knight is as difficult as reaching for the stars, and becoming a noble is simply unthinkable. There's only one way for commoners and outcasts to achieve a miraculous jump in status: joining the [Stellar Knights] and becoming one of them.\n\nThe Stellar Knights are unique in Vilatria, unlike traditional [knight orders]. They are the most elite military force in Vilatria, the key force in dealing with Void Particles pollution, Mutant, and Shogger-related incidents, and the foundation of Vilatria's enduring strength. As such, they hold immense prestige and political power in the country. To ensure their combat effectiveness, Stellar Knights regularly conduct selection across Vilatria. Regardless of identity or background, any Vilatria citizen can participate.\n\nAt first glance, this seems like a remarkably fair opportunity, yet this fairness ironically creates significant challenges for commoners aspiring to become knights.\n\nFirst is the sheer number of participants. According to incomplete statistics, over the last ten knight selections, more than 200,000 individuals have registered each time, yet only a few hundred end up becoming Stellar Knights Members. This one-in-ten-thousand chance makes the competition extraordinarily fierce.\n\nSecondly, the diverse background of applicants. Since identity and background are not restricted, participants include offspring from distinguished families and regular noble households. These individuals inherently possess better material resources than commoners and were often specially trained from a young age, leaving commoners far behind from the start.\n\nIn this reality, for commoners to join the Stellar Knights has become an almost impossible dream.\n\nHowever, Adaine achieved this miracle."
},
	[47176]={ language="Information One: Loves to look at the starry sky while thinking and looks at flowers when relaxing.\n\nInformation Two: Skilled at making dried flowers.\n\nInformation Three: Never follows gardening guides for growing flowers, because she believes that growing flowers, like interacting with people, has no fixed approach."
},
	[47177]={ language="1. Some Galaxy and Starry Sky Photos: relics of the old days, must have taken quite an effort to collect.\n\n2. Dried Starry Sealan Flowers: carrying a faint scent, not sure if specially treated or sprayed with some special perfume.\n\n3. Vilatria's Stellar Knights Medals: Vilatria has extremely strict rules for issuing and storing Stellar Knights medals, they must be returned once leaving the knight group."
},
	[47178]={ language="Information One: A knight exiled by Vilatria, but the reason for the exile is unknown.\n\nInformation Two: Very knowledgeable about Vilatria's customs; if you want to learn about the place, ask her.\n\nInformation Three: She often receives letters from unknown regions."
},
	[47179]={ language="Adenie was born into a commoner's family in [Stardom,] the capital of Vilatria. Even when she was young, her parents noticed her uniqueness—she showed great interest in learning early on and could quickly grasp complex problems. She had extraordinary wisdom and leadership abilities for her age, allowing her to win over others and achieve her goals—like gaining free snacks using the favor of certain kids.\n\nAs Adenie grew older, she began to realize her talent could lead her to a bright future—as long as she observed carefully and skillfully used some tricks, she could get something she wanted from events. Most importantly—she understood that appearing too clever might attract unnecessary jealousy and attention most of the time, so she chose to stay humble, strategizing secretly, keeping a low profile in everything while observing her surroundings, using various [clever] elements of events to achieve success for herself.\n\nWith this skill, Adenie passed through the level of knight selection and eventually became the lowest-ranking attendant in the Stellar Knights, at just over 16 years old. However, our story was just beginning—\n\nAdenie knew she had never received any formal tutorial and wanted to become a Star Knight or even the Star Knight. She had only a slim chance of doing so by getting the most professional and effective guidance, which could only be provided by the Stellar Knights' knight commander—\n\nAfter using some means, Adenie secured an opportunity to [just happen] to let the commander see her injuries from protecting others during an inspection. She expressed her desire for guidance and her wish to rise from attendant to knight.\n\nTo be honest, with the commander's rich experience and excellent observational skills, he would naturally notice the design element in Adenie's series of [just happens.] But maybe he appreciated her little cunning, or perhaps... saw his past self in the girl's determined eyes, the knight commander ultimately didn't expose Adenie's poorly designed plan but chose to give her some guidance and allowed her to come and practice and attend training sessions.\n\nNaturally, Adenie was delighted to receive such a gift—three years later, she successfully passed the [Star Expedition] during the knight ranks' trial and earned the pope's recognition, inheriting the knight title named [Dawn]."
},
	[47180]={ language="Information One: Quite knowledgeable about astrology, but also very interested in things like zodiac signs.\n\nInformation Two: Her favorite flower is actually the red rose, but it doesn't match [the aura others associate with oneself,] so this fondness is kept quietly in the heart."
},
	[47181]={ language="Every few years, different areas of Vilatria are subjected to large-scale Mutant attacks, often accompanied by anchor invasion incidents. The people of Vilatria call this the [Stellar Judgment] and a key duty of the Stellar Knights is to protect the citizens during these events.\n\nAfter becoming a Star Knight, Adenie faced her first [Star Punishment] mission in her life. She bravely fought alongside other knights, slaying incoming Mutants and Shoggers. However, after the [Star Punishment] ended, she discovered, to her surprise, that the bodies of fallen knight comrades were missing from their graves.\n\nUpon investigation, Adenie found that the incident might relate to the Star Summoning Cult. She used her connections to investigate further, uncovering that the active cycles of [Star Punishments] historically seem linked to the cult's rituals.\n\nIn a web of doubt, Adenie began to suspect something terrifying and started secretly investigating the Star Summoning Sect. Before she could find any leads, she was summoned alone by the Knight Commander.\n\nThe Knight Commander instructed Adenie to cease her investigations, promising that the knight order would pursue these matters in their name, then took all of the evidence Adenie had gathered—It turned out her secret investigation had attracted attention, and to protect her, the Knight Commander had to make this decision.\n\nSoon after, under false [charges], Adenie's title of [Dawn] was revoked, and she was ordered to reside permanently in Leistance, forbidden to return to Vilatria without the knight order's summons.\n\nAdenie understood the Knight Commander's intention. She realized her investigation might have touched upon secrets that could cause upheaval within Vilatria. Hence, she remained silent, accepted the Knight Commander's arrangement, and went to Leistance to receive political sanctuary. She also aimed to leverage Leistance's power to uncover the secrets that the Star Summoning Sect was striving to conceal."
},
	[47182]={ language="Information One: There's a rumor that back when she was in Vilatria, her temper wasn't as good as it is now, but no one has verified this.\n\nInformation Two: The Stellar Knights medal from Vilatria is still preserved."
},
	[47183]={ language="Real Name: Hillley Promi\nIdentity: Promian tribal ambassador to Leistance Security Bureau\nInterests: Solitude, communicating with Taras, weaving ethnic fabrics"
},
	[47184]={ language="In the Arctic Circle of Taino Star, there lives an indigenous tribe known as the [Promi.] They are small in number, living a self-sufficient, tribal life, without entering the so-called [modern scientific civilized society.]\n\nPromian people have a magical talent—through certain witchcraft methods and mental exercises, they can link with the Stellar Crystal, thereby [perceiving the will of the Stellar Crystal] and materializing it. This materialization occurs when the Stellar Crystal transforms into a [Crystal Beast] that follows its owner; having a Crystal Beast is also a sign of coming of age for every Promi individual.\n\nCrystal Beasts are not only symbols of the Promi tribe but also excellent helpers in their lives. Whether it's pulling carts, carrying goods, riding, or hunting, Crystal Beasts are highly skilled. During the Shogger invasion war a century ago, it was the Crystal Beasts that helped the Promi withstand the Shogger monsters, enabling their survival.\n\nAfter the war, while reviewing wartime materials, some researchers noticed the [commonality] between Crystal Beasts and Shogger monsters. The debate over whether [Crystal Beasts and Shogger monsters are the same species] became a highly controversial topic. This topic later evolved into a conspiracy theory questioning the loyalty of the Promian people to humans—whether they are... traitors.\n\nSuspicion towards the Promian people grew heavier, compounded by their habit of not integrating into modern society. After several [accidents,] slaughtering the Promi began—"
},
	[47185]={ language="Information One: Because of Taras, personal rooms are twice as large as usual.\n\nInformation Two: Popular with other Operators in summer, but not in winter.\n\nInformation Three: Occasionally speaks a few strange dialects."
},
	[47186]={ language="Promian Pattern Scarf: A scarf Hillley knitted by hand when she was little. Although it has become worn, she still likes to keep it with her.\n\nIce Carving Knife: In her free time, Hillley carves lifelike ice sculptures. Unlike the Arctic, the ice sculptures here always melt quickly.\n\nSewing Kit: A tool Hillley uses to practice her knitting skills. After drawing on various cultural trends, she always manages to create magical patterns."
},
	[47187]={ language="Information One: Once sparked a trend of ethnic-style decorations within Leistance.\n\nInformation Two: Actually likes raw meat products, but chooses to hide it to avoid unnecessary comments.\n\nInformation Three: Not good at using electronic devices."
},
	[47188]={ language="During months of massacre, many Promians died. This clear inhumane slaughter was initially covered up but later exposed to the international community by insightful individuals and do-gooders.\n\nPeople condemned the massacre but still couldn't trust the Promians—the Crystal Beasts are the root of Promians' suffering. Humans going through perpetual night couldn't trust creatures looking almost exactly like Shogger, which seem to have a subtle connection, leading to distrust of Promians who live and die with the Crystal Beasts.\n\n\nSuspicion breeds hatred, and hatred eventually turns into blood and fire. Promians are innocent victims, but a stop must be put to this groundless suspicion and cruel slaughter.\n\nFinally, with the maneuvering of Star Council and Leistance Security Bureau, the international community agreed to allow the remaining Promians to live in so-called [Autonomous Regions] and dispatched [ambassadors] to reside in various countries—it's clear to everyone that this is just a euphemism for surveillance zones and hostages, but for survival, the Promians agreed to this plan.\n\nHillary is the ambassador representative of this generation of Promians sent to Leistance. She came to Leistance at fourteen after having her own Crystal Beast and has been there for nine years.\n\nOver nine years, she underwent the Operator remodel surgery and got the codename [Cold Jiao]. She went from unfamiliar to familiar with Leistance, forming deep friendships with peers and always showing love for Leistance and trust in [colleagues.] Even when faced with personal attacks, she handled them lightly. But the only exception is when her [Crystal Beast] is attacked; the sudden drop in temperature around her warns the questioner—if they continue, they'll face consequences."
},
	[47189]={ language="Information One: When angry, she can cause the surrounding temperature to drop sharply.\n\nInformation Two: She becomes stiff all over when she encounters overly enthusiastic people, especially those also from the extreme north like Karentilo."
},
	[47190]={ language="Regarding Hillley's code name, maybe it can be broken down.\n\nUsing [Leng] to describe the first impression of Hillley seems fitting—when people first meet her, they're often struck by her reserved and cold demeanor, as if surrounded by an aura that feels frozen.\n\nThis isn't an image she deliberately portrays—being a Promian from the Arctic ice plains, cold is in their genes. They have to face the cold, endure the cold, and use the cold. Cold has given them a tough body and mind, and Hillley is no exception.\n\nAs for [Jiao], it refers to Hillley's inseparable companion—Taras.\n\nThe existence of the Crystal Beasts remains shrouded in mystery, unable to be explained effectively from either mythological or scientific perspectives. Why Taras has the appearance of a Jiao is something even Hillley can't explain, but she knows that Taras is her [alter ego], a companion moving with her soul.\n\nFrom a conventional perspective, Hillley's efforts in those dangerous tasks seem to be the necessary responsibilities for ensuring the stability and survival of her people—just like the contract she signed when she came to Leistance specified. But to Hillley herself, these actions aren't simply an exchange of value—in other words, Hillley prefers to see it as her effort as a Promian for the continued advancement of her tribe.\n\nOperator Cold Jiao and the Promian ambassador Hillley are identities that can coexist, just like the Promian tribe and the civilized world can coexist.\n\nHillley hopes for this and fights for it."
},
	[47191]={ language="Information One: Most people's first impression of her is [cold,] but their final assessment always changes to [gentle.]\n\nInformation Two: She has worn a bikini only once."
},
	[47192]={ language="Real Name: Rita\nIdentity: [Moonlight Kiss] Bar Members\nInterests: She likes anything fun, especially playing pranks and causing trouble."
},
	[47193]={ language="Rita rarely talks about her past. Some say her parents died when she was very young, while others say they abandoned her.\n\nWhatever the case, from Rita's earliest memories, she has always been alone. Growing up, some bad things happened to her that left emotional scars.\n\nIn Rita's own words, she has already died once, and it was Grenache who saved her then. So, Grenache is like her reborn parent. As for the place she lives now, [Moonlight Kiss]... that's her home.\n\nRita absolutely cannot stand, and is most afraid of, being alone in a confined dark environment—she fears that in complete darkness, the loneliness would slowly consume and tear her apart.\n\nRita hates being ignored and often prefers to pull off some utterly boring pranks to catch people's attention—she feels that getting scolded or criticized is better than being alone.\n\n[Rita, oh, many people in Foden City know her. She's our famous 'troublemaker' here. Every household bears traces of her graffiti, though some of them are quite nice to look at. And when kids walk on the streets at night, they might occasionally get startled by Rita popping out from around a corner with a lamp that lights her face eerily.]\n\n[This kid, Rita, I've watched her grow up. She had a pretty tough childhood, living on meals from different families, but no one truly cared about her. So, I understand why she acts out—to get attention. It's actually not too bad. At least she never does anything to hurt others, and she'll step up when someone is in danger.]\n\n—some words from residents of Foden City."
},
	[47194]={ language="Information One: Currently self-learning mixology, but often ends up creating drinks that cause strange reactions.\n\nInformation Two: Always mischievous and destructive, but she does it just to get attention.\n\nInformation Three: Really admires Grenache and hopes to become a cool big sister like her."
},
	[47195]={ language="1. Tarot Cards: Rita's homemade tarot cards with special designs, though she's actually clueless about them and just uses them to fool people.n\n2. Dice: Rita carries them as a toy for entertainment and is also a dice expert.n\n3. Grapes: Her favorite fruit, and also the origin of her codename.n\n4. Concealment Cloak: Grenache personally put it on Rita before her first [mission,] she likes it a lot and cherishes it."
},
	[47196]={ language="Information One: Rita grew up without parents and was adopted by the aunt next door. Eventually, she left the aunt's house, so deep down, she really wants a home of her own.\n\nInformation Two: She usually likes to wear hip-hop casual-style clothing and is very interested in street graffiti. She once got in trouble with Grenache for messing up the walls around the [Moonlight Kiss] bar with graffiti.\n\nInformation Three: Rita likes listening to rock music. Several times, the rock music she played herself heated up the bar atmosphere and earned her praise from everyone."
},
	[47197]={ language="Medical Record [Authorization Activated]—This record is supplementary post-surgery\nTreatment Location: Foden City Central Hospital\nMedical Record No: LFD1865653\nName: Rita\nGender: Female\nAge: 12 years 5 months\nChief Complaint: No complaints due to patient's coma.\nPresent Illness: Hit by heavy object, initial diagnosis of tibia fracture.\nPast Medical History: Patient in coma, unknown at present.\nExamination Record:\n1. Fever at 38.5℃, low BP, pulse 67/min, vitals normal.\n2. Swelling and redness near injured joint. Unable to perform palpation and percussion due to coma.\n3. X-ray results show transverse or short oblique tibia fracture lines.\n4. Genetic test results match Alpha injection.\nPreliminary Diagnosis:\n1. Fever caused by internal wound inflammation due to fracture.\n2. Comminuted fracture of tibia and fibula.\nDiscussed treatment plan with medical team: immediate reposition and fixation treatment. Prosthetic implantation and replacement surgery recommended.\nInformed Consent: Patient in coma, consent form signed by escort using personal guarantee for related treatment and surgery.\nSurgical Procedure: Some parts involve ■■■ confidentiality, temporarily unrecordable.\nFollow-Up Observation: Surgery successful; escort to observe, advised immediate return to Healer department if discomfort occurs.\nPhysician Signature: 8245 Tusseil"
},
	[47198]={ language="Information One: She often steals Grenache's cosmetics to play with, but because she always forgets where to put them back, she gets caught for putting them in the wrong places.\n\nInformation Two: She values the friends at the bar very much, treating them like her family, and secretly vows to protect her family forever."
},
	[47199]={ language="[Find joy in mixing drinks, treat it as a delightful journey!]\n\n[Consider every cocktail as a piece of art, create it with care, and make it your masterpiece!]\n\nOn the bar, many bottles and a book titled [Bartender's Quotes] were casually placed, with the first page displaying the above words, highlighted.\n\nAt the other end of the bar, an already tipsy Rita was slouched there, with a drink in front of her head.\n\nIn the Martini glass was a crystal-clear light purple liquid, with a grape elegantly placed at the rim. This was Rita's newest creation, a drink named after her—[Merlot].\n\nIn [Moonlight Kiss,] everyone should have a drink that represents them, except for Rita, which made her very upset. She tried many times to create a drink to represent herself.\n\nAnd today marked the birth of a great work, the signature drink of Rita.\n\nHowever, unlike her coworkers who seem never to get drunk, Rita was the weakest when it came to alcohol in [Moonlight Kiss.] Every time she drank her concoctions, she would pass out right at the bar—\n\nSuddenly, asleep Rita twitched, her fingers touched the tablet in front of her, unlocking the screen and revealing the browsing interface:\n[Ingredients for the Purple Night Cocktail]\n1. Violette liqueur 20ml\n2. Cointreau 40ml\n3. Grape juice 20ml\n4. Ice cubes as needed\n[Detailed Recipe]\nStep 1: Place ice in the glass and stir until frosty\nStep 2: Add 20ml of Violette liqueur\nStep 3: Add 20ml of grape juice\nStep 4: Stir evenly with a long bar spoon\nStep 5: Add 40ml of Cointreau\nStep 6: Add ice cubes, then shake freely to your liking\n"
},
	[47200]={ language="Information One: Rita's Crystal weapon is a sniper cannon as tall as she is. Although Rita is usually mischievous, there's no denying that she is the best sniper in all of Foden City.\n\nInformation Two: Being afraid of pitch-black darkness reminds her of lonely and helpless times."
},
	[47201]={ language="Real Name: Truce Sylvia\nRole: Owner of Uzyanta bar [Moonlight Kiss]\nInterests: Mixing drinks, drinking, playing cards"
},
	[47202]={ language="Fire, explosions, Void Particles spreading like a virus, cries in the dark.\n\nThese were young Truce's last memories of Foden City.\n\nFoden City in southern Uzyanta had always been controlled by gangs, with criminal influence permeating every corner. Almost every day, shady illegal activities took place. No one ever knew when they would be caught up in gang conflicts. Ordinary citizens could only struggle to survive in the cracks.\n\nDuring a gang fight over the Stellar Crystal, an unexpected accident triggered a Crystal explosion. The blast nearly destroyed a part of Foden City and caused widespread Void Particles pollution, leaving devastation in its wake. At the time, Truce's parents were passing through the area with her, and they were unfortunately caught in the explosion.\n\nIn the aftermath of the explosion, Truce watched helplessly as her parents were contaminated by spreading Void Particles. Her parents used all their strength to push her out of the polluted area before being rescued by the arriving Leistance Members. Her last memory was seeing her parents completely transform into monsters.\n\nAll of this was caused by the gangs.\n\nThe tragic scene planted a seed of hatred in the young girl's heart, and she kept telling herself that one day she would return and bring justice to the evildoers.\n\nBesides Truce, some other children survived the explosion.\n\nLeistance took these children for their own purpose. Due to Foden City's unique circumstances, they struggled to establish a branch there, while the south was often hit by Shogger disasters and Crystal catastrophes. Thus, Leistance needed unconventional means to establish a division in Foden City.\n\nThese children from Foden City were the perfect candidates.\n\nLater, Truce and other kids quickly passed the Tutorial of Leistance's internal academy and underwent the D-Blood infusion surgery, becoming AIMBS. They started carrying out Leistance's mission: to establish an operational base in Foden City.\n\nBesides fulfilling Leistance's mission, Truce had her own personal vendetta—she never forgot the gang responsible for her parents' deaths. Hatred drove her rapid growth, and she would find them and make them pay for what happened years ago."
},
	[47203]={ language="Information One: When first started learning to mix drinks, her skills were bad, so she could only drink them herself. Over time, she developed a tolerance for alcohol.\n\nInformation Two: Likes using her charm to tease younger girls and feel happy seeing them blush.\n\nInformation Three: Good at various topics and gives girls advice on love, but she's been single since birth."
},
	[47204]={ language="1. Wine Glass: Specifically for Grenache, casually placed on the bar, but no one dares to touch it.\n\n2. Old Letters: The only relic left by Grenache's parents.\n\n3. [World Famous Wine Tasting]: Records various famous wines, most of which Grenache has collected.\n\n4. Perfume: According to them, it's a [weapon] essential for a boss."
},
	[47205]={ language="Information One: Once attended a tutorial at Leistance, and some events occurred then. She's not fond of bringing up that experience.\n\nInformation Two: [Moonlight Kiss] is privately called a [black shop] by some nosy people. Grenache actually likes this nickname.\n\nInformation Three: Some nosy people have observed that Grenache wears a different lipstick shade every day, each with a different scent."
},
	[47206]={ language="#Foden City Suburb Explosion#\n\nOn the night of August 20, XXXX, an explosion occurred in the A3 Depot area of Foden City's suburbs. After an on-site investigation, police believe the accident was caused by gang members whose firearms and ammunition ignited flammable materials inside the Depot.\n\nAccording to nearby local witnesses, several suspected gang members were seen carrying unknown objects to the Depot before the incident. One of the members was a tall woman. The witness said the Depot area is a major hub for gang activity in Foden City, and gang fights often occur. The citizen immediately called the police upon seeing what seemed to be illegal trade.\n\nPolice have found what appears to be the bodies of gang members inside the Depot.\n\nFoden City Guard Bureau advises citizens to avoid going to the Depot area in the near future. Residents are advised to keep their doors and windows closed and to not provoke any illegal individuals, seeking police help if necessary.\n\nOur reporter will continue to follow and report any further updates."
},
	[47207]={ language="Information One: No matter who you are, the first time you come to [Moonlight Kiss,] you'll definitely be tempted by Grenache and order the most expensive drink.\n\nInformation Two: Claims to be able to drink a thousand cups without getting drunk, but it's because she drinks low-alcohol beverages."
},
	[47208]={ language="Reporter: Grenache\nRecord Time: August 13, XXXX\nReport Content:\nSorry for sending the report only now. After three months, we've successfully infiltrated the underground forces in Foden City and found a suitable base. However, the local gangs don't seem keen on letting us operate smoothly... I'll handle this.\n\nReporter: Grenache \nRecord Time: August 30, XXXX\nReport Content:\nRegarding the base's name... we've decided on a bar called [Moonlight Kiss.] This will be our Information center in Foden City.\n\n......\nAdditionally, about the explosion incident in the Foden City suburbs last time, the investigation reveals it was an accident during illegal trade of Stellar Crystal by the gangs.\nAlthough we managed to control the pollution spread in time, there were still some casualties. The casualty list is attached.\nMoreover, one of the deceased was responsible for the Foden City Void Particles contamination incident in XXXX. The gang led by this person has declined, and we will take further actions regarding this.\n......\n\n[Attachment 1: Overview of Foden City Gangs]\n[Attachment 2: Casualty Statistics from the Incident]\n[Attachment 3: Basic Information and Work Scope of Moonlight Kiss]"
},
	[47209]={ language="Information One: Very self-disciplined, engages in strict fitness tutorials and leg strength tutorials after work.\n\nInformation Two: Likes to bet with guests using playing cards, even decides some trivial matters this way."
},
	[47210]={ language="Real Name: Veldora Valls\nIdentity: Signed artist with Starlog Media\nInterests: Composing, singing."
},
	[47211]={ language="Echo became famous within just a year of debuting, building a strong reputation and gaining popularity quickly. The company really didn't expect that a [part-time idol singer] like her could become famous so fast—there are plenty of singers who look better and sing sweeter than she does. Only Echo knows that her rapid rise and million-fan following are closely tied to her hard work offstage.\n\nEcho really loves her job. She enjoys every moment of singing and loves the feeling of shining on stage. She is proud of being able to bring joy to her fans with her singing and dancing, lighting up their lives.\n\nBecause of this, she doesn't mind putting in much more effort than others.\n\nOn non-performance days, Echo practices for more than 10 hours—3 hours of singing, 5 hours of dancing, and 2 hours of observing and learning. This intense schedule is part of her every day and is the main reason for her fast progress on stage.\n\nTo perform each song perfectly, Echo tirelessly practices again and again, trying to completely align her emotions with the music. She firmly believes that only by pouring her true feelings into a song can she deliver a perfect performance—and her efforts have proven to be worthwhile."
},
	[47212]={ language="Information One: In her spare time, she likes to do yoga. She thinks yoga not only relaxes the body and mind, but also stretches the muscles and bones, helping to quickly grow taller.\n\nInformation Two: She's strictly controlling her diet and managing her body shape.\n\nInformation Three: She knows DJ techniques and enjoys mixing music. This is a skill Echo learned while singing at a bar before debuting as an idol singer."
},
	[47213]={ language="1. Lily: An everlasting lily given by fans at Echo's first public performance, said to symbolize wishes for everything to go smoothly and a happy life.\n\n2. Custom Microphone: A perfect microphone tailored for Echo, capable of reproducing vocals meticulously and clearly, while capturing sound perfectly without being affected by external noise.\n\n3. An Old Record: A twenty-year-old record featuring a beautiful woman on the cover, reportedly the only record released by Echo's mom.\n\n4. Promotional Poster: A promotional poster displaying Echo's debut look, framed and hung at the head of their bed as a debut memento."
},
	[47214]={ language="Information One: Her dream is to become a globally popular idol singer, bringing hope and joy to everyone under the infection of her songs, and becoming the [best idol] in the hearts of her fans.\n\nInformation Two: Echo is known as a [fan-loving idol]. She cherishes every fan who likes her and tries her best to satisfy them. She is constantly working hard to grow so that she doesn't let them down.\n\nInformation Three: Enjoys taking photos and can skillfully use dozens of impromptu photo poses."
},
	[47215]={ language="On March 21, ■■ the long-awaited popular idol singer Echo from Starlog Media finally took the stage at the Lissugen Dome.Besides her classic hits, she also released her latest single [A Future with You] and performed it live at the concert.\n\nAfter the performance, VAMusic interviewed Echo herself.\nInterview written by Monica (VAMusic reporter)\n\n[You have been silent for months, is it true that there are rumors claiming you became AIMBS?]\n\nIn our era, the existence of AIMBS is an indispensable part. If I have the ability, I'd be happy to use my skills in my spare time to fight evil and protect everyone.\nBut currently, I just want to focus on my music.\n\n[What do you think idol singers can do in this era?]\n\nMaking fans happy has always been my goal, and original aspiration, I discuss with many people what idol singers can do—in the current era, the world is unpredictable, and we need to continuously and cautiously think about this issue.\n\n[Could you briefly introduce your new song [A Future with You]?]\nHmm... This song is quite different from my usual style. It's a song full of strength and vitality, expressing joy and a pioneering atmosphere. I tried some new methods to convey these emotions, mainly through the arrangement and rhythm—a bold prelude in the arrangement and noticeable emotional shifts in the rhythm. I hope everyone will like it.\n\n[What's the most memorable lyric in this song?]\nFear cannot defeat me—I look forward to a future with you.\n\n[How do you feel about the choreography for this song?]\nSince this is a release of a new track, I invited a famous choreographer to create the dance, especially the chorus part, which has a distinctive rhythm and arrangement. But with the fast-paced song, the dance moves were quite complicated, and practicing was really challenging (laugh).\n\n[Anything you'd like to say to your fans?]\nAlthough I can't meet all my fans around the world, I will keep working hard and conveying light and warmth through various videos. Please continue to stay passionate and excited!"
},
	[47216]={ language="Information One: In her leisure time, she often listens to music to spark her creative inspiration.\n\nInformation Two: On non-performance days, her daily practice time averages over 10 hours—3 hours of singing practice, 5 hours of dance practice, and 2 hours of study and observation."
},
	[47217]={ language="Echo loves interacting with fans. Even after a busy day of work, she still finds time to communicate with them. Her popularity in her live stream and interactive platform is always high.\n\nSome fans have recorded things Echo said in her live stream, showing she's truly a kind-hearted girl.\n\n—Echo Live Stream Record on February 12,■■\n[When everyone celebrates my birthday, it makes me really happy, truly happy. So many people love me, how could I not be happy? But I often think that earning money isn't easy for fans. In this era, doing these things takes a lot of energy. I hope everyone can do things with more substantial meaning.]\n\n—Echo Live Record on February 18,■■ \n[I really appreciate the family that loves me because this journey is tough. Having you all by my side, if you weren't there, I wouldn't be where I am now. It's hard for me to express my gratitude in words—but I hope people don't do things beyond their ability because they like me. Live your life well, make yourself happy every day, that makes me happiest.]\n\n—Echo Live Record on February 27,■■ \n[I do have made some donations, but I don't want this to be public, nor do I want people to think my charity is a performance. I have encountered difficulties before and felt the pain of having no money—there are too many who need help in this era. Lending a hand can save some families and lives, which is something I can't not do.]\n\n—[Echo Quotes] Echoism Fan Club"
},
	[47218]={ language="Information One: Anonymously made a charitable donation, but for some reason it was eventually discovered.\n\nInformation Two: Actually, Echo doesn't like her cat ear decoration, thinking it makes her look too cute, but since it pleases her fans, she doesn't mind as much."
},
	[47219]={ language="Real Name: Karanissa ·Lancelot\nIdentity: Confidential Operator under Joshburg Government\nInterests: Collecting various lipsticks"
},
	[47220]={ language="Joshburg Central Council is the brain of the strongest Union on this planet. Any topic discussed here directly affects Joshburg, this giant entity, and even impacts the global landscape, meaning it strategizes unimaginable wealth and resources here.\n\nBut besides discussing those glamorous and constructive topics, there are also issues that cannot be known or should not be known to the public, which need to be addressed accordingly.\n\nFor troubles that cannot be publicly resolved, professional individuals are naturally required to ensure the parliament's image remains intact.\n\nElite agents are such professionals, and Karanissa is the elite of elites.\n\nTo the people of Joshburg, the fact that the parliament raises those driven agents, known as dogs, is no secret—they specifically serve those filthy nobles, fulfilling their vile and dirty purposes, and eliminate any informed witnesses.\n\nHowever, Karanissa doesn't care about this and won't let it affect her actions.\n\nShe is just a gun, a gun executing the upper echelon's will; she is also a knife, a sharp knife meant for excising rot."
},
	[47221]={ language="Information One: Extremely dislikes people who ramble.\n\nInformation Two: In great physical shape, could run 100 meters in 12 seconds even before becoming AIMBS.\n\nInformation Three: Likes drinking chilled high-proof spirits, with alcohol content above 75%, just like her mother."
},
	[47222]={ language="1. Dual Guns: Special firearms named [Electricity] and [Light] by Karanissa.\n\n2. Small Trinket: A slightly old small trinket that can be opened, revealing a somewhat faded family photo of four.\n\n3. Lipstick: Combat and beauty can coexist, Karanissa's favorite shade is Dakelyn #202.\n\n4. Badge: A badge composed of a sword, laurel branch, and lion, symbolizing the Lancelot family.\n\n5. Ice Bag: Though called an ice bag, it is actually a small flask that can maintain a constant temperature of 7°C inside."
},
	[47223]={ language="Information One: Has high standards for quality of life and only buys brands they trust.\n\nInformation Two: Actually has a refined taste for luxury items like famous wines, expensive watches, and handcrafted bags.\n\nInformation Three: Once said as a child, [When I grow up, I want to go with my family to see the real starry sky.]"
},
	[47224]={ language="Even within the spy organization, no one knows Karanissa's specific origins.\n\nTrue, hiding your information is a necessary skill for a spy, but Karanissa seems to excel at it – to the point where no one knows who she was or what she did before being officially hired by Joshburg.\n\nShe almost never partners with anyone on missions, nor does she travel with anyone on her way back, and she refuses to engage in any activities besides work with others.\n\nWhenever she completes a commission from the Central Council, Karanissa always leaves alone – some curious people have attempted to follow her, but invariably lose her or are discovered and end up getting a beating.\n\nNo one knows where she lives, how many hideouts she has, or what her identity is after work. Some have claimed to have seen Karanissa in a tavern in Joshburg, while others say they've seen her alone in the Wilderness outside the fortress city, but those who say such things invariably cannot verify the truth of their words.\n\nMaybe Karanissa's origins are truly a mystery?"
},
	[47225]={ language="Information One: Besides gun skills, she actually knows swordsmanship as well, but Karanissa is tight-lipped about where she learned it from.\n\nInformation Two: A speed freak, she owns three fully customized motorcycles—and this number might still be growing."
},
	[47226]={ language="This was a story that happened when someone was young.\n\nDean stood at the door, holding the informed consent for the ■■ plan.\n\nBehind him, Karanissa watched her brother, feeling uneasy—she knew this plan was important for Dean and the Lancelot family, but it came with huge risks.\n\n[Brother, are you really going?] Karanissa asked softly.\n\nHer eyes were slightly wet—she didn't want to lose her brother and feared he'd get hurt in danger.\n\nDean turned around and held his sister's hand.\n\n[Yes, you know what this means for our family…]\n\n[But this plan is dangerous, if anything happens to you…]\n\n[Then you'll be the new head of the Lancelot family.]\n\nPerhaps feeling he was too harsh, Dean softened his tone and patted his sister's shoulder.\n\n[Silly girl, I'll be careful. For the family, I'm willing to take this risk. You have to trust me.]\n\nKaranissa looked up, tears sliding down her young face. [But I don't want you to leave me, I'm afraid I won't see you again…]\n\nDean gently hugged his sister.\n\n[Fool, I'll be back. It's just a temporary separation, we'll be together again. Be strong and take care of yourself.] Outside, the sound of a car engine was heard. Upon hearing this, Dean turned and walked away toward the unknown ■■ plan.\n\nKaranissa didn't realize at this moment that this would be their last meeting before Dean [died]—\n"
},
	[47227]={ language="Information One: The relationship with her brother was once very good, and the current hostile state is very frustrating for Karanissa.\n\nInformation Two: The relationship with Lycosha is both antagonistic and friendly, but privately they are considered drinking buddies."
},
	[47228]={ language="Real Name: Korinna Barrow\nIdentity: Part-time employee at Dreams Consult\nInterests: Hidden weapons, throwing, dark-themed items, vampire and assassin novels"
},
	[47229]={ language="[…Months ago, there was evidence that the duo thieves 'Raven and Dove' had already arrived in our city. Before this, they had just stolen a batch of pure Crystals from the Stellar Crystal industrial exhibition in the neighboring city. There are still no leads on how the stolen goods were sold, but there is evidence that a large anonymous donation received by the city-owned Gospel Orphanage at the end of last month is related to this duo.\n\nThey haven't stolen anything in our city yet, but several Professionals have predicted that their target is likely the antique weapon set 'Eagle Claws' to be exhibited at the International Trade Pavilion downtown next Friday night.\n\nThis weapon set is designed with the concept of raptor claws, with gemstones featuring high-grade cutting techniques, shaped like Simulation hooks—making it a precious collectible with both aesthetic value and historical significance.\n\nMeanwhile, in the hands of specific individuals, it can also be a highly lethal weapon. However, based on the behavior of 'Raven and Dove', even if they manage to steal the treasure, they would return it in its original form a few days later.\n\nCurrently, the police have contacted the exhibition's manager, and they will work closely to ensure the safety of this exhibit. We hope citizens will pay attention to their safety and not gather around the exhibition area. If suspicious individuals are spotted, please report to the relevant authorities immediately...]\n\n[The perfect finale—Fireworks, the last performance of the infamous duo!\n\n...After igniting an exceptionally grand display of Fireworks, 'Raven and Dove' returned their last stolen treasure to the Lissugen City Museum, and under the watchful eyes of Lissugen's citizens, they departed into the night, disappearing behind the dazzling Fireworks!\n\nThat recent heist was said to be the curtain call for this notorious couple. Based on a bold statement they made, from today on, 'Raven and Dove' will no longer act publicly, and they are permanently ending their escapades. However, they believe that talented individuals who are just and enjoy fun won't stop, and a new breed of sky wanderers will soon arise. Perhaps twenty years from now, a new generation might completely take over the world…\n\nSome speculate that their retirement is because they are preparing to start a family, but since no one has ever seen the true faces of 'Raven and Dove', this theory remains questionable.\n\nHowever, it is certain that the world's police forces will lose a formidable adversary, and the suffering people of the world may lose a pair of sanctuaries—or maybe not. Let us continue to watch for the latest news about them with a sense of regret! Perhaps the next generation they hinted about, twenty years later, will be their successors…]\n\n— Two clippings from Korinna's scrapbook"
},
	[47230]={ language="Information One: She's currently attending Lissugen High School for Girls, which is actually a highly selective school. She got in as a special student thanks to her exceptional sports achievements.\n\nInformation Two: Her math scores are shockingly poor, yet she's doing quite well in language classes.\n\nInformation Three: She takes so many days off that some folks joke she writes thirty days' worth of excuses in advance each month to hand in to the teacher on time."
},
	[47231]={ language="1. [Rotor]: A dart given by her parents. It has an unbelievable magical spin speed and is only allowed to be sharpened when Korinna comes of age.\n\n2. [Raven Feather]: A dagger Korinna traded with her boss for using her wages from Dreams Consult. It's remodeled after the rotor and can also be used for throwing—already secretly sharpened.\n\n3. Lollipops: Her pockets are full of them. Grape flavor is her favorite.\n\n4. Flip Phone: Looks like a relic from a past era, covered with flashy stickers. More like a toy than a communication tool.\n\n5. Scrapbook: Filled with clippings of the lovebird thieves [Dove and Raven.] Carefully hidden to avoid being confiscated by her parents."
},
	[47232]={ language="Information One: Really loves eating sweets, prefers full-sugar milk tea, but to keep face, only orders black coffee when visiting milk tea shops with classmates.\n\nInformation Two: Is actually the author of the bestselling novel [Eclipse Over Lissugen] and persistently continues writing online. However, because of school assignments and daily tasks, disappearing is common, earning the nickname [ghostwriter] from readers.\n\nInformation Three: Despite the stark contrast in true personality, the skills are almost on par with the protagonist in the books, hence firmly believes that the writing is non-fiction."
},
	[47233]={ language="[Korinna? I'm not really familiar with her. She always seemed kind of distant, but cool at the same time, so she's a bit hard to approach. But I think she's pretty easygoing. Last time, she was called in to talk with the homeroom teacher about her exam scores, and she didn't react much. I even thought I'd get yelled at for delivering the message...\n\nBut when her parents came to school, they didn't really scold her. Korinna really has super cool parents! I mean, they look very young and have a great sense of humor.\n\nWhile Korinna's dad was talking to our homeroom teacher, I was in the office helping sort out the math and science assignments.\n\nHe cheerfully told the teacher, 'As long as my daughter excels in doing what she loves, that's fine with me. After all, it's soon going to be the next generation's world!' I thought, well, uncle, the problem is Korinna doesn't even have a favorite subject—or maybe, does sports count?\n\nThat seems inherited from her parents because later, when I was taking the assignments back to class, I accidentally dropped the whole stack in the hallway...\n\nBut then a beautiful lady in a dress collected all of them before they hit the ground and handed them back to me! I realized it was Korinna's mom because they really look alike.\n\nYeah, Korinna... her grades aren't great because she's often absent for various reasons, so there's not much to be done. But she's super athletic! Plus, she's really tall. I won't be surprised if she tells me she becomes a sports star in the future.\n\nDuring dodgeball in class, we always want to be on Korinna's team. She's amazing; no one escapes her throws, though getting hit can hurt a bit...\n\nThe literature teacher seems to have a different view on her, though. She always says Korinna's writing is too dark, deep, and unrealistic, not meeting our exam standards.\n\nI haven't read Korinna's essays—seriously, no one dares to ask for them—but I think that's just nitpicking of our test-focused education! At least, I think her style sounds intriguing, like that recent popular novel, 'Eclipse Over Lissugen'. Have you heard of it? I really recommend it. Sometimes, I think Korinna is a lot like the heroine in that book.\n\nYou mentioned you were Korinna's colleague at an off-campus internship. So are you looking for her now, or just asking? I know some companies do background checks, but I thought you'd use online communication instead of coming directly to school...\n\nNo need? Huh, why are you rushing off? I saw Korinna over there! She's coming this way!\n\nHmm, strange person. Their style didn't seem local, maybe I shouldn't have said that...]\n—Comments from a classmate about Korinna"
},
	[47234]={ language="Information One: While working at Dreams Consult, she was long exploited by the boss, but personally, she dosen't think there's anything wrong with that. It's entirely reasonable for the heroine to go through trials.\n\nInformation Two: Very interested in the retired couple of chivalrous thieves [Raven and Dove], collected many clippings about them. However, her parents don't seem to support this."
},
	[47235]={ language="Dear Miss Newcastle,\n\nHope this letter finds you well.\n\nThis letter might seem impolite or even provocative, as it hasn't been tastefully sent as a message to your communicator, nor through the official postal system. It's merely appeared on your desk, like an uninvited guest. But there is a certain romance and meaning in traditional ways; written agreements are more solemn. Please understand our concern and affection as parents for our child.\n\nAlthough we embrace open-minded education and have long adopted a free-range attitude toward our child, even when she found the [Pandora's Box] from depot that completely changed her fate, we didn't intervene. After all, the sky of the future belongs to the fledgling, and new raptors will take over the order under the night. It's a natural process. Yet knowing she chose your Missions as a part-time work location, we inevitably worry for her. The world isn't as peaceful and serene as people imagine, and the profound shadows behind this facade are not meant for her to delve into at such a young age. Your work is all about digging deep into presented issues, and she's evidently capable of becoming a significant asset to this mission having learned from us. We worry this might have a negative impact on her.\n\nOf course, this letter is also about truths we don't want her to know prematurely. As our child, she deserves a peaceful childhood, something not easily achieved, hence our willingness to pay the price to ensure this effort is not in vain. Previously, we've only confiscated her secretly kept clippings to express our disapproval. But now that she's part of your team, our actions are more limited. Thus, we hope you can strictly keep the secret we've now disclosed to you until Korinna comes of age, and promise to protect her safety. Otherwise, the long-vanished pirates will visit your window, leaving more than just a letter behind.\n\nSincerely,\nRaven and Dove"
},
	[47236]={ language="Information One: Walks silently, likes to observe from the shadows. Often appears suddenly like a creature from the abyss, frequently startling others.\n\nInformation Two: Actually gets along with most people, but tends to be quiet. Even without intending to, there's a subtle tendency to become the school's leader."
},
	[47237]={ language="Real Name: Alice\nIdentity: Executive of the mysterious organization [Coordinator Sect]\nInterests: Unknown, rumored to be cooking"
},
	[47238]={ language="Recently, there's a rumor on the internet about a [UFO]—\n\nIt's a strange bird in red, white, and black, frequently appearing in the night sky, tearing through the air at lightning speed, crossing the heavens like a Meteor.\n\nIs this a new UFO? Or an unknown creature? With continuous reports, it's becoming a new urban legend.\n\nUnlike urban legends that only concern the general public, this [white strange bird] has caught the attention of major powers. The reason is simple—sightings of this creature have occurred in different territories of various Unions—but only sightings, not a single real photo has appeared. All claimed images of the white strange bird are plagued by black noise.\n\nMajor powers suspect this is a new kind of Mutant—judging by the distribution of sightings, there must have been a massive Void Expanse nearby, and Mutants arising within is quite normal.\n\nBut... the surprising part is... after the strange bird's appearance, the number of Mutants locally almost vanished.\n\n[If my guess is right, the white strange bird seems to be hunting Mutants... no, more accurately, exterminating them? But what kind of creature would have such power? It's too unrealistic, too bizarre...]\n\n—Ecology Researcher A"
},
	[47239]={ language="Information One: Once bid on the limited edition plush of [Little Donkey Family] with someone online, but lost due to not having enough money.\n\nInformation Two: Hates people who don't follow etiquette.\n\nInformation Three: Makes delicious dishes, but without exception, they all look terrible."
},
	[47240]={ language="1. Donkey Plush: The main character Danchey's Plush from the timeless stop-motion animation [Little Donkey Family,] has been with Alice for at least ten years \n\n2. Scarf: A scarf someone gave to Alice, one of her favorite personal items \n\n3. Silver Pendant: An accessory that Alice always keeps with her, possibly like a talisman."
},
	[47241]={ language="Information One: Has a special fondness for B-movies and privately collects many classic B-movie copies.\n\nInformation Two: Average learning ability, did not pass Joshburg's universal [Encyclopedia Grand Exam] for adult citizens.\n\nInformation Three: Known for being skillful, but sometimes the crafts made can look quite peculiar..."
},
	[47242]={ language="Once again, she wakes up in the wilderness.\n\nBeside her lies the remains of Mutants yet to face annihilation.\n\n Surrounded by boundless chaos.\n\nVoid Particles drift through the chaos, irritating her.\n\nAbove is only the dim, fake starry sky.\n\nIt's nauseating.\n\nshe stands up, feeling a bit weary, but it's actually a pleasure—for this body injected with D-Blood, fatigue is a luxury.\n\nPain brings the real sensation of being alive, but excessive strength has stripped that sensation away.\n\nAnger fuels the will to survive, and without pain, anger is all that sustains her—\n\nIt's time to move to the next hunting ground; in the ever-nightfall of the Wilderness, countless pitiable creations await her.\n\nIt's not an end, but a mercy.\n\nAlice spread her wings once more, like thunder, soaring into the sky."
},
	[47243]={ language="Information One: A bit troubled that the [feathers] her hair has turned into are too fluffy; she often spends time tidying it up.\n\nInformation Two: Very satisfied with her fighting style, she likes to provoke and taunt opponents in battle to bring out their full strength."
},
	[47244]={ language="Even among the eccentric Coordinator Sect, Alice is the most unique.\n\nShe never arrives on time for any gathering, and she shows up less than half the time. Even when the cult leader himself is present, her attendance rate only goes up by 10%.\n\nEvery time she takes action outside, Alice chooses to travel alone to her destination—she sweeps across the eternal night of the Wilderness with her wings, destroying every Mutant along the way like a relentless storm.\n\nAlthough Alice is quite rude in her interactions with every Adjuster, she unexpectedly has the best relationships within the group—perhaps in this complex cult, Alice, who acts purely on emotion and instinct, is the most genuine presence."
},
	[47245]={ language="Information One: Previously had an implant called [emotional nail] that allows enduring pain.\n\nInformation Two: Actually a very kind person who donates a small amount of money every month to a chosen charity."
},
	[47255]={ language="Real Name: Viano Alexandra Ahmatova\nIdentity: Leistance Security Bureau tactical instructor\nInterests: Tutorial, reading literature books"
},
	[47256]={ language="Viano's parents came from Uzyanta, and were among the many industrial immigrants brought in by Burksomi. Although called industrial immigrants, this was merely a fancy term Burksomi used for [cheap labor.] Most of them were assigned to work at factories or ores, doing basic manual labor in poor working conditions all day long, yet earning very little pay.\n\nUnder such circumstances, Viano's parents were assigned to work at a small mine in northern Burksomi. The monotonous life wasn't unbearable for them—compared to the dead-end life in Uzyanta, the stability of the mine was exactly what they needed most. Three years after arriving in Burksomi, they had a daughter, Viano.\n\nAs Viano grew up, her family's situation began to change. Her parents believed she should become a scholar, to change her fate through education and leave the mine for a better life. They even went to the extent of registering a fully Burksomi name for her on official records—Viano Aleksandrovna Akhmatova.\n\nHowever, after some personal reflection, Viano didn't pursue the academic path her mother hoped for but chose a different route—instead, she applied to join a military academy.\n\nViano's decision to join the military wasn't due to poor academic performance. On the contrary, her grades were among the top at the mine's local school. The real reason she chose to become a soldier was that she understood Burksomi's martial and aggressive state. She believed becoming a soldier was the quickest way to fulfill her parents' expectations.\n\nWhen the admission letter from the military academy arrived at Viano's home, her parents finally became aware of her choice. Although they were a bit upset that she kept it a secret from them, they also understood Viano's nature and ultimately accepted her decision."
},
	[47257]={ language="Information One: Because of years of tough tutorials, she adheres to a HPy diet. But she hasn't completely quit snacks yet, and her taste is very spicy, often accidentally burning those who want a small bite.\n\nInformation Two: She has quite strict self-requirements and show no mercy during tutorials. At such times, she's a typical case of responding to firmness rather than softness—whining or pleading will only have an adverse effect.\n\nInformation Three: Due to the strict demands during tutorials, she's earned the title of [devil instructor,] and her name is known within Leistance Security Bureau for its ability to stop children from crying at night."
},
	[47258]={ language="1. Wine Collection: Surprisingly has a dedicated wine cabinet with half stocked with various wines, and half with Burksomi's specialty spirits. Likes to have a couple drinks after work.\n\n2. [How Crystals Are Made]: The most frequently read book in the entire bookshelf. There are similar books like [The Silent Shield River ] and [The Stars Here Are Quiet].\n\n3. Personal File of the Trainee: Very thick and detailed, even to the extent that the personnel department regularly borrows it from Lionblade.\n\n4. Old Medals: Old medals from Burksomi, seemingly carelessly tossed deep in the drawer, but judging from their condition, they appear to be frequently handled."
},
	[47259]={ language="Information One: There's a long-lasting boring game among Leistance battle trainees: correctly spelling Instructor Lionblade's full name.\n\nInformation Two: Known for meticulously caring for everyone. Often makes people cry miserably during tutorials, and witnesses many trainees shed tears of reluctance at the end.\n\nInformation Three: Enjoys reading Burksomi's novels in free time, even has a notebook for jotting down quotes to educate trainees during Tutorials."
},
	[47260]={ language="After graduating from the military academy and officially joining the military, Viano quickly made a name for herself in her unit. Whether it was domestic security maintenance or international proxy conflicts, her team was very active and perfectly accomplished the tasks assigned by superiors. With her red hair, she soon checked up to the rank of Major and was given the title [Red Lion.] Consequently, her team became known as the Red Lion Squad.\n\nThe military awards and rapid rank promotions brought Viano many benefits. She bought property in the capital of Burksomi and brought her parents to live in the capital.\n\nHowever, good times never last. With Viano's rapid rise in rank, a series of problems followed. In Burksomi, where the military and politics were heavily intertwined, officers who reached a certain rank often aligned with a political faction for various reasons. As a Major, Viano was no exception. But when it came time to choose a side, she didn't align like other officers. She chose to avoid all kinds of recruitment, believing that being a good soldier and fulfilling her duties given by the country was enough.\n\nThis neutral stance soon brought trouble for Viano. Although her popularity and skill made her a prized asset in the eyes of senior generals, after several unsuccessful attempts to recruit her, she became someone to eliminate.\n\nFinally, during a [peacekeeping] mission in the Joshburg controlled area, Viano's team encountered Joshburg's military, which were also proxy campaign personnel. After intense fighting, they retreated to the relay supply point, but no expected support arrived—they were abandoned by Burksomi.\n\nWhat followed were a series of events worthy of a movie. After narrowly escaping death and returning to the Burksomi-controlled area with a handful of surviving subordinates, Viano was arrested by the Burksomi military court. She was charged with [disobeying military orders,] [taking unauthorized actions,] and [causing civilian casualties,] with dubious accusations leading to her being stripped of her rank and sentenced to two years in prison."
},
	[47261]={ language="Information One: She's very moderate when it comes to drinking but can really hold her liquor. No one has ever seen her drunk. More than once, trainees have heard her claim in communications, [There's no difference between the alcohol here and juice.]\n\nInformation Two: Although she's called the devil instructor, during holidays she often receives the most gifts in the base, which makes others quite jealous."
},
	[47262]={ language="Sentencing Authority: Burksomi Central Military Committee Adjudication Agency Third Tribunal\n\nConvicted Person: Viano Aleksandrovna Akhmatova\n\nUnit: Burksomi Army, Central First Group Army, Special Control Forces [Solken,] Second Battalion, First Company, Third Platoon\n\nCurrent Rank: Platoon Leader, Second-Class Major.\n\nCharge: Violation of military orders; unauthorized seizure of weapons; unauthorized contact with non-essential targets; unauthorized use of dangerous arms to engage with non-essential targets; causing civilian casualties.\n\nFirst Judgment: Convicted person Viano Aleksandrovna Akhmatova committed the following actions during the operation on ■■, ■■, ■■■■at ■■■■, ■■■.\n…\n…\n…\nIn view of the above actions, the convicted person Viano Aleksandrovna Akhmatova is sentenced to a five-year imprisonment and stripped of her rank. However, considering her contributions during her service in the group army, the Central Military Committee deems it necessary to conduct a second trial based on her military service record.\n\nSecond Judgment: After unanimous voting by the ■■■ tribunal, the convicted person Viano Aleksandrovna Akhmatova is issued a final sentence of a two-year imprisonment and stripped of her rank. The convicted person has no objection to this judgment and will be handed over to ■■■■ and ■■■■■■ for subsequent processing.\n\n—Burksomi Central Military Committee, Verdict No. 23149"
},
	[47263]={ language="Information One: Has a terribly rigid schedule, but easily suffers from insomnia when troubled. When experiencing insomnia, disguises it by patrolling at night and tucking in the students.\n\nInformation Two: Regularly sends money to their parents. Having learned some social tact, when asked about their current situation, they describe their job as a [kindergarten teacher]."
},
	[47264]={ language="Real Name: Michesse Christo\nIdentity: Leistance Security Bureau Headquarters Crystal Weaponry Development Staff\nInterests: Crystal Weapon Design, Dolls, Tech Research"
},
	[47265]={ language="[Leistance Security Bureau Employee Interview Record A02138]\nConfidential Level: Lv.2\n\nName: Michesse\nCode Name: Prism\nGender: Female\nAge: 18\nHeight: 165\nOrigin: Joshburg\n\nIntended Position: Leistance Security Bureau Crystal Weapon Development Department Researcher\n\nComprehensive Evaluation Results:\nThe applicant's professional abilities are outstanding, impressing both in intelligence and practical experience. Physical fitness is excellent, mental strength exceeds average standards, possessing basic qualifications for becoming an AIMBS Operator.\n*Note*\nThe applicant seems to have concealed her origin. For security reasons, in-depth investigation is recommended.\n\n10.01 Update—\nPreliminary investigation confirms she is the daughter of a Joshburg Upper House [data deleted] member. Childhood experience includes kidnapping, leading to strict family protection. Left home alone months ago without causing a stir, indicating some consensus with family, though specifics remain unclear. Applicant has no salary demands, appearing unaware of such concepts. If recruiting this applicant as an AIMBS Operator, a contingency plan to handle her background is needed.\n\n10.02 Update—\n\nDue to the impact of childhood trauma, her mental HP needs verification. The nature and operation of the doll [Narcissus] accompanying her require further understanding.\n\n20.01—\nConfirmed [Narcissus] is not a strong AI. Applicant has some communication difficulties but shows no anti-social tendencies. After consideration, decided to hire this applicant as a Leistance Security Bureau Crystal Weapon Development Department Researcher."
},
	[47266]={ language="Information One: Her office has air conditioning running all year round, and it's even colder than the refrigerated section of a large warehouse store. Initially, some thought it was a way to drive people away. Later, Michesse hung a winter coat at the office door for visitors to use during long conversations.\n\nInformation Two: Unless you explicitly request to speak with Michesse herself, it's likely that her puppet Narcissus will answer you.\n\nInformation Three: She enjoys designing appearances for Narcissus, and the final product often matches her own attire."
},
	[47267]={ language="1. Crystal Weapon: A self-forged long sword named Echo, capable of unleashing powerful ice attribute Energy. Narcissus has an identical one.\n\n2. Narcissus: A doll that can be considered the other half of Mischess. No one has ever seen them apart.\n\n3. Design Manuscript Collection: Half consists of design drawings for Crystal weapons, the other half consists of clothing design sketches.\n\n4. An ice cube-shaped magic cube: A transparent cube kept at zero degrees, which Prism carries around outdoors without air conditioning... It seems to be a controller for something."
},
	[47268]={ language="Information One: Narcissus wasn't actually placed in an independent strong AI. Michesse manipulates her like a puppet master through some technique.\n\nInformation Two: The puppet Narcissus is completely different from Michesse. She's lively, enthusiastic, and very talkative. Many people have witnessed Narcissus telling jokes to amuse Michesse. It seems like she only shows emotion when facing her puppet.\n\nInformation Three: Even though no one has seen them apart, there seems to be a consensus: If that kind of thing happens, it would have catastrophic consequences."
},
	[47269]={ language="Interview Record Appendix: Candidate Process Record\n[Attachment-Interview Process Record Segment 01]\nQ: Miss Michesse, hello. Congratulations on reaching the final round of interviews.\nA: Hello. Thank you.\nQ: The person behind you is…\nA: This is Narcissus.\n(The human-shaped mechanical creation beside the candidate greets the interviewer)\nYes, certainly—it's best to consider us as one entity; it makes things much easier.\nQ: …Alright.\nA: Thank you for understanding.\n\n[Attachment-Interview Process Record Segment 02]\nQ: Do you mind answering this question? We want to know why you want to join Leistance Security Bureau.\nA: I…like developing Crystal Weapon.\nQ: Is that all? Your intentions include becoming an AIMBS Operator, which is not just research work. We hope you've thought this through, because regrets or disputes can lead to unimaginable trouble.\nA: That's it. There won't be any trouble.\n(The human-shaped mechanical creation nods)\nSee, Narcissus says the same. You have our assurance.\n\n[Attachment-Interview Process Record Segment 03]\nQ: Do you have any salary expectations?\nA: No.\nQ: …\nA: Or, what kind of salary level would allow me to live here indefinitely?\nQ: What kind of…?\n(The human-shaped mechanical creation touches the candidate's shoulder)\nA: Ah…please ignore what I just said. If possible, I'd prefer a work environment with sufficient air conditioning. Other than that…no other requests."
},
	[47270]={ language="Information One: Michesse owns a villa specifically for placing her dolls and Crystal Weapon which hasn't been utilized after design yet. Later, that piece of land was expanded into an exhibition hall.\n\nInformation Two: If you mention dolls to Michesse, she'll unexpectedly become very talkative. Before she realizes it, she can go on talking with you for hours. Meanwhile, Narcissus won't join your conversation."
},
	[47271]={ language="I've always heard that Miss Prism from the General Bureau's Crystal Weapon Development Department is... quite a unique person, but I never got to see her in person. It wasn't until I was responsible for tracking a batch of equipment inspection and storage that I finally got a chance to talk to her.\n\nMiss Prism's office is really, really cold! As cold as her expression. She even has a warm jacket hanging behind the office door for guests, which I guess means she's not that hard to get along with. While working, Miss Prism had no intention to make small talk, but the doll behind her named Narcissus warmly greeted me and asked me not to mind.\n\nNarcissus is totally different from her master. While Miss Prism was busy checking forms, she was chatting with me, from what I had for breakfast to what I was wearing that day. She even said that earrings suited me better than ear studs and that I suited blue better than red. It made me curious about what kind of programming controls Narcissus. I cautiously gathered my courage and asked Miss Prism if Narcissus was equipped with strong artificial intelligence, but she shook her head.\n\nMiss Prism, with a very cold tone, firmly and curtly said, [Narcissus is me.]\n\nShe didn't seem to be joking and clearly didn't like others guessing like that. I quickly apologized. For the first time all day, I felt Miss Prism was indeed a bit odd... but stranger things were yet to come.\n\nAfter thanking Miss Prism and leaving, I discovered in the corridor that there was a spot on the form that still needed a signature, so I hurriedly returned. As I was about to knock on the Development Department office door again, I heard voices inside.\n\nAh... it was Miss Prism talking to Narcissus.\n\nI heard Miss Prism say, [Did I scare her? Sorry... if only I could be more like Narcissus...]\n\nAnd Narcissus replied, [It's okay, Michesse did really well today!]\n\nI must admit, this actually scared me... I fled with the form in hand, pretending I didn't notice the spot that needed a signature, and handed it in directly. Afterwards, no one mentioned it again, which was a relief.\n\nHmm... what is going on here? \n—A Leistance Security Bureau employee"
},
	[47272]={ language="Information One: You might hear Michesse repeat word for word what you said to her a few months ago, as she claims it's for learning purposes.\n\nInformation Two: She has a very strong talent in Crystal Weapon design, advocating for a minimalist style and pure, ultimate power."
},
	[47273]={ language="Real Name: Ivylona\nIdentity: Burn Bear Mercenary\nInterests: Racing, modifying motorcycles"
},
	[47274]={ language="In the economically depressed south of Uzyanta, most families have to work in ores to make a living, leaving their children lacking parental love. These kids often become precocious and rebellious, skipping school and hanging out on the streets, gradually turning into [troubled teens] in the eyes of teachers and parents. The [Skull Club] is a group of such troubled teens in the town where Ivylona is from.\n\nIvylona had known about the [Skull Club] for a long time, but actually encountered these so-called troubled peers due to a seemingly fated coincidence.\n\nShe couldn't remember the last time she opened her textbooks. After an argument with a teacher, she jumped over the school wall and, coincidentally, landed on a passing bike.\n\nThe rider was startled and forgot to brake, and just like that, without either fully understanding what was happening, the unicycle sped all the way to the [Skull Club] base, an abandoned factory.\n\nMost of the troubled teens gathered here were known to Ivylona. When the two got off the bike, one of the waiting kids complained, [Skull, what's taking you so long? We were supposed to have a race today. Why'd you bring someone else?]\n\n[Sorry, sorry, it was an accident,] the boy who had brought her there explained with a wry smile to his companions.\n\nThat's when Ivylona realized her ride was with Skull, the notorious troubled teen.\n\n[So, is this a... junk bike expo?] Ivylona lifted her chin, inspecting the unibikes parked in the depot.\n\nThey were all assembled from scrap materials, and the midnight street racing noises were their handiwork.\n\n[This junk bike brought you here,] the boy named [Skull] confidently patted the seat. [We're racing today. My junk bike can go faster. Interested?]\n\nRecalling the thrill of speeding just moments before, Ivylona nodded almost involuntarily.\n\nAnd that's how she met the [Skull Club] and quickly bonded with them over their shared experiences.\n\nThese [rebellious teens] were not what everyone thought. Skull was just a kid who liked eccentric clothes and unicycles, and they all gathered around bikes for warmth and friendship. Skull's dad was a mechanic, and he grew up using tools. Everyone's bikes in the club were made from found materials and assembled by Skull.\n\nIvylona's bike was also assembled with Skull's help.\n\nThough made from junk, they enjoyed it, the speed and excitement making Ivylona feel she had found her true self, free-spirited and cool. The roar of the shoddy engines often drew complaints from residents at night, who only ever saw their bikes speeding away.\n\nLater, they all set a goal: to earn big money and own the best unibikes, and participate in races under the name of the [Skull Club] to win championships."
},
	[47275]={ language="Information One: Often gives her motorcycle various nicknames, leading others to mistakenly think she has several motorcycles.\n\nInformation Two: Enthusiastic about changing motorcycle paint jobs, but she's terrible at doing it herself, always buys the paint and finds someone else to do it.\n\nInformation Three: Learned a lot of trash talk while hanging out on the streets, and occasionally uses it to taunt opponents during competitions."
},
	[47276]={ language="1. Multifunctional Toolbox: Used for modifying and repairing motorcycles, each tool is made to Ivylona's most comfortable specifications.\n\n2. Paint Sprayers: Ivylona uses them to regularly change the paint job of her motorcycle.\n\n3. Replay Data Box: Contains recordings of major unicycle racing competitions so Ivylona can watch and learn anytime.\n\n4. Skull Handkerchief: A symbol of Ivylona's agreement with the club, with designs everyone created together.\n\n5. Racing magazine: A racing magazine that Ivylona buys every issue, she particularly likes the motorcycle modification section."
},
	[47277]={ language="Information One: After becoming AIMBS, the only requirement for her crystal weapon is [it must be a unicycle motorcycle.]\n\nInformation Two: During her chuunibyou phase, she fantasized about looking the coolest by waiting at the school gate on a motorcycle, saying to the waiting schoolgirls, [Hop on, I'll take you for a ride,] but this has never happened.\n\nInformation Three: She used to be a class-skipping rebel, with the longest time skipping school being two months without attending a single day."
},
	[47278]={ language="It's like all good things have an expiration date, always arriving unexpectedly. The news of the mine collapse where their parents worked hit like a heavy blow, shattering the dreams of these naive teenagers, forcing them to return from their dreams to reality.\n\nAfter the club disbanded, [Skull] left his motorcycle to Ivylona.\n\nThe boy's entrusted dream became Ivylona's motivation to keep going. To earn money, she had to work various jobs during the day, but whenever she had free time, she participated in unicycle racing everywhere. Her skilled techniques and wild style, contrasting with her appearance, made her quite popular in the underground racing world.\n\nDuring an underground race, an agent from the famous motorcycle club Uzyanta noticed her and asked if she'd like to sign with the club and participate in official races.\n\nThe high competition rewards and signing fee gave Ivylona a glimpse of a turning point. She signed the contract to represent the club in official races, stepping into the public eye, and gradually became famous in the racing scene. She got the top-end motorcycle she had always dreamed of. Even though she couldn't use Skull's name, she still bore the name [Skull] in races.\n\nAn international unicycle race was approaching, and the opponents were very strong. To ensure she won, the agencyt injected her with illegal performance-enhancing substances under the guise of a routine check-up, all without her knowledge.\n\nHowever, this move did not help Ivylona win. In fact, she was discovered by the race committee midway through the race due to a rejection reaction and was disqualified.\n\nTo avoid responsibility, the club terminated her contract. She was banned for life by the race committee and faced a manhunt by the authorities. If not for a chance rescue by the Maritimus couple, she wouldn't know where she might have died, in some forgotten corner.\n\nBecoming AIMBS meant she could no longer participate in races as a regular person, nor return to normal life. It meant her old dreams could never be achieved again, and she would never race under the name [Skull] again.\n\nThe speed she once prided herself on was no longer a limit to break through with her extraordinary abilities. Regular races no longer appealed to her, but she still loved motorcycles, the roar of engines, and the sting of wind against her face at high speeds.\n\nEven if she can't race under the competition's name, she thought, perhaps the promises of the past could be fulfilled in another way."
},
	[47279]={ language="Information One: Initially, she joined Burn Bear just because it was easier to make money, but in the end, she treated the mercenary group as a [team].\n\nInformation Two: Both parents are alive, and she sends money home every month."
},
	[47280]={ language="[Sports News Entry: Popular Racer Mustang Issues Statement: [Permanent Withdrawal]? Is There More to the Story?]\n[A Screenshot]\nViews: 13XXX Shares: XXXX Comments: 6787 Likes: XXXX\nIvylona's Dog: ????? What? No! I don't accept this!!!\nReply: @Ivylona's Dog: What's wrong? If you're having trouble, just talk about it! Why are you withdrawing? What am I going to do now? Boo hoo hoo QAQ\nReply: @Ivylona's Dog: Okay, no matter what choice you make, I'll support you QWQ\nPassing Curious Ravend: Seems like I recognize this name. Who is it?\nGossip Expert: Reply: @Passing Curious Ravend: Unicycle racer, privately injected drugs and rigged a race three months ago in an international competition, illegal drugs too, the kind that are life-threatening. Really brought this on herself.\nIvylona's Dog: Reply: @Gossip Expert: Stop spreading rumors, internet warriors! I've been following her races for so long; she's not that kind of person! Someone must have framed her! She'll be okay!\nGossip Expert: Reply: @Ivylona's Dog: Fans, stop defending her here. I'm just stating facts. Who knows if this is even about her.\nRacing Fanatic: Suspicions? What suspicions? It's match-fixing, what more is there to say?\n…\nCrystal Dealer: I have a friend who works odd jobs at the club; he said Mustang used to be a troubled teen from the slums. It's not surprising she'd do such a thing for money, especially since the prize this time is big.\n…\nMotorbike Enthusiast: Think a simple apology statement clears things up? Racing is sacred! Take responsibility properly!\n…\nPassing Scientist: It's been three months. If it was Void Particles, an illegal drug, she wouldn't have survived long. The authenticity of this statement is questionable.\nAspiring AIMBS: Very suspicious. If she knew it was a life-threatening illegal drug, why would anyone actively ask to inject it? Where did she get the drugs? I can't believe the club knows nothing.\n…\nCity Wanderer: Saw Burn Bear doing security at Lissugen a couple of days ago; seems like there's a new sister working there who looks quite like Mustang.\nIvylona's Dog: Reply: @City Wanderer: Where did you see them? Any pics?\nCity Wanderer: Reply: @Ivylona's Dog: No pictures allowed, just a back view [Image Message]\nIvylona's Dog: Reply: @City Wanderer: Thank you, thank you, though it's hard to see, if that's her, it'd be great!\n..."
},
	[47281]={ language="Information One: The motorcycle jackets are all designed by herself, but some of the overly outrageous designs are privately mocked by the producers.\n\nInformation Two: There are speeding tickets stuffed in the nightstand, stacked up to at least over ten centimeters high."
},
	[47291]={ language="Real Name: Unknown\nIdentity: Dreams Consult bodyguard and technical professional\nInterests: Calligraphy creation, drinking, appreciating crafts, jade appreciation"
},
	[47292]={ language="List of items for travel:\n1. A jug of Little Sis's favorite Huadiao wine\n2. Three sets of Little Sis's sect clothes\n3. Little Sis's favorite jade set\n4. Lissugen brochure (with map)\n5. The crane Tuantuan you've plucked (crossed out) (Note: Do not take sect pets!!!)\n6, …\n…\n—\nDear Little Sis, these are the travel items we've prepared for you, all packed up~\n\nAbout the bet and having to leave the sect to travel... we're really sorry, it's not the senior brothers and sisters ganging up on you. You're the most cherished little sis in our sect, and we hate to see you travel alone, but... we must all leave the mountain gate eventually. We hope the first to leave is you because you possess talents we don't have, and these talents might bring some change to this messed-up world.\n\nThere are many rumors about us in the outside world, and misunderstandings about Spark. This journey is a chance to clear up those misunderstandings and promote Spark culture.\n\nWe know our Little Sis isn't truly introverted, so if you're feeling a bit uneasy about yourself, have some more wine. After drinking, you'll surely make some friends!\n\nWe hope you have a great time in Lissugen and remember we're all thinking of you.\n\n(Keep your ability to seal Shogger a secret!)\n\n(There are many bad people out there, take care of yourself and don't get your wallet stolen again.)"
},
	[47293]={ language="Information One: She didn't really like drinking alcohol as a kid, it was all because of being pushed by senior students.\n\nInformation Two: Getting drunk releases a hidden personality, but she firmly denies it.\n\nInformation Three: Her favorite calligraphy style is cursive script, but she's terrible at it. Her writing in other calligraphy styles actually looks pretty good."
},
	[47294]={ language="1. White Jade Hairpin: Given by senior sister as a farewell gift for going to the outside world.\n\n2. Sword Sheath: Used for holding a sword, not needed most of the time, only used in public places.\n\n3. Wine Jug: A small wine jug made from jade from her hometown, carried around.\n\n4. Feather pen: Material comes from a bird called [crane] from her hometown, brought a few when leaving.\n\n5. Pine Inkstone: A black object, hard to imagine where she got it from, said to be a specialty of her hometown."
},
	[47295]={ language="Information One: As a kid, she actually didn't like drinking, but after being teased by good-natured relatives, she fell in love with the feeling of being drunk.\n\nInformation Two: It's said that getting drunk releases your hidden personality—though this claim is not very reliable.\n\nInformation Three: Her favorite calligraphy style is [wild cursive], and when intoxicated, her writings become completely illegible to everyone but herself."
},
	[47296]={ language="I'm Raven, this is the 2014th voice log record, about my new colleague.\n...\nWhen boss said she'd found a new employee to help with our workload and insisted strongly that I attend the welcome party, I was really resistant. It's not that I'm against new colleagues, I just can't help wondering who's stepping into this mess. The thought of the welcome party money being deducted from my salary makes me sad.\n\nBut I still had to go.\n\nAt the welcome party, when I first saw the girl dressed in a style with obvious regional cultural flair, just a glance told me we were the same type of people, both socially anxious and uncomfortable in such settings. After introducing ourselves, we settled into a comfortable silence.\n\nInitially, I was puzzled about how boss managed to convince her to join, until boss, who was all about promises, started pouring drinks.\n\nI watched as the girl, who only said [Hello, my name is Yan] throughout the party, drank bottle after bottle without a change in expression and then got drunk. With that much alcohol, getting drunk is expected, right? Boss who kept encouraging her to drink should really take responsibility!\n\nWhat happened next was... a bit more than I anticipated. I'd heard of people behaving oddly when drunk, but I didn't expect her to completely switch personality… She started chatting away nonstop and even pulled me aside, saying she wanted to become sworn siblings.\n\nSworn siblings... what does that even mean?\n\nIn the end, she gave me a jade bracelet as a meeting gift, which is kind of her, I guess? It seemed fragile, so I put it away.\n\nSo, that's how we bizarrely became good friends.\n\nTo add, when she sobered up, she completely forgot what she'd said, and I decided not to remind her…"
},
	[47297]={ language="Information One: Deciding to learn jade identification stemmed from being deceived by fake jade sold at a street stall and losing pocket money in her youth.\n\nInformation Two: Occasionally forget where she buried the jar of her homemade wine.\n\nInformation Three: Wants to learn mixology, but lacks any talent in this area."
},
	[47298]={ language="For the employees of Dreams Consult, the lively festival in Lissugen isn't much different from usual. Their exploitative boss doesn't give them time off just because of the festival. In the boss's words, it's during such times that unexpected things are discovered. Surprisingly, today the boss let everyone take a day off. Yan, who usually follows the boss around as a bodyguard, suddenly finds herself unsure of how to spend this rare day off.\n\nThis is her first time acting on her own.\n\nTo Yan, life in Lissugen is fresh and interesting, but also full of changes and uncertainties. Initially, her outfit, distinct with Spark cultural elements, attracted quite a few looks, making her even quieter given her introverted nature, and reluctant to engage with others. But now she's completely accustomed to life here, never forgetting her original purpose.\n\nWith just a drinking session, she can become friends with anyone… as long as those embarrassing words aren't recorded.\n\nIn the morning, she practiced martial arts and calligraphy at home, then used the feathered pen she brought from her sect to write a letter back to them. After a simple meal, she went to a bar she and her boss often visit, planning to spend her afternoon there.\n\nOnce life falls into place, the routine daily life isn't much different from when she was in Spark.\n\nAs usual, she ordered a large cup of highly distilled liquor, found a quiet corner, and took out her special tools to carve the high-quality jade she'd previously received but hadn't had the chance to work on.\n\nA reporter who happened to be spending the weekend at the same bar noticed her and conducted a simple interview after seeking her consent. However, there was a bit of a mishap; Yan got nervous and kept drinking during the interview, eventually getting herself drunk, and she didn't remember what she said.\n\nAfter sobering up, she recalled drinking too much and having too much fun, casually giving the jade to the reporter.\n\nThat evening, sober and back home, Yan regretfully felt like banging her head against the wall, perhaps because of the hard-earned jade or maybe because her entirely different side was seen by a stranger. But perhaps next time, she won't learn from this lesson either.\n\nThis is the ordinary day-off routine for Dreams Consult's bodyguard Yan."
},
	[47299]={ language="Information One: Got lost in the mountains, was found while fighting a bear.\n\nInformation Two: Her favorite activity is spending winter under a blanket by the stove, drinking and eating oranges.\n\nInformation Three: Came to Dreams Consult to promote hometown culture because of losing a bet to a senior while drunk, but now enjoys being here."
},
	[47300]={ language="Real Name: Flonicle Latif\nIdentity: A member of Latif family from Uzyanta\nInterests: Collects various gems, enjoys afternoon tea"
},
	[47301]={ language="[Ice Agate? No thanks.]\n\n[Blazing Stones from a live volcano? No thanks.]\n\nFlonicle leaned back casually against the chair, and tossed the gemstone in her hand onto the long table in front of her. It landed in the pile of treasures with a crisp [ding] and slid onto the tabletop. The middle-aged man standing opposite took a breath, heart aching: [Miss Latif, these are rare gems—]\n\n[I want one-of-a-kind collections,] Flonicle interrupted impatiently.\n\nBehind her, Ciri timely handed a cup of perfectly warm red tea to Flonicle. She took a sip, and leisurely put down the cup, addressing the smiling boss beside her: [No need to bring out ordinary gems. I have plenty of these in my collection. Besides, if I'm only buying regular items, there's no need for me to come here.]\n\nThe boss smiled proudly: [If you want quality goods, I'm not bragging, but nowhere else in the Sacred Union meets your standards like my shop.] He paused, [But, though unique collections exist, what is it you're looking for this time, Miss?]\n\n[Demon's Eye.] Flonicle withdrew her smile, looking at the Boss. [Even the highest quality Stellar Crystal is just more vividly swirling with stars inside. But 'Demon's Eye,' supposedly, the path of spinning stars looks like an eye, appearing as if a demon is blinking between motion and stillness.] [I heard this treasure arrived last week, I hope I'm not too late?]\n\n[Well…] the boss blinked, [it's inconvenient timing, yesterday—]\n\n[Yesterday someone placed a deposit but hasn't picked it up, the 'Demon's Eye' is still here.]\n\nBoss: [Miss's information is timely, you must also know who placed the order.]\n\n[Not at all, I only need to verify its location.] Flonicle waved indifferently, [Name your price.]\n\n[It's not about the price, if it were another customer, I would repay ten or twenty times the deposit just to present it to Miss Latif. But… the identity of that customer is quite unusual, I really can't break my promise.]\n\n[If asked, just say Flonicle from the Latif family personally requested it.] Flonicle said impatiently.\n\n[I'm afraid not…]\n\n[You're afraid of offending that customer, but not of offending the Latif family?]\n\n[…]\n[Last year's museum missing centerpiece gem, I think it's currently with you, right?]\n\n[…]\n[If Santa City Lord knows their hefty purchase of black opal is fake, they might be quite angry.]\n\n[…]\n[And…] Diamond paused, looking towards the ever-attentive Ciri next to her, who continued: [If the batch of arms arriving at the border in three days were to disappear, wouldn't that cause trouble?]\n\n[… Ahem, you are very informed, I'm impressed. The Latif family has been collecting rare Stellar Crystals, and if that customer knows 'Demon's Eye' was taken by Miss Latif, I believe they'd understand.] The boss replied with a forced smile, [Please wait, I'll go fetch 'Demon's Eye.']\n\nFlonicle nodded and only after the boss left the room did she proudly look at Ciri: [How was it? I did well, didn't I?]\n\n[Miss Latif is getting more impressive.] Ciri patted Flonicle's head, smiling in praise.\n\n[I'm bringing'Demon's Eye' back this time, Dad will definitely be pleased~] Flonicle beamed with happiness."
},
	[47302]={ language="Information One: Don't talk about height issues in front of her, or the consequences will be very serious.\n\nInformation Two: She's the youngest child in the family and has been spoiled since childhood.\n\nInformation Three: She changes clothes at least three times a day, and each outfit is different."
},
	[47303]={ language="1. Starry Sky Umbrella: Designed personally by Diamond's mother, it was made through a special channel commissioned to Divinelight Heavy Tech.\n\n2. [Stellar Heart] Necklace: A gift from Diamond's grandparents at birth."
},
	[47304]={ language="Information One: She's very picky about flavors. Even with top-notch black tea, if it's not brewed in her usual way, she can taste the difference.\n\nInformation Two: She enjoys collecting various precious gems, especially those naturally perfect and uncut.\n\nInformation Three: She likes playing tricks on people but will apologize slightly if she goes too far."
},
	[47305]={ language="(Seems like a piece of paper torn from Ciri's notebook)\n\nSince I have matters to attend to with the lady tomorrow morning and cannot accompany the young miss, I'm asking you to care for her for half a day. Here's her schedule and notes for tomorrow. Thank you:\n\n6:00\n \nIron the morning clothes for the young miss\n(The style has been chosen, located in the second wardrobe, cabinet 5, second row, third piece, silk fabric, be cautious about the ironing temperature that it isn't too high).\n\n6:15\nCheck the young miss's breakfast preparation in kitchen number 3, and confirm the sugar content and lunch menu with the head chef. Recently, the young miss has been squinting a bit, and Dr. Edward recommends controlling sugar intake.\n\n6:30-7:30\nWake the young miss, help her dress, and have breakfast (if she resists getting up, play music through the speaker. If she throws a tantrum, give her the Little Demon Puppet by the bed to hold. If these measures don't work, you can get a snack from the lowest shelf of the storage cabinet in my room for her).\n\n7:45-8:30\nWhile the young miss is washing up, iron her going-out clothes and confirm that the driver, Elvin, has the car ready.\n Accompany the young miss to the Steve Group building, room 2104 [Brilliance] and arrive no later than 8:45.\n \nOn the way, review the meeting details with the young miss to ensure no information is missed. The meeting agenda has been emailed to you.\n\n9:00-11:30\nDuring the meeting, please pay close attention to the young miss's emotional state. If she has noticeable mood changes, signal her under the guise of refilling water.\n\n11:45\nContact driver Elvin to have lemon water and snacks ready in the car.\nContact the head chef to confirm lunch preparation.\n\n12:00-13:00\nAccompany the young miss home and prepare her naptime robe while she rests and dines.\nScent the young miss's bedroom.\n\nI will return by 12:30. Before that, if any issues arise, feel free to contact me."
},
	[47306]={ language="Information One: Very petty, but if you apologize to her, she gets flustered.\n\nInformation Two: Not good at dealing with familiar, enthusiastic people."
},
	[47307]={ language="Flonicle:\n\nMy dear daughter, how are you faring at Leistance Security Bureau headquarters? Even though you'll be back in Uzyanta in a few days, I wanted to write you this letter. Of course, I won't show it to you right away; I'll wait until you're older, maybe in three years or ten, before you see it.\n\nI'm in the garden now, with the sun warmly shining down, and it suddenly reminds me of when you were little.\n\nWhen you were born, you were as small as a kitten and always liked to hold my fingers with your little hands, as if you'd never grow up and would always depend on me. Then, in no time, you'd be running and jumping, sitting on your father's lap listening to him talk about work like a little adult.\n\nYour father praised your business talents and insisted on taking you to various business meetings. At first, I worried you were too young to sit still, but after a few years, you've managed to handle things on your own and assist your father with his work.\n\nI thought life would continue this way, with you gradually taking over more responsibilities. Busy, yes, but under your father and my sanctuary, nothing would go wrong. But then one day, you suddenly told me you wanted to see Leistance's collection of Stellar Crystals, and that's how you went to Leistance to discuss business for your father. I never imagined you'd tell us you wanted to become an Operator.\n\nI was both happy and worried when you passed Leistance's Operator assessment. The anchor events at Leistance are much more daunting than any battles your aunts have ever told you about. Will you get hurt, become accidentally contaminated, or...\n\nI don't dare to think about it. I considered stopping you from joining Leistance; you didn't need to grow up, just stay by our side, safe and sound.\n\nBut your father stopped me first.\n\n[Let her go; she has her own path to follow,] he said back then, trying to comfort me, though he seemed a bit troubled himself.\n\nI understand him. If he could, he would, like me, do everything to ensure nothing would happen to you. But after some things I'm not aware of, he had to agree... even helped facilitate your decision to join Leistance.\n\nAlthough your father and I are worried and anxious, as parents, the only thing we can do is fully support you since it seems unavoidable.\n\nSince you're determined to join Leistance, we'll provide you with an extra layer of protection. Xiri has been taking care of you since you were small, and her care for you is no less than mine. With her by your side, at least your father and I can be a bit more at ease.\n\nWell, I'll end it here. Remember to listen to Xiri, eat well, study well, and try not to get hurt.\n\nLove, Mom"
},
	[47308]={ language="Information One: Although she always acts like a boss towards Ciri, she's actually very dependent on Ciri.\n\nInformation Two: Afraid of thunder"
},
	[47309]={ language="Real Name: Nessila Austin\nIdentity: Selevie First Biological Research Institute External Personnel\nInterests: Sleeping, going out to play after waking up."
},
	[47310]={ language="On July 1st, ■■, my body is getting weaker, and today it's really hard even to sit up. Mom and dad seem to be arguing with the doctor. I saw mom crying... Am I going to die soon...\n\nOn July 6th, ■■, I'm feeling a bit better today. Mom did my hair in two big braids and told me a story about fireflies. She said that even though fireflies have a short life, it's amazing because they shine brightly in the dark, lighting up their little area. I've never seen a firefly, but I really want to see one for myself.\n\nOn July 10th, ■■, mom and dad told me today that I'm going to have surgery. I just need to sleep, and when I wake up, I'll be better and can leave this white room. But after mom said this, she hugged me tight, and I felt my shoulder getting wet from her tears. Is this surgery going to be really difficult?\n\nOn July 15th, ■■, the surgery is tomorrow. Today, dad brought me a bottle with several glowing bugs inside. Dad told me these are fireflies! They really glow! So beautiful! But they seem a bit unhappy staying in the bottle...\n\nOn July 27th, ■■, the first diary entry after the surgery! I slept for so many days! Just now mom and dad told me I'm already healed and can go home tomorrow! That's great! I want to write it down, but for some reason, I feel really sleepy...\n\nOn July 28th, ■■, I'm home! But it's completely different from when I left. I got a new room, and mom decorated it so nicely, with lots and lots of firefly patterns, which I really like.\n\nOn August 11th, ■■, today I went to the forest to see fireflies! They're so beautiful, really beautiful! The forest smells so fresh! We also took a family photo with the fireflies, but I don't know why, I suddenly felt really sleepy... and just fell asleep...\n\nOn August 28th, ■■, dad gave me a set of gear that can instantly locate where I am. And when I put it on, I can fly, just like a firefly. It's so fun, I really love it.\n\nOn September 10th, ■■, today mom introduced me to a big sister named Sophia, who will be with me wherever I go! She's really pretty, just a bit stern, but I think we can get along well!\n\nOn September 10th, ■■, tomorrow I'll be going on a trip with Sophia! I won't be writing in my diary anymore because I'm going to start writing travel notes, haha! (Big smiling face)"
},
	[47311]={ language="Information One: She feels scared in a white-painted empty room because she often stayed alone in empty hospital rooms as a child.\n\nInformation Two: Her parents strictly controlled Nessila's diet, prioritizing balanced nutrition in every meal, often over taste.\n\nInformation Three: Monthly HP check-ups are a routine, and any minor aches or pains make her parents worry for a long time."
},
	[47312]={ language="1. Fireflies: When young and sick, her parents used fireflies [able to shine and glow in a limited life] as an example to encourage Nessila to face everything with bravery, a lesson she's always remembered and loves these creatures even now.\n\n2. Customized Sleep Products: Sleep products, including pajamas with firefly patterns, firefly-style pillows, and eye masks with firefly designs.\n\n3. Camera: A gift from her father, hoping Nessila can capture beautiful moments during her travels."
},
	[47313]={ language="Information One: Drowsiness, she can fall asleep anytime and anywhere. This is a special aftereffect after becoming an AIMBS Operator.\n\nInformation Two: She loves to travel around because she spent her childhood in the hospital and never went out. After recovering, she often goes on trips.\n\nInformation Three: Her dream is to become an [adult] who faces everything with bravery and to travel around the world."
},
	[47314]={ language="Early yesterday morning, Sophia and I took a flight to Lissugen. We flew for quite a while, but I slept a lot on the plane, so I wasn't bored at all~\n\nWhen I woke up, we had already arrived in Lissugen. The city lit up with neon lights was really beautiful, and there was a huge Ferris wheel there. They say it's called Neoscope Park. I told Sophia that we definitely have to check it out.\n\nSo today, we went to Neoscope Park. It's so big here! I have never seen a theme park this big in Selevie!\n\nThere are so many fun places in Neoscope Park. Besides the Ferris wheel, there's a big circus, Starry Fantasy Land, a merry-go-round, etc. It's like a real dream garden with lots of cute fantasy fairies. They can really fly, just like me! :) There are also cards that look like people, and a magical mirror world where I almost got lost!\n\nOh, and the big circus is really amazing: there are animal training shows, magician performances, and acrobatics shows. My favorite was the animal training show, where the lion jumping through hoops was the best. A huge lion jumped through three hoops, that's incredible. After the show, Sophia and I even took a photo with that lion. I heard it's really hard to tame a lion.\n\nAfter the circus, we also enjoyed the merry-go-round and the Ferris wheel. Unfortunately, I fell asleep before the Ferris wheel reached its highest point... If I have the chance, I'll definitely come back to experience it again!\n\n—Nessila's Global Travel Journal, Part One"
},
	[47315]={ language="Information One: To fulfill Nessila's wish to travel the world, her parents specially hired a former AIMBS Operator to accompany and ensure her safety during her travels.\n\nInformation Two: Drinks a glass of high-calcium milk every day"
},
	[47316]={ language="[Nessila's Postcard Book]\n\nPage 1, Picture 2: With the gateway of the Neoscope Park as the background, the big ferris wheel stands out in the night sky.\nIt says: Dear Mom and Dad, thank you for letting me explore how beautiful the world outside is. We've arrived at the largest amusement park in Lissugen, and this postcard captures my longing and gratitude for you right at this moment. I truly hope we can come here together someday.\n—Love, your daughter, Nessila Austin\n\nPage 2, Picture 1: The background is the largest Technology company in southern Uzyanta, an impressive and lofty building.\nIt says: Dear Mom and Dad, we are now in the south of Uzyanta. The buildings here look so unique. Sophia says it's called [punk.] There's a technology company in the air here, but I can't remember its name.\nI hope you are happy and HPy while working hard at home as I explore outside.\n—Love, your daughter, Nessila Austin\n\nPage 3, Picture 1: With the iron city of Burksomi as the background, the enormous gears grab most of the attention.\nIt says: Dear Mom and Dad, Sophia and I have arrived in Burksomi, the iron city, with a huge gear that looks so spectacular, though I don't know what it's used for. I always heard Burksomi was cold, and now being here, I know it really is so cold! But don't worry, I'm dressed warmly, and Sophia is taking great care of me. You also need to take good care of yourselves.\n—Love, your daughter, Nessila Austin"
},
	[47317]={ language="Information One: Can't resist sweets, especially fancy cakes that look good.\n\nInformation Two: Naturally has a [lucky charm] effect; people who are with her tend to have good luck"
},
	[47318]={ language="Real Name: Anvenora Momir\nIdentity: Researcher at Leffel Life Science Research Institute\nInterests: Watching documentaries related to life, writing diaries, diving"
},
	[47319]={ language="Anvenora's thoughts on life stem from an accident.\n\nDue to her parents' research work, the aquarium where Anvenora's parents worked would occasionally take in injured marine animals for various reasons, and once they healed, they'd be released back into the sea.\n\nOnce, the aquarium took in a severely injured dolphin. From her parents, Anvenora learned that this dolphin was rescued from an amusement park that held animal shows. It had gone wild and hurt people, and the park staff injured it severely to subdue it, leaving it barely alive. Anvenora's parents rescued it and placed it in a large pool near the ocean.\n\n[It's hurt; it must be so scared.]\n\nEvery time she passed by, Anvenora saw the dolphin quietly resting at the pool's edge, just one wall away from the vast ocean, but its seriously injured tail could never again propel it out of the water.\n\nLater, Anvenora managed to convince her parents to let her feed the dolphin daily. While adults fed and treated its wounds, Anvenora kept company nearby; the dolphin didn't fuss or struggle.\n\nAnvenora felt that these animals were quite intelligent, knowing who's good or bad. Marine life is just like humans; there's a lot about them we don't know.\n\n…That dolphin still looked at the ocean through the glass.\n\nAnvenora believed animals could express emotions through their eyes. She felt the dolphin's gaze towards the sea was filled with anxiety and longing, never having seen the vast world it should have belonged to, born in the amusement park.\n\nDriven by an impulse, Anvenora made a decision.\n\nShe quietly set the dolphin free.\n\nShe could never forget the dolphin's free movements and calls as it swam towards the sea.\n\nOf course, releasing the dolphin couldn't be hidden from her parents; they didn't blame Anvenora for her reckless behavior, but... not long after, the dolphin's body was found at Dolphin Bay.\n\nIt exchanged its life for a brief moment of freedom.\n\nAnvenora fell into a deep self-reproach for a long time, believing it was all her fault; if she hadn't released the dolphin, it wouldn't have died.\n\n[Releasing it simply because you think it's well before it's healed—how is that not an arrogance towards other lives?[ The voice inside her reminded.\n\nThis incident felt like a thorn deeply embedded in young Anvenora's heart. Later, whenever she saw someone harming animals or trampling life, she would do everything she could to stop it. Besides her own work, she also engaged in environmental and animal protection efforts. She wasn't good at communicating with people, but she would actively participate in anything related to life.\n\nExploring the origin of life, its meaning, and respecting each life equally became her lifelong goals."
},
	[47320]={ language="Information One: Brings back dead marine creatures found while diving, tries to make them into specimens, but isn't good at it. The specimens at home are actually all bought.\n\nInformation Two: Besides diving, has a particular fondness for beachcombing but often gets pinched by crabs on the beach.\n\nInformation Three: The only time she got 'lucky' was in middle school when a super typhoon hit on a day shey didn't want to go to school"
},
	[47321]={ language="1. Diving Equipment: Improved diving gear allows for longer underwater work.\n\n2. Marine Creature Handbook: An encyclopedia with a vast record of marine life.\n\n3. Portable Waterproof Camera: A multifunctional camera that can shoot and record in abyssal sea.\n\n4. Anvenora carries it around, it's Crystal Jellyfish Jelly's snack.\n\n5. Biological Specimen: Rare marine life specimen obtained from a fellow marine life enthusiast.\n\n6. Coral Hair Accessory: A souvenir from Dolphin Bay tourism"
},
	[47322]={ language="Information One: Likes marine life, but also likes eating them.\n\nInformation Two: Enjoys going to the aquarium, can stare at the same fish all afternoon.\n\nInformation Three: Was once suspected by people around her, wondering if she could really understand what marine life was saying."
},
	[47323]={ language="Abyssal Crystal Beast: Biological Feature and Remodel of Abyssal Crystal Beast Dominated by Crystal Jellyfish\nReport Version: NO.053\nReport Date: July 4th, XXXX\nSample Analysis Time:\nStart Date: May 15th, XXXX\nEnd Date: April 18th, XXXX\nSample Analysis Unit: Leffel Life Science Research Institute\nApplicant: Anvenora Momir\n\nI. Experiment Purpose\n1. Preliminary understanding of the biological Feature and species ecology of Abyssal Crystal Beasts dominated by Crystal Jellyfish\n2. Confirm the feasibility of Abyssal Crystal Beast Remodel\n\nII. Experiment Principle\nAbyssal Crystal Jellyfish mainly live in temperate warm sea regions with no fixed depth distribution. For the experimental subject, they can adapt from the continental shelf at a depth of about 300 meters to Abyssal water pressure over 1000 meters. These creatures mainly feed on plankton, and possibly on Crystal as well, primarily observed through free-range observation in the experiment.\n\nInvestigation found a determining factor in the sample individual memory that resembles the new gene coding SH56, which is similar to gene SH54 (Note: SH54 gene was first discovered in XXXX, only terrestrial Remodel Crystal Beasts carry it, and it deterores adaptability in various environments for Crystal Beasts). The appearance of similar gene coding in Abyssal creatures is unprecedented.\n\nTo confirm if SH56 gene and SH54 gene have similarity and conversion possibility, in this experiment, devices simulate different environments to test if Crystal Jellyfish can adapt to water quality and pressure different from their habitat. Using gene analogy rebuilding system, the feasibility of recreating SH56 gene as a sample example, and whether conversion can enable Abyssal Crystal Beasts to adapt to land.\n\nIII. Experiment Process (See attachments)\n1. Encode the genetic code of sample individuals\n2. Confirm the environment that experimental individuals can directly adapt to based on genetic coding\n3. Confirm the adaptation limits of individuals in the actual experiment\n4. Rearrange genetic structure data and test feasibility using crystal technology\n\nIV. Experiment Results\n1. Through long-term observation, experimental individuals show universal biological behavior, with a tendency to feed on pollutants\n2. Confirm the feasibility of re-encoding Remodel for SH56 gene and its adaptation characteristics, Feature can act on other organisms\n3. Confirm the possibility of Crystal Beast Remodel\n\n(Note: Remodel surgery has received consent from Jelly, if surgery is feasible, under certain insurance mechanisms, other Abyssal Crystal Beasts can also be utilized by humans. We strive for methods to coexist peacefully with these creatures as the purpose of exploring the ocean has never been to indiscriminately slaughter other life due to our fear and the unknown.)"
},
	[47324]={ language="Information One: Every time she visits a new coastal area, she makes sure to buy all the local souvenirs related to marine animals.\n\nInformation Two: When there are unfamiliar people around, she keeps talking to Jelly to ease her anxiety."
},
	[47325]={ language="Excerpt from [The Depth of Life]—Leffel Life Science Research Institute Press, by Anvenora Momir\n\n...\nI first discovered the whale in XXXX, in a sea area called the Fallen Whale Sea.\n\nWhale fall in the deep sea, when a whale falls, it gives life for many. It's named so because many whales die in this ocean area, making it a beautiful yet sad name.\n\nAt that time, I had just finished a routine dive to survey the ecosystem and was about to return to the boat when I saw the whale.\n\nIt was very close to me. I didn't know why it appeared here, but it wasn't a good sign. It might be dying or seeking help.\n\nAnimals have their own language, and ocean creatures are no different. In the pitch-black ocean, sound waves inaudible to humans became their most convenient means of communication. Through interpreting these sound waves, I heard its call at that moment, seeking help from me.\n\nThis is what my partner Jelly told me.\n\nJelly is an Abyssal Crystal Beast jellyfish I met on my first dive into the Abyssal. It has the ability to communicate with humans. After research, we discovered that she can also communicate with other marine animals. This was a very important discovery, proving that we might one day master methods to converse with the ocean.\n\nNow through research on Abyssal Crystal Beasts, we can also engage in simple communication with higher marine mammals. This is one reason why the Leffel Life Science Research Institute insists on developing research and peaceful coexistence with the Abyssal Anima Crystal beasts.\n\nThe whale told me it had lost its way.\n\nIt accidentally arrived in this sea area and couldn't find a way to leave.\n\nInitially, I was puzzled too. We know that in the ocean, where the eye can't distinguish direction, creatures rely on instinct to navigate—currents, echoes, and water temperatures influence them for many reasons. I couldn't determine the cause. If examined, this area where many whales die is indeed suspicious.\n\nI led it out of this sea area and applied to the academy for an investigation. Our findings showed that humans had once dumped pollutants in this area, causing whales to lose their direction. Once they entered, they couldn't leave and would eventually exhaust themselves to death, becoming skeletal remains on the seabed, upon which new life emerges.\n\nAfterward, we spent some time clearing those pollutants, and no more whales got lost in that area.\n\n...\nLater, during my dives, I occasionally saw that whale. It's doing well now and has its own calf. We sometimes communicate through Jelly's translation, like old friends. Even now, I return to that sea area in that season to meet it.\n\nThey, like us humans, are residents of Teno, living under the same starry sky. Perhaps one day it will eventually become a whale fall, but life is a cycle, and death is a new beginning. Before reaching the life-ending abyss, there's much we can do.\n\nRevering life is also a reminder to ourselves."
},
	[47326]={ language="Information One: Not truly indifferent, just feels that showing indifference can avoid a lot of unnecessary communication. Actually, she has deep social anxiety.\n\nInformation Two: Very afraid of underwater tall seaweed forests, specific reason unknown."
},
	[47327]={ language="Name: Alicia Klein\nRole: Leistance Headquarters Special Operator\nInterests: Decorats her donkey puppet"
},
	[47328]={ language="Alicia is an orphan, and that's something everyone knows at the Leistance Security Bureau headquarters.\n\nAccording to public records, Alicia's parents worked at Leistance and tragically died during a mission. Beyond that, details about Alicia's identity are vague.\n\nFor the reason of [caring for members' orphans,] Alicia has lived at Leistance Security Bureau headquarters since childhood. Director Harper took on the responsibility of being her guardian and taught her Leistance's core beliefs and duties—they are the last sword and shield of humanity, a last bastion in times of crisis.\n\nWith this influence, Alicia's worldview was completely shaped in the Leistance way. She showed incredible talent in the AIMBS Operator training and exams, passing all assessments with perfect scores, becoming an AIMBS Operator.\n\nBefore and after that, Alicia continued striving diligently, hoping to become a qualified field Operator and join others in leaving the headquarters to carry out missions worldwide."
},
	[47329]={ language="Information One: Has no concept of money and often pays multiple times more than necessary for things she wants.\n\nInformation Two: Holds a black card from her father, rumored to have a nine-figure limit—but that's just a rumor.\n\nInformation Three: She's the main person involved in the legendary story of someone spending a seven-figure sum in an online auction to buy a limited edition [Little Donkey Family] puppet."
},
	[47330]={ language="1. Sword Case: A transformable sword case officially called [Type 30 Prototype Transforming Weapon,] but Alicia prefers to call it [Box.] \n\n2. Twin Swords: Customized weapons, called [One] and [Two] by Alicia, which actually sound quite ordinary...\n\n3. Donkey Puppet: The puppet of the main character Danchey from the timeless stop-motion animation [Little Donkey Family,] which has accompanied Alicia for at least ten years.\n\n4. Photo Album: A gift from Alicia's father Harper, containing group photos of Alicia at the Leistance headquarters."
},
	[47331]={ language="Information One: Really enjoys looking at illustrated guides and encyclopedias, but not good at remembering the content.\n\nInformation Two: Sensitive to heat, can't eat very hot food.\n\nInformation Three: Once secretly tried being an online broadcaster, but the platform shut down a week after starting."
},
	[47332]={ language="Alicia doesn't remember the exact time she became an AIMBS Operator. What remains in her memory are the day-to-day tutorials and the empty multimedia classroom. In the multimedia classroom, she can learn the same courses as peers in fortress cities. The only difference is—she has no classmates and the teaching is done by knowledgeable yet cold AI.\n\nAlthough she lacks peers in the traditional sense, this isn't an issue for Alicia—the Members of Leistance come from all over Taino Star. They gather together to work toward common goals. During her tedious tutorials, Alicia listens to their stories, learns about events and traditions from around the world, and this becomes one of her favorite pastimes over the past ten years.\n\nAt some point, Alicia became obsessed with stop-motion animation [Little Donkey Family,] and begged [Father] Harper for the complete set of related merchandise, often holding the donkey plushies made based on the animation.\n\nThis isn't something unusual for a young girl, but it did raise some objections within Leistance. For unknown reasons, every action of Alicia is recorded and evaluated by her guardian Harper. Alicia's dependence on a particular thing might have been noteworthy, but Harper unusually did not comment, intervene, or even refused to add monitoring devices in the donkey plushies.\n\nAnd so, the donkey puppet Danchey accompanied Alicia for ten years."
},
	[47333]={ language="Information One: Has a dependency on puppets, must sleep hugging her donkey doll after returning to their room.\n\nInformation Two: Works very hard on things they are committed to, is genuinely a hardworking person."
},
	[47334]={ language="Not sure if it's intentional or accidental, Alicia has no concept of money and often spends several times the price for things she wants.\n\nOnce, at an online auction, she saw a limited edition [Little Donkey Family] plush and decided to buy it. But as she began bidding, a rival appeared.\n\nThis competitor, with an ID consisting only of numbers, kept bidding against Alicia, each time higher.\n\nAlicia was unwilling to back down, and felt she couldn't lose here due to her upbringing. So she increased her bid, and the competitor followed suit—the auction turned into a solo duel. They kept challenging each other's limits, and the bids climbed from four digits to six.\n\nAs time passed, the competitor raised the bid to 700,000, an astonishing price for a puppet.\n\nWithout waiting for the auctioneer's countdown, Alicia entered her next bid—the screen displayed a seven-figure sum. The room fell silent, as if time had stopped.\n\nThe auctioneer began the countdown, and Alicia's opponent chose to withdraw from the auction.\n\nTwo days later, Alicia received her item, and her [father] Harper just smiled faintly upon hearing the news."
},
	[47335]={ language="Information One: Has a secret notebook of their own. When feeling down, she jots things down furiously, but nobody knows what she writes.\n\nInformation Two: In certain situations, she clearly shows a dislike for having [things that belong to her taken away by others]."
},
	[47336]={ language="Real Name: Kymia ·Albert\nIdentity: Outsourced personnel from Lawton Institute of Bionic Mechanics.\nInterests: Writing diaries, understanding knowledge related to emotions, like through observing humans, reading books, watching movies, etc."
},
	[47337]={ language="[Notes of Project Angel Developer (Final)]\n\nIt's been 72 hours since Michael suffered severe damage and entered shutdown mode.\nAll 26 rescue plans proposed by the R&D and Healer teams have been executed and failed.\nWe don't have much time left. If we can't restart Michael before midnight, she'll be scrapped.\nMichael is a great product we spent over a decade developing, and no one wants to see her end this way. We have four hours left to figure it out.\n\n...\n\nWe failed, and the entire experiment team will immediately start developing the second-generation humanoid angel.\nThe scrapping program for Michael is set for: June 29th at 3 AM, ■■.\nThe moment the scrapping time was announced, the lab fell silent. Everyone was helpless but powerless.\nAllow me to record this for a permanent memory of Michael.\nGoodbye, our first humanoid angel—Michael.\n\nProject Angel Research Specialist No. 424B\nJune 28th, ■■ "
},
	[47338]={ language="Information One: Has a habit of keeping a diary and making records.\n\nInformation Two: Enjoys reading in free time and scribbles dense notes in the blank spaces of books.\n\nInformation Three: Dislikes masks or anything that covers the face, feeling it hinders the observation of human expressions."
},
	[47339]={ language="1. Diary: Kymia's diary, with a yellow and white striped cover, matches her perfectly.\n\n2. [Theory of Human Emotion]: A book that records human cognition, emotion, and social behavior, Kymia usually uses it to learn about human emotions.\n\n3. Fountain Pen: A gift from Leon Albert, he hopes Kymia will record interesting things with her hands like humans do.\n\n4. A Photo: A picture of Kymia and Leon Albert, where she has silver hair and is wearing casual clothes, with half her head resting on her father's shoulder, seemingly making an expression known as a [smile.]"
},
	[47340]={ language="Information One: Although she seems cold, she's a Miss Curious, always asking questions.\n\nInformation Two: Her brain is implanted with a complete intelligent combat system that lets her predict others' next moves during a fight.\n\nInformation Three: It's said her eyes were once both red, but during repairs, her left eye was changed to blue for some reason."
},
	[47341]={ language="■■■■ Maintenance command recorded\nStarting damage inspection>>>>>>>590 locations\nSystem repairable locations>>>>>>>148 locations\nInitiating system self-check program>>>>>>>>Completed system self-maintenance on 148 locations\nRepair time: 22:23:48\nRepair progress: 100%\nSystem evaluation indicates remaining ■■ locations require manual repair.\n△ Warning: The biological functions of this unit have reached their limits, please replace soon.\n\nAs the leading development engineer and deputy director at Leyton Bionic Machinery Institute, Leon Albert stared at the first-generation humanoid angel—Michael, now just a head and a damaged upper body—and fell into deep thought.\n\nBy chance, he acquired this [treasure] a year ago, and when he first laid eyes on her, he knew—if he could successfully repair this legendary humanoid angel, the achievement would earn him a place in history.\n\nWho would have thought that ten years would pass—\n\nAs of today, Leon has completed all repairs and prepared a brand-new body for Michael—only one final challenge remains—to awaken Michael's brain.\n\nFor the past ten years, Michael's brain has been in statis, rejecting external electromagnetic signals. To activate it, special measures were necessary—after some hesitation, Leon decided to inject D-Blood into Michael's brain.\n\nAfter a series of frantic surgeries...\n\n■■■ Functional check completed, commencing Model installation program.\n>>>>>>Communication Model installation<<<<<<\n>>>>>>Power enhancement Model unlocking<<<<<<\n>>>>>>Perception Model activation<<<<<<\n>>>>>>Granting analysis circuit access<<<<<<\nCalibrating visual Model >>>>>>>93.98%\n\nFamiliar yet unfamiliar concepts flooded the brain accompanied by a mechanical female voice—Hello, Kymia."
},
	[47342]={ language="Information One: Every once in a while, the mechanical parts on her body need maintenance.\n\nInformation Two: It is said that Kymia's eyes hold her past memories, but she herself seems unaware of this."
},
	[47343]={ language="According to the official statement, Kymia is a [cyborg] developed over decades by Leon, the deputy director of the Leiden Institute of Bionic Mechanics. At Leistance Security Bureau, where she has long served, she holds a particularly unique status.\n\nYou could call her human, but she has a mechanical body; claim she's not human, yet she possesses a human brain and heart.\n\nWhen she first arrived at Leistance, Kymia avoided all communication with others, usually staying in her room and only emerging when on missions.\n\nInitially, the staff at Leistance perceived her with fear; Kymia exuded an aura that they felt was like killing intent. To the average person, Kymia seemed like a heartless executioner.\n\nHowever, later tests revealed that Kymia suffered from memory loss and lacked human emotions—the emotional model installed in her couldn't function properly.\n\nBecause of these factors, Kymia refused to communicate with others, afraid of unintentionally harming someone through interaction.\n\nBut this doesn't mean Kymia doesn't care about others. In fact, she's very attentive, listening carefully to everyone's conversations and preferences, recording everything meticulously.\n\nWhen Kymia is alone in her room, she's also reading and studying various books and films about emotions.\n\n[I speculate that Kymia's lack of emotions and inability to understand others' feelings might be some form of 'aftereffect.' Even after multiple tests, the exact situation is unclear. But I think the cause isn't important; what matters is that she deeply desires to make friends, understand everyone's emotions, and communicate like a normal person.\n\n\nI believe that if everyone knew the truth, they would understand her. At least I can, and most of the time, our interactions are very harmonious now.]\n\n— Leistance Security Bureau Healer Testing Administrator Y.C"
},
	[47344]={ language="Information One: Not just longswords, Kymia can skillfully use various cold weapons existing in the world.\n\nInformation Two: Likes watching movies, especially those with themes about robots and humans."
},
	[47345]={ language="Real Name:Cylterrin Eugene\nIdentity: Mercenary of Burn Bear, Medical Doctor\nInterests: Medical research"
},
	[47346]={ language="Miss Cylterrin is sick.\n\nThis isn't an insult, but a statement of fact.\n\nUnlike most Operators, Miss Cylterrin's process of becoming an AIMBS Operator was highly irregular, leaving significant aftermath—a mental illness that science currently cannot understand or cure.\n\nIt doesn't sound terrifying, as if it's just an ordinary psychological problem, but what if this psychological problem can affect reality?\n\nPeople's inner thoughts are complex, filled with countless ideas at all times, good thoughts, bad thoughts, complex thoughts, terrifying thoughts...\n\nWhile people can't control their thoughts, they can constrain what their true thoughts are. But if there is a force that makes it impossible to distinguish one's true thoughts, causing them to realize all ideas... that would be an unimaginable nightmare.\n\nThis is Miss Cylterrin's taboo. Every 21-day and night cycle, her thoughts lose control, and so does her power.\n\nEveryone familiar with Cylterrin knows that it's best to let her stay alone at this time. You should absolutely not appear in front of her, no matter how brave you are; on this day, you will try everything to stay as far away from her as possible..."
},
	[47347]={ language="Information One: The Crystal Weapon used is an injection gun, loaded with dozens of special potions she concocted.\n\nInformation Two: After becoming an Operator, she apparently gained legendary telekinesis.\n\nInformation Three: She likes drinking soup so thick it could be called mush."
},
	[47348]={ language="1. Dr. Marceau's Photo: A cherished photo by Cylterrin, featuring a woman in a white robe with a warm smile on her face.\n\n2. Homemade Medicine Bottle: A bottle of medicine without a clear label, only Cylterrin knows what's inside.\n\n3. Something like Cigarettes: Looks like cigarettes, but is actually a pain-relief and calming medication frequently used by Cylterrin."
},
	[47349]={ language="Information One: Cylterrin can use some special techniques to precisely control her muscles, but this control can't last too long.\n\nInformation Two: Hates meditation, but must rely on it to prevent herself from losing control.\n\nInformation Three: Has placed a lot of soundproof padding in her room to block out the terrifying noises she makes when she loses control."
},
	[47350]={ language="When someone grows from naive to mature, it's either through enough time to settle or through harsh experiences that come at a cost.\n\nCylterrin is the latter.\n\nA few years before joining Burn Bear, she was a naive young girl. Driven by her beautiful vision, she chose to walk alone in Uzyanta's Wilderness, offering free Healer aid to the locals as a physician.\n\nHowever, Cylterrin learned enough knowledge from her foster mother but failed to learn the necessary caution and suspicion towards the world. Her sincere good deeds did not bring gentle returns; instead, misfortune and malice came looking for her.\n\nWhat exactly happened during that time remains Cylterrin's eternal secret. When her foster mother, Dr. Marceau, found her again, Cylterrin had become an Operator with near uncontrollable power through unofficial means.\n\nThe young physician treating patients in Uzyanta disappeared. A year later, during a mission in Uzyanta, Burn Bear encountered a girl on the battlefield with a strange smile.\n\nShe called herself [Streyne].\n\nA deadly poison."
},
	[47351]={ language="Information One: Seventy percent of her income is sent to Dr.Marceau.\n\nInformation Two: highly cherishes Dr. Marceau's photos and believe she's not worthy of returning to Dr. Marceau's side."
},
	[47352]={ language="Although Burn Bear was accepted by Uzyanta at Cylterrin, she's not originally from Uzyanta herself.\n\nUnlike most in Burn Bear who have their own secrets, she's not shy about her origins.\n\nAccording to Cylterrin, she was born in Selevie, where nature and technology often clash. Though orphaned with no parents, she was fortunately adopted and raised by Marceau, a genetics PhD, enjoying a fairly happy childhood.\n\nSadly, those good times are gone; now she lacks the qualifications to stand beside Dr. Marceau, and can only wander alone to forge her own path.\n\nWhen Burn Bear asked her reason, Cylterrin responded, [Someone like me who frequently gets sick and causes harm, and can kill without guilt, shouldn't be standing in the spotlight. Better to find some place to lay low than bring trouble to others.]\n\nAs Burn Bear's [specialist doctor,] Cylterrin can be considered diligent—the daily work of a mercenary group is fraught with danger, so injury and pain are common. The medicine Cylterrin concocts easily heals anything from bruises and burns to Frozen. However, her treatments aren't entirely free—often mercenary Members must agree to help Cylterrin with some [harmless] experiments, leading to the consumption of dubious potions with unknown effects..."
},
	[47353]={ language="Information One: Cylterrin's most frequently used venom is a neurotoxin.\n\nInformation Two: Cylterrin's [treatment] works at the genetic level, which also means... she can heal you, but also... deal with you."
},
	[47354]={ language="Real Name: Rotta\nIdentity: Leistance Lissugen Branch Information Technology Professional\nInterests: Stargazing, chess online"
},
	[47355]={ language="Rotta was born into an ordinary family in Lissugen, with both parents being regular employees, but she was anything but ordinary. While a typical child starts speaking around the age of one, Rotta was nearly three years old and hadn't yet spoken. Worried about her HP, her parents took her to see a doctor.\n\nTo their surprise, the test results showed Rotta had an IQ close to 220. After checking records, the doctor mentioned that a person with such high intelligence is extremely rare in history, appearing only once in millions.\n\nThe doctor suspected that Rotta's high intelligence was related to her not speaking, as all other physical indicators were normal. So the parents were advised to take her home and educate her well.\n\nLeft with no choice, Rotta's parents brought her home and cared for her, allowing her to grow at her own pace.\n\nFortunately, it wasn't long before Rotta started speaking and could communicate normally with her parents. They were thrilled and, upon confirming Rotta was [all normal,] began planning her future.\n\nUnder her parents' arrangement, Rotta joined an early education class. She learned quickly but was very reclusive, never speaking to anyone other than her parents, including the children and teachers at her class. The kids didn't want to play with her, thinking of Rotta as a weirdo.\n\nAfter finding no joy in the early education class, Rotta no longer wanted to attend school and instead preferred to stay at home reading books. After consulting with her teachers about Rotta's situation, her parents decided to withdraw her from school."
},
	[47356]={ language="Information One: Really hates dry weather because it causes a lot of static in her hair, making it messy.\n\nInformation Two: Sneers at things related to divination, religion, and metaphysics, but every bad prediction she's received always comes true.\n\nInformation Three: Can access the secret files of every Leistance member if she wants to, but of course, good kids wouldn't do that."
},
	[47357]={ language="1. Charging Backpack: In addition to work essentials, it also contains a large bottle of milk and several picture books about stars.\n\n2. Star Stone Collection Manual: Collected many meteorite fragments gathered before the Skyborne Barriers launched; they emit beautiful light in the dark.\n\n3. Limited Edition Thermos from the Stargazing Association: Although Deling isn't very interested in stargazing, the gift thermos from the Stargazing Association is surprisingly attractive, so managed to get one."
},
	[47358]={ language="Information One: Trying hard to drink milk to grow taller.\n\nInformation Two: Recently started following a certain Operator's advice to increase sleep time and used AI to plan a complete sleep strategy.\n\nInformation Three: Usually works in calling AI to integrate planning information, but recently, many people asked Rotta to use AI for advice on their life troubles, especially love, which is a bit troubling for her."
},
	[47359]={ language="After returning from preschool, Rotta's parents once again faced a dilemma with their daughter. They even started to wonder if she had mild autism.\n\nThe parents took her to see a doctor again, but the doctor gave a negative answer—Rotta is too smart, so smart that she is not interested in things that aren't intelligent. She needs an environment and things that match her intelligence.\n\nThis left Rotta's parents worried again—they are just ordinary people. How could they create such a high-intellect environment for their daughter?\n\nAt this moment, Rotta showed her understanding side. She comforted her mom and dad and suggested that all she needed was a computer.\n\nRealizing this could be the easiest thing for them to do, her parents agreed without hesitation. In the following years, Rotta spent most of her time alone with the computer, and nobody knew what she was doing online.\n\nUntil one day, a group of people broke into Rotta's home to arrest her entire family."
},
	[47360]={ language="Information One: Once anonymously played against Newcastle online for a week straight and was recognized by Newcastle as a mysterious rival.\n\nInformation Two: Due to disagreements over star beliefs, didn't initially get along with , but after Adenie made Vilatria snacks that Deling liked, they became friends."
},
	[47361]={ language="Why did these people arrest Rotta and her family, and who are they?\n\nIt turns out over the years, Rotta has been investigating the [real night sky]—she's been fascinated by stars since childhood. After learning online that all the stars currently seen are fake, she began searching for what the real night sky looks like.\n\nUsing her genius abilities, Rotta explored every corner of the internet and eventually found Star Council's backend, successfully hacking into it.\n\nRotta discovered many real stars in the Star Council's backend network, but her actions were also noticed, and they came to find her.\n\nFacing the people from the Star Council, Rotta confessed everything, admitting she only wanted to find information about the [real night sky.] She also presented her records of star-related knowledge.\n\nThe Star Council was perplexed by Rotta's honesty. After consideration, they sent her to the Leistance Security Bureau branch in Lissugen for investigation.\n\n\nIsis, the head of the Lissugen branch, was unusually interested in this young [offender.] She personally participated in the questioning but did nothing—she simply played a game of chess with Rotta.\n\nEveryone next to the interrogation room witnessed Rotta checkmate Isis in just eight moves, prompting Isis to make a decision—to invite Rotta to join Leistance. How could they let a super genius capable of hacking into Star Council slip away easily?\n\n\nAfter exchanging information about the [real night sky,] Rotta accepted Leistance's invitation.\n\nBecoming an AIMBS Operator and gaining the codename [Deling] is another story altogether..."
},
	[47362]={ language="Information One: Surprisingly strong controlling desire, but she doesn't realize it due to her young age.\n\nInformation Two: Many people privately suspect that the sharp-tongued sarcasm behind Deling's [little thing] is largely Deling's true feelings."
},
	[47363]={ language="Real Name: Yuanya \nIdentity: Operator under Lissugen Branch of Leistance Security Bureau\nInterests: Eating and drinking, enjoys anything edible or drinkable"
},
	[47364]={ language="Why does Yuanya like little bunnies? Most people wouldn't ask such questions. Just like no one asks Koraz why she likes cats.\n\nAfter all, it's natural for a girl her age to like cute creatures like this.\n\nBut if you really ask Yuanya, she can give her own reason.\n\n[When I first started learning to sleep alone, my mom told me that if I really, really missed her and couldn't sleep, I should hold tight to this little bunny puppet. Since the puppet carries my mom's love and longing, hugging the bunny is like hugging mom.]\n\n[Later, it's not just that mom couldn't keep me company at night anymore. Mom went far away, and the time I needed to look at the bunny to miss mom became longer and longer. Even though I'm bravery enough to face the night without relying on the puppet, separation is still really tough.]\n\n[And besides, bunnies are not just cute on the outside and useless! Even though bunnies eat grass, they bite hard, and it hurts. It's like my mom who gently loves me but can protect me and Koraz like a superhero. I want to become such a superhero too.]\n\n[So, I like bunnies the most.]"
},
	[47365]={ language="Information One: Small stature, but can really eat—a lot, as she claims using Crystal Weapon requires intense mental power, and she needs lots of sugar to replenish.\n\nInformation Two: Lissugen branch acknowledges her as the encyclopedia of snacks.\n\nInformation Three: If you need Yuanya to do something, it's best to prepare plenty of food to bribe her."
},
	[47366]={ language="1. Bunny Ears: Actually a signal jammer with positioning function, but Yuanya rarely uses it for operation, instead only for communication and listening to music.\n\n2. Glasses: Actually Yuanya isn't nearsighted. The main function of these glasses is to prevent radiation, and she wears them mostly because they were left by her mom.\n\n3. [Special Mobile Chair MK46]: Yuanya's Crystal equipment, shaped like a gaming chair, made by her mom before she left. However, Yuanya later improved it herself. Due to her young age, Isis and Julia had experts test and check to ensure her improvements wouldn't harm herself before allowing Yuanya to use it."
},
	[47367]={ language="Information One: Even though often playing around with Koraz, whoever messes with Yuanya will likely get smacked by Koraz's paw first thing.\n\nInformation Two: A true genius, with intelligence far beyond their apparent age, inherited their mother's talent for research, and is a top-notch technician in the security bureau.\n\nInformation Three: Always drinks bubble tea with full sugar, and secretly adds more sugar. People accidentally drinking her beverage often find their minds blank."
},
	[47368]={ language="If you don't have at least three packs of snacks ready, there's no way to coax Yuanya into working well, even though technically, it's her job. When she's in a good mood, she might even ask for more. After all, how can you talk about contract spirit with a kid?\n\nEating without working might be criticized as [lazy] in many places, but no one at Leistance Security Bureau would ever accuse Yuanya of that. Especially, don't let Koraz hear you say it or you'll get a painful smack from her moew hammer! You wouldn't believe how many apology letters she's written for fighting to defend Yuanya... Growing up together sure makes a difference. They aren't biological sisters, but their bond is so strong.\n\nCome to think of it, just a few bags of chips can have her hack into any backend terminal you want, you can't even call that a good deal anymore!\n\nLuckily, Yuanya's mom had the foresight to send her to the agency. Otherwise, what if bad people tricked her away?\n\nPlus, she's just a kid, and kids need to grow properly!\n\nIf Yuanya worked diligently and nonstop, someone might complain to the Star Council about Leistance employing minors.\n\nIn short, we're all happy to stock up a few boxes of snacks in the office. Sometimes we even compete to see whose snacks Yuanya likes best. Her opinions in this area are quite valuable!\n\n—A staff member from the HR department at Leistance Security Bureau Lissugen Branch who wishes to remain anonymous."
},
	[47369]={ language="Information One: Really loves bunnies, almost everything around has bunny elements.\n\nInformation Two: To prevent her from getting cavities, her teammates have made a great effort."
},
	[47370]={ language="When she was little, Yuanya only knew that her mom was gone. As she grew older, she started to wonder about other things.\n\nWhere did mom go? How long would she be away?\n\nYuanya found her mom's obituary in an old newspaper, describing her as a core technology Professional at Skyborne Barriers, along with a report of a disastrous laboratory accident. Koraz's parents died in that accident. But all this happened before Yuanya was born. Meaning, for some secretive reason, her mom chose to give up her promising scientist career, faking her death, and then leaving with Yuanya and Koraz, disappearing from the public eye forever.\n\nShe knew that mom first contacted Director Isis because of Koraz's illness. That was the first time in Yuanya's young life when she understood what a [life-or-death moment] meant. Even now, Yuanya can't clearly say what sickness Koraz had; she only remembers that at the time, no one could assure her that Koraz would definitely get better.\n\nUntil Isis, as an old friend, provided them with a reliable treatment plan.\n\nLuckily, maybe fate always intended for them to be a family. Yuanya's bone marrow matched Koraz's, and she could save Koraz's life. After she took that brave step and underwent the surgery, they could even be called true blood relatives.\n\nHowever, she was lucky not to face death's farewell with Koraz but had to confront a life separation with her mom.\n\nLooking back, because of that secret, mom might still fear that her survival would be discovered by malicious people and used against her. To protect them, she had to entrust Yuanya and Koraz to Isis and leave first.\n\nThe first time they went to the Lissugen branch, they called Isis [Aunt Isis.] Of course, now that they've both become AIMBS Operators, they should call her the officer.\n\nTime has flown by so quickly, and they've both grown into Operators capable of handling things on their own. What about mom? Is she doing well?\n\nIf only mom could come back sooner... that would be great."
},
	[47371]={ language="Information One: If she can lie down, she definitely won't sit; if she can sit, she definitely won't stand. If she can snack, she definitely won't work.\n\nInformation Two: Though usually not obvious, actually very dependent on Koraz and really misses mom. Occasionally, when alone, a sad expression may appear on her face."
},
	[47372]={ language="Real Name: Andanna Hallowin\nIdentity: Researcher at Selevie Lab 05 [Incubator]\nInterests: Cultivating various plants, earning course credits"
},
	[47373]={ language="[Breeding Log of 'Incubator' Central University Natural Plant Department A3 Laboratory] (Andanna's Personal Compilation)\nOverview of Plant Numbers and Status\nDate: April 13, XXXX\n[A3-06]\n(Little Sprout) Today's Status: Good\nPerformance: Leaves are slightly yellow, preliminarily considered as nutrient excess\nCountermeasure: Reduce supply of meat-based food\n(Note: No injuries occurred today)\n...\n[A3-08]\n(Bubble) Today's Status: Poor\nPerformance: Roots are somewhat shriveled, lacking water, fruit tastes sour\nCountermeasure: Increase watering by 1.355 units over the next three days\n(Updated hand-drawn illustrations)\n...\n[A3-26]\n(Can't remember the name) Today's Status: Very Poor\nPerformance: Individual proliferation, poor development, not suitable for consumption recently\nCountermeasure: Adjust nutrient solution composition this week, add 0.85mg of H45 nutrient solution\n(Note: Updated illustration, renamed to Soup Dumpling)\n(Hand-drawn illustration)\n(Tastes bad, needs adjustments) (Marked as important)\n...\n[Log Message]\nVivian: Andanna! How many times have I told you not to keep carnivorous mutant plants in the laboratory! And don't steal food casually! Are you having diarrhea again?\n(…)\n(I've returned from the hospital)"
},
	[47374]={ language="Information One: She cultivates some edible mutant plants herself and often ends up in the hospital when experimenting on herself. Doctors privately call her a mad scientist.\n\nInformation Two: She gets anxious for days before giving reports and speeches, thinking about facing a large Ravend.\n\nInformation Three: Her drawing is terrible. The plant illustrations she creates can only be understood by herself, so the public version of the illustrations is done by others on her behalf."
},
	[47375]={ language="1. [Selevie: The History of Plant Changes]: A handwritten manuscript signed by Vivian, carried around by Catalpa.\n\n2. Catalyst Emitter: Looks like a handgun, but most of the time it's used to shoot seeds and hormones, not very lethal.\n\n3. Medicine Kit: Usually hung at the waist, making it convenient for Catalpa to tend to sick plants at any time.\n\n4. Plant Specimens: Some fossilized specimens of extinct plants collected by Catalpa in the laboratory."
},
	[47376]={ language="Information One: Names every plant they cultivate seriously, but sometimes forgets due to sheer number.\n\nInformation Two: Their messy room and tidy lab are worlds apart.\n\nInformation Three: Occasionally trips over flat ground due to absent-mindedness and doesn't mind being seen."
},
	[47377]={ language="[I'm sorry, if it wasn't for me insisting on investigating the Void Expanse knowing the supplies weren't enough, you wouldn't be hurt, and things wouldn't have turned out this way.]\n[They say I haven't turned into a Mutant because you left all the medicine for me...]\n…\n[Although they've injected us with drugs, the damage from Void Particles contamination is irreversible, I don't know how much longer I can hold on...]\n[...Vivian, I promise I'll find a way for you to regain your memory... just hang on a little longer...]\n…\n[Vivian, how are you feeling today?]\n[Today is college graduation day, they introduced me to the fifth lab, do you remember it here? It has the largest natural greenhouse in Selevie, a place we always wanted to visit.]\n[If possible, I really wish I could attend the graduation ceremony with you.]\n[I've already revised and completed the first chapter of 'The History of Selevie Plant Changes.' Without Vivian, my progress is slow, because this is the book you wanted to finish... Once I complete the last chapter, when you see this book, will you remember me?]\n…\n[Vivian, my body is barely holding on...]\n[The good news is they can remodel me into an AIMBS Operator with 'D-Blood,' so I won't have to worry about being hurt by Void Particles again, and I'll be able to investigate the Void Expanse to finish that book soon.]\n[Once I finish that book and you see it, you'll definitely remember, right?]\n— From Selevie Central Hospital Special Ward 03, visit video recording."
},
	[47378]={ language="Information One: Conducting research on aggressive mutant plants prohibited by labs, currently no record of injuries.\n\nInformation Two: Has extreme interests, likes extremely cute plants and also those that look very dangerous and scary."
},
	[47379]={ language="[Lab 05 [Incubator], Explorations in the Void Expanse XXX times]\n1. Area S-6, check approximate quantity of mutant plants (√)\n2. Area S-6, routine sampling of water bodies (Incomplete)\n3. Area V-05, routine soil sampling (√)\n4....\n…\n10. Area Z-60, sampling of decayed plant fungi after alienation (Incomplete)\n\nTIPS:\nDirector, I've thought about this for a long time, and I think I really need to bring this up with you. It's not just me; everyone involved in the investigation feels the same way. We don't want to work with Catalpa anymore.\n\nCountless times now, during our explorations in the Void Expanse, we can't even find where Catalpa is! She's nowhere to be seen half the time, and only shows up leisurely when we're about to leave!\n\nThis behavior is truly unreasonable! What if she attracts Mutant and puts everyone in danger? We regular experiment personnel aren't AIMBS Operators!\n\nIt's like she doesn't care about everyone's safety at all! I've heard that her college mate, that Vivian or whatever her name is, got into trouble because of her behavior and hasn't woken up yet, right? We don't want to end up like that!\n\nWe've warned her before and really hope, Director, you can think of a way to deal with this. We really don't want to lose our lives one day because of Catalpa's recklessness!\n\n——\nRepo: We've communicated with Catalpa. Future explorations in the Void Expanse by the Lab 05 will grant Catalpa individual permission rights, while other colleagues will continue their tasks as usual."
},
	[47380]={ language="Information One: When going out to explore alone, always brings a guiding drone due to the fear of getting lost.\n\nInformation Two: One of the Interests is earning credits and writing papers, regarded as a weirdo by other peers."
},
	[47381]={ language="Real Name: Pardiya Chorklas\nIdentity: Starlog Media Signed Artist\nInterests: Divination, Studying magic techniques, mixing fireworks"
},
	[47382]={ language="This is an ordinary day in a small town of Uzyanta, and it's also the last day of the Sumiru Circus performance here.\n\nSince they are leaving tomorrow, tonight's Ravend is unusually large—many people have traveled long distances just to witness the debut of the Fireworks Magician, who has been advertised for days. A long queue has already formed outside the venue early.\n\nA small figure emerges from the busy circus backstage among the adults preparing various props, wearing a not-so-fitting costume, and in a hurry, has knocked over several props.\n\n[Make way, make way—]\n[Excuse me, excuse me—]\n[Ah, be careful—]\n[Pardiya—my props—]\n[Oh, sorry, sorry!]\n[Break a leg, Pardiya—]\n[Hehe, watch out for my amazing performance!]\nThe girl turns back with a confident smile.\n\nAlthough Pardiya's answer is full of confidence, her heart is actually pounding hard at the moment.\n\nThis is naturally expected; after all, she is only 11 years old and has always been her grandfather's assistant on stage. But today, she is going to perform solo as the main act, with no one by her side, just herself.\n\nAs it's almost time to go on stage, Pardiya goes to the curtain, takes a deep breath, and quietly peeks through the corner to observe the state of the audience—she needs to see their expressions to decide whether to use her little secret—\n\nPardiya's so-called little trick is a special ability she discovered when she was very small—she can faintly sense who around her likes or dislikes her and can influence people's emotions to some extent. This special power has troubled her before, but now—\n\nShe only uses this ability to bring joy to the audience—even if she forces herself a little bit.\n\nHowever, when Pardiya peeks through the curtain and sees that all the audience members have anticipation on their faces, her worries instantly vanish.\n\nShe boldly draws back the curtain and steps onto the stage—"
},
	[47383]={ language="Information One: Good at performing cute and lively magic acts, but sometimes longs to perform thrilling magic like body segmentation or escape room type acts.\n\nInformation Two: Due to being skilled in magic, occasionally invited by police to assist in solving some theft cases.\n\nInformation Three: Dreamed of becoming a phantom thief during middle school, but it was just a thought."
},
	[47384]={ language="1. Movie Projector: The vintage model bought by Pardiya when she earned her first income.\n\n2. Fireworks Playing Cards: They look like regular cards but have been modified by Pardiya for performances, with secrets unknown to anyone.\n\n3.Tarot Cards: A small prop for divination, with cards designed by Pardiya herself. \n\n4. Fireworks Formula: Pardiya's original exclusive recipe, for which she's already applied for a patent."
},
	[47385]={ language="Information One: As a child, there was a time she firmly believed that [witchcraft] and [magic] were the same thing.\n\nInformation Two: During early performances, there was a mistake, and although the audience didn't notice, it still bothered me for a long time.\n\nInformation Three: Banned from participating in any card games because the winner would definitely be her."
},
	[47386]={ language="The accident happened on a usual afternoon.\n\nToday was a major performance after Pardiya became famous. She had spent a long time on preparation for this show, and spectators traveled from afar to fill the square.\n\nPardiya did not disappoint; she showcased her latest exclusive Fireworks magic during the performance, igniting the emotions of the audience. As the cheers continued, the show gradually reached its finale.\n\nBut suddenly, an explosion sound came from afar. Due to the loud Fireworks, many thought it was part of the show. However, standing high on stage, Pardiya realized something was wrong.\n\n She saw the explosion occur, certain it wasn't due to her own performance mishap. But if she stopped the show immediately and urged the audience to leave, it might cause panic and a stampede, leading to a bigger disaster—\n\nIn just an instant, Pardiya decided what to do next—she used her emotion-influencing ability to infect all the spectators, then diverted their attention with a spontaneously performed Fireworks magic, guiding them to leave the performance venue orderly.\n\nAfter the show, Pardiya immediately contacted local police. The police, after investigating, told Pardiya it was a terrorist attack and hoped she wouldn't perform again for the time being to avoid further danger.\n\nNot long after, an organization called [Leistance Security Bureau] approached Pardiya, saying they had been observing her for a long time—the explosion during the show wasn't just a simple attack, and Pardiya's displayed abilities had another explanation.\n\nTurns out she was born with Stellaron Resonance ability, possessing the special qualification to become an AIMBS Operator. The people from Leistance Security Bureau told Pardiya that if she wanted to better utilize this ability, becoming an AIMBS Operator might be a better choice.\n\nTo bring happiness to everyone and knowing there were many other girls like her, after a discussion, Pardiya agreed to sign a contract with Leistance, inject D-Blood to become an AIMBS Operator, and head to Leistance for a six-month tutorial."
},
	[47387]={ language="Information One: Escape room expert; there's no lock she can't open or puzzle she can't solve, making her the Challenge target for all escape room theme parks.\n\nInformation Two: She designed multiple sets of costumes herself, to the point where she struggles with [which costume to choose for the performance] in the end."
},
	[47388]={ language="Pardiya 12/05/XXXX 9:20:08\nWhen the stars move to designated orbits and the scentless flower blossoms and fades, the grand neon will return again to take its place on the throne of dawn, offering you a performance beyond anything imaginable\n—— Neon\nPardiya 12/05/XXXX 9:20:15\n\nDear Manager, this is the best promo I could think of. How about it? I believe that such a glamorous introduction will capture everyone's attention! (confident.jpg)\nManager 12/05/XXXX 9:40:08\n...This is what you came up with after racking your brains for two days?\nPardiya 12/05/XXXX 9:40:10\nThat's right! How about it?!\nManager 12/05/XXXX 9:41:04\nThis is your comeback show, take it seriously!\nPardiya 12/05/XXXX 9:42:35\nBut I think it sounds cool! Don't you think so?\nRiddle-talking is all the rage now, it will definitely get buzz! I promise this will be unprecedented, unmatched! \nManager 12/05/XXXX 9:43:04\n...Did you fry your brain at that Leistance Tutorial Camp? Come back and discuss it with me, I have already booked your ticket.\nPardiya 12/05/XXXX 9:43:20\nWow! When? You've already bought the ticket?\nManager XXXX/12/05 9:43:44\nIt's today! The Boss wants to see you tonight, hurry up, pack your things!\nPardiya 12/05/XXXX 9:44:00\nNo problem at all! Just wait for the return of the genius magician Miss Pardiya~ Heh~\nSee you at the company!"
},
	[47389]={ language="Information One: No one really knows how many Fireworks she's carrying with her. Can that hat really fit them?\n\nInformation Two: She has emphasized that her fortune-telling offers no guidance on emotional fortunes, yet people still keep coming to book emotional fortune-telling."
},
	[47390]={ language="Real Name: Koraz \nIdentity: Operator under Lissugen Branch of Leistance Security Bureau \nInterests: Cats, all cute animals, sweets, eating"
},
	[47391]={ language="Leistance Security Bureau Disciplinary Notice\n- Number 10xx27xxA\nDisciplinary Level: E- (Lowest)\n\nOn xx/xx/xxxx, Operator Koraz was involved in a fight, causing serious negative impact. Considering the provocation and disrespectful remarks from the other party before the fight, and since the altercation didn't result in significant bodily harm, the security bureau's disciplinary committee decided to give a notified verbal reprimand.\n\nAll department Operators and staff should take this as a warning, pay attention to their behavior, and strictly adhere to the security bureau's regulations and discipline.\n\nThis is hereby notified.\n\n- Leistance Security Bureau Disciplinary Committee Inquiry Record\n- Record Number 10xx27xxB\n\nInquiry Time: xx/xx at xx:xx, xxxx\nTo xx/xx at xx:xx, xxxx\n\nName and Unit of Interviewee: Koraz-Flying Fish Squad\n\nQ: We are members of the disciplinary committee, now questioning you according to regulations. Please answer truthfully, understood?\nA: Got it meow.\nQ: Do you have any requests?\nA: Can we hurry? Koraz is starting to feel sleepy meow.\nQ: We're here because of the fight with a trainee at the base, we hope you can answer truthfully.\nA: Uh uh uh... uhh. I will meow.\nQ: Why did you fight?\nA: That guy talked bad about Yuanya! I heard everything meow. People always think Yuanya is too young to be in the Flying Fish Squad. They say her reputation is all bragged about, that she just eats and drinks, and she sticks around the bureau without achieving anything... They even said she stayed in the security bureau because she doesn't have parents!\nQ: So you hit him?\nA: How can I tolerate that meow! If you were me, you couldn't stand it either. Plus, I didn't exactly hit him, I just hit him with a hammer.\nQ: That's hitting him.\nA: Not even one hit is okay meow...\nQ: He's still in the medical office.\nA: That's not... alright, alright. Koraz hit him meow.\nQ: We've understood the situation.\nA: Uhh...\nQ: ... Operator Koraz, don't be like this. Since it didn't cause too serious harm... we ultimately decided to give you a notified verbal reprimand. We will also give a verbal reprimand to that trainee. Do you have any objections?\nA: No meow. But you must promise, you'll definitely educate him well, right? You have to promise me meow!\nQ: ... You may leave.\nA: Then I'll take it as you promised meow! Thank you, miss committee, I'm going back to sleep! Good night!\nQ: Good night."
},
	[47392]={ language="Information One: Due to experiences in childhood, afraid of being alone in dark, confined spaces, and also dislikes Chilled.\n\nInformation Two: As a child, often broke the door lock when forgetting the keys, leading to many serious warnings and written reflections, but no longer does it now.\n\nInformation Three: Every now and then has to suffer from allergies because of [risking allergies just to pet cats.]"
},
	[47393]={ language="1. Mechanical cat ears and tail: Designed with Yuanya, these are precision machines that can sense neural signals and respond accordingly.\n\n2. Meow Meow Hammer: Designed with Yuanya, equipped with a Model that looks super cute but is useless in combat. It's really heavy, but feels like a balloon hammer when held by Koraz.\n\n3. [Lissugen Cat Encyclopedia]: A practical, handy guidebook for cat lovers, summarizing the cat species and group characteristics found on the streets of Lissugen.\n\n4. Diary: A diary commonly used by children, it has a password lock. Sometimes Koraz forgets the password and then asks Yuanya for help."
},
	[47394]={ language="Information One: Eats a lot, with the highest record being finishing a four-person meal in one go at a fried chicken joint.\n\nInformation Two: Doesn't like spicy flavors and can't eat things that are too hot or too cold. But loves peppermint flavor in ice cream.\n\nInformation Three: Though claimed to be a cat, has a great routine. Sleeps very early like a school kid and wakes up full of energy."
},
	[47395]={ language="Patient Name: Koraz \nGender: Female\nDepartment: ■■■■\nWard: ■■■\nBed Number: 01\nHospital ID: AX■■■032\nSurgery Date: ■-31st-■■■■\nPreoperative Diagnosis: Patient's ■■■ indicators normal, ■■■■ normal, no notable allergic reactions to ■■■■, ■■■■. Gene fragment ■■■■ shows ■■ signs, ■■■■ decreased, ■■■■■■■. Diagnosis shows the lesion is in ■■■, ■■■ treatment necessary.\nIntraoperative Diagnosis: ■■■■■■■\nSurgery Name: ■■■■ Gene ■■ Surgery\nSurgeon and Assistant: ■■■■·■■■, ■■·■■\nAnesthesia Method: General anesthesia with tracheal intubation\nSurgery Procedure, Findings, and Management:\n(Large amount of encrypted text)\n(Large amount of encrypted text)\nRecord Date:■-31st-■■■■\nSurgeon Signature: (Signed by Guardian) ■■\n\nPostoperative Course Record\nPatient Koraz, female, ■■ years old, hospitalized at guardian's ■■ request due to ■■■■, ■■■■■■■. Diagnosed as ■■■■■■ and with all preoperative preparations, underwent ■■■■ Gene ■■ Surgery under general anesthesia with tracheal intubation, detailed process in surgery records. Anesthesia worked well during surgery, minimal incision, smooth operation, patient returned safely to the ward. In childhood, the patient lived long-term in a high-risk laboratory environment, causing the current genetic condition. Lesion removed, but uncertain future developmental impacts are estimated. Currently, patient shows tendencies to allergic reactions, requiring close monitoring during treatment. Post-op treatment aims to restore physical functions, stabilize gene ■■■■■■■, and other comprehensive treatments.\n…\n...\nOn ■-5th-■■■■, ■■ Director's Ward Round\nOn the fifth postoperative day, the patient reported no discomfort or allergic reactions recently, vital signs stable, in good general condition, no cardiac or pulmonary issues, abdomen normal, good compatibility with ■■, significant improvement in physical function. Rest is good at night, good spirits, especially high appetite, except for extraordinary strength compared to average subjects, no other abnormalities. ■■ Director instructed: Patient has recovered smoothly post-op, approve infusion and discharge once cured, and advised rest after discharge. Half month later, commence free movement recovery, six months later, begin using ■■■■ for further physical enhancement.\n\n——■■■■ Private Healer Center, ■■■ Treatment Record"
},
	[47396]={ language="Information One: She gets angry easily, but she's easy to cheer up—just bring her some tasty food.\n\nInformation Two: If her excess energy bothers you, just give her any book and she'll fall asleep within five minutes."
},
	[47397]={ language="Month X, X\n\nLast night, I had a dream. I dreamt of that place again.\n\nNot dark, but a very cold place. I was there alone, unable to move, and couldn't see anything. I remember I didn't like that kind of light, it was a really white white. From the direction the light was coming, I could hear some muffled voices...\n\nMy body felt uncomfortable, like something had locked it up.\n\nI used to have this dream often when I was little. I remember the first time I had it, I told Aunt Yuan. She explained to me what a nightmare was.\n\n[Nightmares aren't necessarily real,] she said gently, [It's good to know they're not real.]\n\nThat night, Aunt, I, and Yuanya slept together. I didn't have that dream again.\n\nAs I grew up, I came to know it might've been a lab. The lab where my mom and dad worked. But exactly what they were researching, I have no idea. No matter how much I asked for details, nobody would explain it clearly to me.\n\nBut I can't remember her face anymore. I've forgotten what dad looked like too. Did they hold me, talk to me? I don't know. I also don't want to ask Aunt Yuan. I feel like maybe she doesn't know much about it either.\n\nThese are things only parents and their kids would know.\n\nLater on, if I have a nightmare, I wouldn't tell anyone anymore. Honestly, in my heart, it's gradually less like a nightmare.\n\nIf I hold on a bit longer, could I see the two of them? Would I have a chance to hear them talk to me...maybe even a hug?\n\nThese are uncertain things, right?\n\nIt feels more like an ordinary dream, a vague memory that's stayed. I've been forgetful since I was young, books I've read, things I've learned, I quickly forget. So, it's me who forgot, not that it never happened. This dream reminds me of that.\n\nIt's not a nightmare, I don't think so.\n\nUhh, writing this makes me sleepy again. And a little hungry.\n\nI'll go find a snack in the kitchen and then go back to sleep~ Anyway, there's no task tomorrow, no one will wake me up. Maybe if I sleep longer, the dream will be longer too.\n\nHope there's some cake in the kitchen today, and that Yuanya hasn't eaten it all."
},
	[47398]={ language="Information One: Her ideal height is 178CM, and she has a strong belief in reaching this height.\n\nInformation Two: She is mostly carefree and unaffected, even when asked about background. But when it comes to Yuanya and Yuanya's mom, she unexpectedly becomes calm and serious."
},
	[47399]={ language="Real Name: Roxie Noel\nIdentity: Mechanical Craftsman, Leistance External Prosthetic Professional\nInterests: Creating precise machinery, studying prosthetics"
},
	[47400]={ language="When the title [Little Doctor of Mechanic Town] got around, Roxie was already the top assistant in her father's workshop. If you hadn't seen it for yourself, you might never believe that those intricate instruments and realistic prosthetics were made by a child.\n\nRoxie's mother suffered an arm mutation due to Void Particles contamination. Thanks to surgery and her stepfather's masterful skills, her arm became just like a normal person's. She could finally gently stroke Roxie's head with [normal] hands, and no one discriminated against them anymore. In Roxie's mind, nothing better could happen. At the same time, she gradually formed some ideas—the flesh would eventually get hurt and perish, only machines are eternal.\n\nAs time went on, Roxie became more passionate about mechanics and prosthetic Remodeling. By the time she was college-aged, there was nothing more for her to learn in Mechanic Town. So, she expressed her desire to move to the big city to her parents and got their approval.\n\nIn this way, as an apprentice and craftsman, Roxie arrived at Lissugen. After completing her studies with astonishing results, she used the money she earned to set up her own studio in the city. She created mechanical prosthetics for those who had lost limbs or wished to Remodel their bodies for greater strength, never turning anyone away.\n\nFor Roxie, making mechanical prosthetics is what brings her joy. She doesn't care what others think of her. To her, machinery is the eternal beauty, and creating, Remodeling, and perfecting various mechanics and prosthetics is her delight and pursuit, nothing more."
},
	[47401]={ language="Information One: The studio was set up by herself, and it looks really messy, be careful not to mess with her stuff.\n\nInformation Two: She loves clocks, but the ticking sound keeps her awake, so her bedroom only has a digital clock.\n\nInformation Three: She's a perfectionist and hasn't created anything she considers [perfect] yet."
},
	[47402]={ language="1. Cleaning Cloth: Easy to carry, feels very soft, used for wiping precision instruments.\n\n2. Small Toolbox: Contains multiple sets of tools, each one is the most handy to use, not only for repairing prosthetics but also for some precision maintenance.\n\n3. Magnifying Glass: Sometimes comes in handy.\n\n4. [Taino Mechanical History]: One of Roxie's sources of inspiration."
},
	[47403]={ language="Information One: Doesn't trust electronic magnifiers much, firmly believes human eyes handle precision instruments more accurately.\n\nInformation Two: Although she believes in [mechanical eternity,] she has never tried to remodel herself for unknown reasons.\n\nInformation Three: Has been called a [heartless doctor without morals] and personally agrees with the title."
},
	[47404]={ language="[I just wanted to fix my prosthetic eye, and she asked if I wanted to upgrade it with integrated computer functions, even suggesting I'd look better if I replaced my whole body... What? No way, I'm not going to do that! I just want to maintain my eye!]\n\n[You've been asked that question, right? What? The one about 'if you replaced your whole body except for the head, are you still yourself?' It's just so scary, who thinks of questions like that!]\n\n[She asks every patient that question, and that's scary in itself, isn't it?]\n\n[Consultation? No, no, I just like mechanics, so I frequent the place. That doctor has unique insights on prosthetics and exoskeletons, we get along... As for the consultation fee? It's certainly not cheap, but I can afford it, so it's not a problem... Regarding that question? If possible, I'd really like to try and see what that feels like. Yes, I'm sure I'd still be myself with just a head.]\n\n[I've heard about that strange hospital... but remodeling the flesh into machinery? No way, absolutely not.]\n*\n[Anyway, it's a good thing my poor son who lost his legs can stand again. Those legs are just like his original ones, he can run and jump. I'm very grateful to that doctor. Would I recommend her? I'd definitely recommend her to anyone who needs prosthetics.]\n\n[That hospital filled with all sorts of weird limbs... it's terrifying, right? I heard her repair tools are covered in bloodstains... maybe the materials are taken off people, how else would they look so real?]\n\n[That workshop? I heard the owner went to handle a large project, and now you need to make an appointment a year in advance. What are they up to?]\n— Lissugen Horror Society Episode XX, Excerpts from an interview with [The Strange Doctor on Rainbow Street.]"
},
	[47405]={ language="Information One: Keeps tweaking works she's not satisfied with, but she always delivers on time.\n\nInformation Two: She tries to sell her favorite vintage-style prosthetics to patients, but mostly gets turned down."
},
	[47406]={ language="Roxie knew about the real existence of Leistance on an ordinary day.\n\nThat day, people from Lawton Institute of Bionic Mechanics came to commission some work from her—they had her services a few years back, and now they needed her help to maintain a prosthetic body—one fully mechanized except for the head.\n\nRoxie was intrigued by this request. Driven by curiosity, she asked the Lawton Institute of Bionic Mechanics who needed help. After some hesitation, they took her to Leistance Security Bureau, where Roxie met Kymia for the first time.\n\nSeeing Kymia amazed Roxie—an entire body made of mechanical parts was the [eternal art] she pursued. She immediately decided to provide service to Kymia for free.\n\nTo help Kymia maintain her body, Roxie began frequently traveling to Leistance, eventually signing a long-term contract with them. But this also brought up some issues.\n\nAs a trial mechanical body of AIMBS, Kymia's body had many situations beyond ordinary understanding, and maintenance often faced difficulties.\n\nAfter some thought, Roxie believed the problem stemmed from the part of Kymia that belonged to [AIMBS Operator.] To solve it, she needed to... stand on the same research platform.\n\nChasing perfection, Roxie requested to become an AIMBS Operator with Leistance, believing it would let her utilize her abilities better. Leistance considered Roxie's value to the organization and agreed.\n\nAfter a series of rigorous assessments, Roxie was injected with D-Blood, becoming an AIMBS Operator. After that, she could control Crystal-powered mechanical arms for more complex, precise operations and was stationed at Leistance.\n\nAlthough now stationed at Leistance, Roxie still returns to her studio on the third and fourth weekends each month to offer services to the public—still asking everyone who comes for exoskeleton and prosthetic repairs if they'd like to remodel their bodies. Most get scared away, but she doesn't mind."
},
	[47407]={ language="Information One: Very punctual, calculates time by seconds, feels anxious if time is wasted.\n\nInformation Two: Can multitask at work, but sometimes experiences issues with auxiliary mechanical arms fighting each other."
},
	[47408]={ language="Real Name: Miusha\nIdentity: Leistance Security Bureau Vilatria Religious Consultant\nInterests: Making money, saving money, traveling"
},
	[47409]={ language="Do you have urgent problems without a clue for a solution?\n\nDo you have very difficult but unavoidable tasks to do?\n\nDo you find it tough to let go of items, hard to gather information, or remain intensely curious about secrets?\n\nExpertise matters, so instead of letting these troubles waste your valuable time, why not open your mind, free up your hands, and hire professionals to handle them for you?\n\nI offer fair charges, reasonable prices. Mission accomplished with honesty. Whatever your troubles, I will wholeheartedly find the best solution for you. No matter the difficulty, even if I can't give a one-stop solution, I will definitely point out a clear path. No charge if the goal isn't achieved.\n\nIf interested, please contact Ms. Musa at the Leistance Security Bureau Vilatria Religious Missions office through the provided address below. This number responds 24/7; please leave a voicemail during evening prayer times.\n\nFor inquiries about Vilatria Religious Missions, consultation is open during weekday office hours only.\n\nMay the stars guide your path!\n\n—Posted note on the Leistance Security Bureau bulletin board\n\nThe note was removed by the Security Bureau Ethics Committee 24 hours after posting."
},
	[47410]={ language="Information One: She's a popular choice for a shopping buddy. Many say they've never seen someone better at haggling than Miusha. But she's hard to pin down—always seems to have something going on.\n\nInformation Two: She's good with finances, and a key activity in her spare time is counting her assets.\n\nInformation Three: Sharp-tongued and skilled in biting sarcasm, sometimes a bit harsh. When questioned with [How can a religious person care so much about worldly wealth?], her usual reply is [Aren't the Coins in our hands just earthly stars?]"
},
	[47411]={ language="1. Crystal Weapon: Meteor Staff, looks like the traditional Vilatria staff, lovingly crafted by the Leistance Security Bureau's Defense Supplies Department.\n\n2. A Vilatria Coin: Ordinary currency, not collectible. Very old, with some stains on it.\n\n3. Star Summoning Church Tome: Pages are slightly yellowed, looks like it's often flipped through by the owner.\n\n4. Old Photo: A family portrait of three. The little girl in the photo appears to be a young Miusha."
},
	[47412]={ language="Information One: Can handle almost any request that comes her way. Even if she can't complete it directly, she can at least provide a direction and effective help for a solution. Believes the biggest original sin of humanity is [being easily replaceable as a tiny part.]\n\nInformation Two: Lives a relatively simple life and doesn't have strong material desires. However, very attentive to HP, willing to spend heavily in this area. Has a dark past of being tricked by unscrupulous merchants selling HP products upon first arriving in Lissugen.\n\nInformation Three: Has an extremely broad network and an astonishing contact list. Views everyone as potential clients and maintains good relationships. This seems to be their attitude toward both Leistance Security Bureau and Vilatria authorities."
},
	[47413]={ language="Beware! HP supplement scam reappears, victim range expands further\n\nRecently, fraudsters have been targeting specific groups by promoting overpriced HP supplements, scamming them out of large sums of money. The counterfeit supplements may contain illegal additives that could be toxic, posing further threats to the victims' life and property safety.\n\nPolice received a report the other day about a Vilatria nun who fell victim to such a scam in our country. This nun is only 19 years old, the youngest victim in such cases to date.\n\nSister Sha (a pseudonym) places great importance on her HP. After leaving Vilatria, she came into contact with many high-end Technologies in the Healer community and highly advocates for a lifestyle of HP supplements. She told our reporter in a devoutly sorrowful tone, [Only by taking good care of your body can you serve God better.] Her words moved the reporter deeply.\n\nAs the case involved religious members from Vilatria, the police conducted a thorough investigation. During the process, Sister Sha (a pseudonym) offered substantial assistance to the police, eventually providing crucial clues that led to the arrest of the scam group's leader. She even received a reward from the authorities. She revealed to our reporter that she was keen on further cooperation with the police, but due to various factors, it didn't happen.\n\n[Getting some extra pay would definitely be nice,] Sister Sha candidly told the reporter, [After all, the losses I suffered are hard to recover.] However, when asked why she places such importance on HP at such a young age, Sister Sha was reluctant to elaborate, possibly due to some untold past experiences. This is often the attitude shown by other victims when discussing why they fell for the scam—indicative of how fraudsters precisely target such vulnerabilities in these individuals, making the scams hard to guard against.\n\nHere we also wish to remind the public to stay vigilant and not fall for scams in the name of HP. (Informant: Miss Miao, Reward xx Taino Currency)"
},
	[47414]={ language="Information One: Even though she doesn't appear to be devout believers, she's never gone against the teachings or missed evening prayers. However, she's not very diligent in their primary duty of preaching.\n\nInformation Two: Apart from official personnel, the only old acquaintance she keeps in touch with is the abbey's head, whom she affectionately calls Grandma Abbess."
},
	[47415]={ language="Greetings to you, Bishop... It's truly an honor for me, a humble abbess, to be summoned by you personally.\n\nYou wish to know more about Miusha, to confirm if she is suitable to be the envoy of the stars and brings starlight to the far reaches of the world. I will tell you everything about her truthfully.\n\nMiusha has faced hardships since childhood. A plague took away her parents' HP, and poverty ultimately took them from her side. Of course, this is the trial given by God. So many here endure such trials, which proves we are the chosen ones God intends to test.\n\nDestiny brought her under my care, and I accepted the will of the stars, doing my best to care for her, just like the other children in the monastery. We are bound together in starlight like a family without blood ties. I won't deceive you: initially, she was rebellious, secretly listening to the monastery's Crystal technique classes. Later, she even sneaked into the examination team and achieved excellent results. But I finally made her understand that the gifts destiny gave her did not include these. She should not seek what doesn't belong to her—this is her lifelong practice.\n\nNow, she is the most devout and the youngest nun in the abbey. I can confidently boast to you that she is the person most familiar with the classics, apart from myself. Surely you have witnessed her wisdom and perseverance in the Preacher selection process. Can any devout believer nationwide muster the resolve to leave God's blessed land and sow the seeds of faith in ignorant and barren foreign lands?\n\nThere is no one more suitable than her, Bishop. Please confidently issue the decree, allowing her to embark on her journey.\n\n—Vilatria Star Calling Council Preacher Archive"
},
	[47416]={ language="Information One: Tends to make conservative plans during battles, believing that staying alive is more important than anything.\n\nInformation Two: Strongly resists returning to Vilatria and is reluctant to talk much about her past. However, she excels in being a religious advisor, and some say she can even recite all the Vilatria classics word for word."
},
	[47417]={ language="Real Name: Tilye Skylar\nIdentity: Leistance Lissugen Branch Intern Operator\nInterests: Playing games, collecting retro game cartridges"
},
	[47418]={ language="Tilye's family runs an internet café and game store, so she practically grew up immersed in gaming. She's never picky about the games she plays, and sometimes unconsciously mimics the movements and speech of characters. Moreover, she often plays games to the point of neglecting sleep and meals. Her family thinks she's unambitious and won't achieve much, but she doesn't care about their opinions.\n\nAmong the myriad of game themes, her favorite is the hero saving the world. She especially loves a series called [The World Uniformed Girl.] The game's protagonist, like Tilye, is seemingly a plain girl who transforms into a hero saving the world from peril during crises, making like-minded friends along the way. This cool and slightly over-the-top character portrayal effortlessly captured Tilye's heart. Since she was 12, she started dressing up like the game's heroine—with a JK uniform, eyepatch, and headphones, all included.\n\nTilye never imagined that her love for gaming would bring such significant changes to her fate, but there's still some time before the day her destiny changes..."
},
	[47419]={ language="Information One: Always wears an eyepatch on the right eye, whether it's due to a real eye issue or just to look cool, no one in the entire Lissugen branch knows the answer.\n\nInformation Two: Broke the highest score record of the simulation flight test at the Leistance headquarters, claiming it was because this test is just like playing a game.\n\nInformation Three: In recent years, due to frequently staying up late playing games, her eyesight has deteriorated, and now the eye without the eyepatch is wearing contact lenses."
},
	[47420]={ language="1. QSQ3000 Gaming Console: A birthday gift Tilye received when she was 6, still runs smoothly today. It's been outdated for years, but it's just as fun as any new model.\n\n2. Customized Gaming Headset: With active noise cancellation and surround sound effects, you can feel an immersive experience even without leaving home.\n\n3. Eyepatch: A merchandise from a highly popular game, stocked up on many to rotate through."
},
	[47421]={ language="Information One: When she first started practicing nunchaku, she was so clumsy that she ended up hitting herself and got bumps all over her head.\n\nInformation Two: Not good at playing dating games, reportedly no matter how hard she tries, it always leads to a Bad Ending.\n\nInformation Three: The reason for wearing twin tails is that it's hard to get up on time in the morning to fix her hair, so she just ties it up."
},
	[47422]={ language="[The World Uniform Girl] finally has an online game version. Thanks to its excellent quality, it has gained high popularity and is loved by many young people, becoming a hot topic among Tilye's classmates. As a fan of the series, Tilye... \n\nNaturally, she is hooked and, relying on her outstanding skills and relentless gaming, has become the second-ranked player on the server. Next, she just needs to defeat the former top player to reach the summit of this server.\n\nAt this moment, Tilye does not yet know that this so-called former top player is actually Leistance's information professional, Deling. The online game version of [The World Uniform Girl] is actually just a test set by the Star Council to recruit fresh talent. \n\nFacing Tilye's challenge, Deling designed numerous traps to test her, but Tilye ultimately cracked them one by one. When Tilye finally confronted Deling, Deling offered her a choice to meet at Leistance Lissugen branch office for a chat.\n\nThis kind of dramatic development is exactly Tilye's cup of tea, and she agreed to Deling's invitation without a second thought."
},
	[47423]={ language="Information One: One of the many habitual latecomers at the Leistance Lissugen Branch.\n\nInformation Two: Has many alternate accounts online and used to form a streaming group called [Electronic Zoo] with some people from the branch."
},
	[47424]={ language="What should a true hero be like?\n\n[Void Particles pollution,] [D-Blood,] [AIMBS Operator,] [Leistance]...\n\nOne unfamiliar term after another poured from the mouth of the girl in front of Tilye. She was Deling, and beside her sat a sister with blue hair.\n\nAfter explaining to Tilye, Deling and Isis quietly watched the girl dressed like a high schooler in front of them.\n\n[Of course, the choice is yours, and you have some time to think about it...] \n\nBefore Isis finished her sentence, Tilye responded—\n\n[That's so cool! Can I join right away?!]\n\nA spark of excitement flashed in Tilye's eyes, so much so that Isis was a bit taken aback by her decisiveness.\n\n[Have you thought it through?]\n\n[Of course! Oh, by the way—]\n\nTilye tilted her head and thought for a moment.\n\n[If I need a code name, just call me Arc!]"
},
	[47425]={ language="Information One: The uniform on her isn't merchandise, it's an authentic high school girl's uniform.\n\nInformation Two: The clips on her twin-tails aren't just simple decorations, they're Void Particles detection devices. As for the ribbons... that's the creator's personal preference."
},
	[47426]={ language="Real Name: Typhenie Newcastle\nIdentity: Owner of Lissugen [Dreams] Business Consulting Missions\nInterests: Playing chess, reading financial news, collecting gossip"
},
	[47427]={ language="Since childhood, Typhenie often skipped family education, spending lots of time on the chessboard—even during events she had to attend, she'd sit expressionless in a corner, entertaining herself with a small chess set she carried.\n\nChess isn't just Typhenie's hobby; it's a habit, almost a daily instinct, like breathing and sleeping.\n\nIn daily life, Typhenie merges chess with reality—every business communication, even every daily move, is just a step in her Layout.\n\nOf course, she'd rather be the hand moving the pieces than a pawn on the board. But during Missions' early days, lacking funds and connections forced Typhenie to get involved, leaving her mark in shady bar alleys and upscale dinner parties alike.\n\nMaybe she's too uncomfortable being in the spotlight, making recruitment the most urgent task for Dreams Consult.\n\nAfter Korinna got [lured] into Missions, all outdoor work naturally fell on her, and without Yan's support, Korinna's attendance might have caused her to redo high school.\n\nAs for overtime pay… perhaps the focus should be on the [Minor Employment Regulation] first."
},
	[47428]={ language="Information One: Loves sweets and often tries new products due to exaggerated marketing.\n\nInformation Two: Maintains the top ladder position on several online chess platforms for a long time.\n\nInformation Three: Suspected of being a long-time anonymous contributor to a tabloid in Lissugen, but has never admitted it."
},
	[47429]={ language="1. Stone-carved Chess Piece: It's quite old, a finely crafted [Queen.] Typhenie has a habit of holding it while she thinks.\n\n2. There's no record of business transactions, only filled with what Typhenie considers losses—if all these [debts] could be repaid, Typhenie would definitely top Joshburg's rich list.\n\n3. Voice Recorder: Portable, long-lasting battery, waterproof and dustproof, never missing any valuable information. As for legal risks, they're not within the Mission's owner's considerations."
},
	[47430]={ language="Information One: Spending lots of money on setting up Information online, but often skimping on benefits for Missions' staff.\n\nInformation Two: Has multiple alternate accounts and enjoys spending late nights in various forums and discussion groups.\n\nInformation Three: Has done some research on disguise techniques and will personally step in to gather information when necessary."
},
	[47431]={ language="[Weekly Report]\nSender: Raven\nSent: November 6th, 11:30 PM\n\nThis is Raven.\n\nAs you expected, the Joshburg government has dispatched agents in three groups to Lissugen, located at xx Hotel, xx Tavern, and xx Country Club.\nAccording to the plan, I've set up surveillance spots in advance.\nThe informant list has been updated; we lost the deputy administrator at the city library, but gained two newsboys and an air conditioner repairman.\nAs per your instruction, I checked on the loudmouth bartender, and indeed, he was secretly selling second-hand info to the Southern Family. This has been promptly cut off.\n\nIn the social circle, the Finance Minister's daughter still hasn't decided on a dance partner, with the Southern Family's eldest son, the new district judge, and the Burksomi Investment Bureau director all courting her.\nFamily matters...\nBusiness matters...\nVoid domain matters...\nInternational trends...\n\nPS: Next week, there's an advancement support talk at the school that requires a guardian's attendance. My parents can't make it back from their Selevie research trip, so I'm hoping the Boss can attend in their place.\nNote: Just showing up will do.\nReport complete.\n\n——————————————\nApproval: Request granted. However, next month the Boss's fieldwork hours must be compensated with double overtime pay."
},
	[47432]={ language="Information One: Follows the strange rule of [buy one get one]—meaning when someone buys a piece of Information at the Dreams Consult, they also have to give a piece of Information to the Dreams Consult.\n\nInformation Two: Surprisingly lacks in life skills, which is one of the few characteristics of coming from a large family."
},
	[47433]={ language="It's a widely known but unspoken fact on the Taino Star that the Newcastle family profits from war.\n\nHowever, there's no evidence in any available records of the Newcastle family's involvement in arms trading—in fact, their main businesses include pharmaceuticals, construction materials, and logistics, all essential for people's wellbeing. This is because when war occurs, the demand for these goods sharply increases.\n\nTherefore, the Newcastle family's curriculum includes not only business but also history—they believe that human history is a history of warfare. The Newcastle family isn't interested in how wars end, only in how they start.\n\nIn such a family, Typhenie is an anomaly.\n\nShe despises the act of profiting amidst ruins, especially when her own family is behind the wars creating those ruins.\n\nWhen she received an opportunity that was ostensibly for training but was actually more like exile, she promptly distanced herself from her cold-blooded relatives and headed to Lissugen to take over Dreams Consult.\n\nShe has always believed the Newcastle family needs to change—they can't live off chaos anymore. Instead, they must use Information as a weapon to subtly influence the world.\n\nAll this is for peace.\n\nPeace isn't a harmonious utopia—conflicts and disputes have been around since humanity's birth on earth. Rather than trying to eliminate them, it's better to tame them—control means balance, and balance means peace.\n\nThis is something Typhenie can dedicate her life to pursuing."
},
	[47434]={ language="Information One: She's received countless death threats but remains unharmed, which adds a layer of mystery to her skills.\n\nInformation Two: She likes to overcharge regular customers, secretly raising prices in collaborations, but always makes them feel like they're getting a good deal."
},
	[47435]={ language="Real Name: Teresie Kagame\nIdentity: Employee of the chain maid Cafe—[Dorothy Maid Cafe]\nInterests: Researching various maid skills, passionate about learning different abilities"
},
	[47436]={ language="It's said that when Core first interviewed at Dorothy's Maid Cafe, she almost didn't make it because she spilled coffee on a customer. It was the customer who personally explained to the manager, Dorothy, and assured her that the coffee spill wasn't Core's fault, allowing her to stay. Of course, being able to make a great cup of coffee was one of the reasons she was kept.\n\nSome old staff recall that when Core first arrived, she wasn't as outgoing as she is now. Although she was always eager to work back then, she would constantly be aware of her surroundings, as if worried about something. Her smiles seemed somewhat absent-minded, like instinctual responses. Once, a regular customer tried to joke with Core by quietly calling her from behind, and Core jumped, visibly startled. However, even with that reaction, Core immediately apologized to the customer for her overdrive response. Fortunately, this didn't last long, and Core soon adjusted to life in the cafe, no longer always tense.\n\nCore seems to have no service experience, yet she is passionate about it.\n\nAt first, even when the manager only assigned her tasks like wiping tables and carrying plates, Core took them on with utmost seriousness, even moving awkwardly due to her nerves, which amused everyone present.\n\nTo make up for her shortcomings, Core would always be the first to arrive at the shop every day, willingly taking on the cleaning duties—even if other staff had to redo them while she wasn't paying attention. Luckily, everyone didn't mind at all, and they adored the eager, earnest young woman, willing to give her enough time to grow."
},
	[47437]={ language="Information One: Her favorite book is [The Maid's Work Manual].\n\nInformation Two: She has no experience in the kitchen, but she's a foodie.\n\nInformation Three:she has a collection of various uniforms at home—not just maid outfits."
},
	[47438]={ language="1. [The Maid's Work Manual]: 4th edition, shows obvious signs of perusal.\n\n2. Maid Outfits: A very complete range of styles, and each style has two sets, one for wearing, one for collection.\n\n3. Various Coffee-related Items: including but not limited to brewing supplies, premium coffee beans, and various beautiful coffee cups.\n\n4. Bunny-shaped Accessories: A very complete range of styles, similarly purchased in pairs, one to wear, one to collect.\n\n5. Cute little pocket watch: Although it looks a bit old, the surface has no scratches or dirt, it's clearly well cherished."
},
	[47439]={ language="Information One: When Core first started her part-time job, she would occasionally be late. Later, the manager of the store she worked at gave her a small pocket watch, and she never was late again.\n\n\nInformation Two: Because she's busy and doesn't have time for proper meals, she fills the storage space of her bunny robot Phoebe with snacks.\n\nInformation Three: In her free time, she visits other maid cafes to experience their service and always writes a report. She has quite a thick stack of reports now."
},
	[47440]={ language="Due to the regular duties of fulfilling AIMBS Operator tasks, Core often needs to request leave from the café. But regardless of how urgent the task is, Core always ensures a smooth work transition at the café, with only one exception.\n\nIt's said that during that time, some distinguished guests arrived and specifically asked for Core. However, upon briefly encountering them, she awkwardly escaped without greeting anyone. The manager realized her absence and could not contact her, causing concern among everyone for two days until Core reappeared safely on the third day.\n\nRumor has it that those distinguished guests claimed to be from the Selevie Gonzaga family, having heard their old friend Core had been seen here and came to visit. However, they seemed to have some disdain for the profession of [maid,] showing some scorn that Core was working [in such a place.]\n\nRumors quickly spread within the café regarding Core, such as that the young lady from the Selevie family was out experiencing life, had offended nobility and was exiled to Uzyanta, or had been banished from her family for liking maid outfits. These baseless speculations were soon brushed off by the manager. Core denied the [experiencing life] rumor to the manager, affirming she is very serious about her maid duties and hopes to earn everyone's recognition.\n\nThe manager did not overly criticize her and even clarified that Core had no connection with those guests.\n\nIn short, although this new employee seems to have her secrets and needs improvement in work abilities, her current work attitude is very dedicated, she gets along well with colleagues, and her service satisfaction is extremely high. She is a rising star at the Dorothy Maid Cafe.\n\nThe new employee at Dorothy Maid Cafe—Core—is working hard today, striving towards becoming an excellent maid."
},
	[47441]={ language="Information One: Very sensitive to caffeine, can't sleep after drinking coffee. However, still makes and drinks own brewed coffee for its delicious taste, leading to sleepless nights.\n\nInformation Two: When unable to sleep, she hums lullabies to herself. She can hum lullabies from various places, often lull other colleagues to sleep, but it doesn't seem to work for herself."
},
	[47442]={ language="Teresie:\n\nLong time no see, how's it going in Uzyanta?\n\nWhen I saw your name on the new Members list sent from the Uzyanta branch a while ago, everyone at the store was in disbelief, thinking it was just a coincidence with someone having the same name. But when we pulled up the file photo, it turned out to be you. I hesitated for a while before writing you this letter, but figured since you chose to work at the Uzyanta branch, you probably aren't bothered by that incident anymore. Of course, the most important reason is that I really miss you, so here's the letter.\n\nAfter that incident, we didn't get a chance to ask what happened before you hurriedly left the store and never came back. We occasionally picked up bits and pieces from customers, and guessed that some unfavorable rumors circulated in your circle. We heard you locked yourself at home, not going out or seeing anyone, and we were all worried, wanting to do something for you but couldn't find a way in. We tried asking regular customers to explain the situation in your circle, but they could only shake their heads, powerless against those rumors.\n\nYour father came to the store as a customer. It was clear he was very uncomfortable with the store's environment but was making an effort to adapt. He sat by the window all afternoon and only approached me in the evening to reveal his identity. He asked a lot of questions about [maids,] and also about your time at the store.\n\nI wasn't sure if I was doing the right thing, but I told him everything honestly: from our acquaintance, to how you liked making coffee for us in your spare time, to that one incident… He seemed regretful, feeling he didn't know or care for you enough. I apologized for that incident, but he actually thanked us for looking after you. When I inquired about your situation, he simply said not to worry, he would take care of you.\n\nLater, when the store wasn't so busy, I planned to visit you at the address you gave me, only to hear first that you had left Selevie. Though sad to see you go, we all thought it was good for you to live more freely somewhere else, and judging by your evaluation at the branch, things are indeed going well. It's wonderful that past troubles aren't bothering you anymore.\n\nI've written so much that the paper's nearly full, but there's still more to say. I'll wait until I travel to the Uzyanta branch next week to talk more. Looking forward to seeing you again!\n\nAnya, Manager of Selevie Main Store in Dolice Maid Cafe"
},
	[47443]={ language="Information One: She cleans her room to distract herself when feeling down.\n\nInformation Two: Although reluctant to admit it, Core doesn't mind violence, and might even... like it."
},
	[47444]={ language="Real Name: Gomia Holmheim\nIdentity: Operator under Lissugen Branch of Leistance Security Bureau\nInterests: Engaging in engineering research, creating mechanical gadgets"
},
	[47445]={ language="Holmheim Toy Store is quite famous in Foden City; if a kid doesn't have one or two toys handcrafted by Mr. Volker Holmheim, they lose status at school.\n\nThis situation arises not only because Mr. Volker's craftsmanship is extraordinary, creating toys that are intricate, fun, and beautiful, loved by both children and adults, but also because he prices each of his creations appropriately, offering affordable options for kids and more luxurious ones for adults.\n\nAs Mr. Volker's daughter, Gomia is used to the envious looks from her peers, as she owns every toy in the store, even the latest models not yet released—generous Gomia always shares toys with her classmates, unfazed by occasional damage, and when encountering kids from poor families, she often gives toys away without hesitation.\n\nBesides, Gomia often voluntarily repairs damaged toys for others—regardless of whether they came from her family's shop.\n\nMaybe this was the moment Gomia first realized the joy of using her [craft] to bring happiness to others."
},
	[47446]={ language="Information One: Doesn't like eating coriander.\n\nInformation Two: Enjoys chugging Energy drinks; claims it feels as satisfying as machines gulping down oil.\n\nInformation Three: Has been teased for always smelling like engine oil and is very conscious of it; now, it's no longer an issue."
},
	[47447]={ language="1. Combination Toolbox: Contains dozens of tools, capable of handling repair needs in most situations, a collection Gomia is proud of.\n\n2. Children's Tool Set: A birthday gift Gomia received at age 7, quickly used to dismantle all the large appliances at home.\n\n3. Engineering Goggles: Effectively protect the eyes from glare and sparks, though just an ordinary product on the market, surprisingly suitable for Gomia."
},
	[47448]={ language="Information One: Not good at saving money, will buy various interesting gadgets.\n\nInformation Two: Serves as the communication bridge between the Engineering and Research departments at Lissugen branch, quite popular across all departments.\n\nInformation Three: Believes big is good, more is beautiful, and appreciates the romance of giant ships and cannons."
},
	[47449]={ language="Though born in Foden City, Gomia isn't really an Uzyanta native—her parents hail from the northern Burksomi. When mentioning Burksomi, one must talk about Divinelight Heavy Tech, the mega industrial group located on the Frozen Plains, known as the heart of Burksomi.\n\nAs skilled artisans from Burksomi, the Holheim couple was often teased by neighbors as former employees of Shenguang Heavy Industry. In response, they'd simply smile nonchalantly and say their little gadgets couldn't compare with Burksomi's heavy industry.\n\nDespite that, Gomia's innate talent in mechanics wasn't destined to be buried in [little gadgets.] At the age of 10, she excelled in science and engineering, skipping grades to enter Uzyanta's top academic institution—Uzyanta Royal College—and completed all undergraduate courses in a year and a half.\n\nAfter graduation, Gomia followed her mentor's advice and headed to the emerging city of Lissugen in Yosephburg Union, embarking on a double master's degree at Lissugen University.\n\nFollowing two years at Lissugen University, Gomia accepted recruitment from Leistance's Lissugen branch and became an AIMBS Operator."
},
	[47450]={ language="Information One: Not very good at using the internet, will seek Yuanya's help when needing to handle internet issues.\n\nInformation Two: Skilled at making various small toys, very famous in the handmade toy community."
},
	[47451]={ language="Whether it's at Uzyanta Royal College, Lissugen University, or even in Leistance, Gomia stands out—a rarity among female mechanical researchers, even in an era where AIMBS technology has been developing for decades.\n\nFrom an unrecognized rookie to the lab's favorite, and now with her own studio, Gomia has proven her worth step by step through her actions.\n\nBut that's not enough.\n\nGomia always believes that while she can create some [gadgets,] her work on Crystal technology is mere [improvement,] not [innovation.] She needs to be personally involved in missions and face human threats to discover real needs. Serving as both an AIMBS intern and an engineering technician, she is destined to put in more effort and action.\n\nFortunately, the cheerfulness of life in Uzyanta and the tenacity she inherited from Burksomi have helped Gomia overcome every challenge. Given time, she is sure to become a pillar of Leistance."
},
	[47452]={ language="Information One: Adds various [improvements] to other Operators' Crystal Weapons based on self-assessment, but whether these improvements are useful is hard to say...\n\nInformation Two: Has a self-modified motorcycle, but it has never hit the road because she has no driver's license."
},
	[47453]={ language="Full Name: Karentilo Donova\nIdentity: Burksomi Arctic Science Expedition Team Member\nInterests: Talking with people, reading environmental reports"
},
	[47454]={ language="Karentilo's talkative nature seemed to have been ingrained in her from a very young age.\n\nThe ice field has always lacked entertainment options, and the scientific expedition team members can only chat casually around the heat source stove after a day's work. Compared to Karentilo's family who have been stationed in the Arctic for a long time, the expedition members from all over the world obviously have more interesting things to share.\n\nBut the curious Karentilo won't be satisfied with just being a listener. Whether it's customs from various countries, fanciful legends, or anecdotes from that century-old war, anything that piques Karentilo's interest will be subjected to her endless questioning. And the enthusiastic elders are always happy to answer Karentilo's inquiries.\n\nIn this environment, Karentilo has become a language expert, in addition to her native Burksomi and Joshburg common languages; she is also fluent in at least seven other languages and dialects. Every newcomer to the research base is amazed by Karentilo's linguistic abilities (and her desire to communicate), so much so that chatting with young Karentilo has become the best way to quickly integrate into the scientific expedition team.\n\nThis characteristic has naturally been brought by Karentilo to Leistance. With seamless communication and full of topics, she was quickly dubbed the [Burksomi Loudspeaker,] which made Karentilo feel very proud (Ling: not exactly a compliment).\n\nThe only thing that troubles Karentilo is that she seems to easily get acclimatization issues on the Leistance mothership, accustomed to the extreme icy weather. Whenever she unfortunately gets a [heat cold,] her swollen throat leads to the tragic situation of being voiceless, which is not uncommon.\n\nAfter experiencing the discomfort of not being able to speak smoothly, Karentilo fully leveraged her gifts and advantages, quickly mastering a new skill—sign language.\n\n[Now there really won't be any situation where I can't communicate!] \n\nKarentilo thought to herself.\n\nSo the next time she caught a cold, Karentilo even forgot about her temporary physical discomfort and was excited to prepare for a big [chat] session.\n\nBut she seemed to forget that communication is always a two-way street, and it can only happen if both parties know sign language.\n\nAs the only AIMBS Operator who knows sign language on the entire mothership, Karentilo, while suffering from a cold, still couldn't chat with others smoothly."
},
	[47455]={ language="Information One: Always carry snacks and jerky to share with new friends or stray animals right away.\n\nInformation Two: Surprisingly good at handling spicy food.\n\nInformation Three: A ski expert, able to master any skiing equipment, whether it's a snowboard or skis."
},
	[47456]={ language="1. Snack Bag: A bag filled with chocolate and jerky, perfect for a quick energy boost. Also handy for handing out candy as a friendly gesture when meeting new people.\n\n2. Faux Fur Shawl: More than keeping you warm, it provides a comforting psychological feeling. Karentilo actively promotes renewable materials over natural fur and leads by example.\n\n3. Animal Ear Goggles: They block the glare from ice reflections and can be used as binoculars. The decorative faux animal ears might help blend into animal groups... probably."
},
	[47457]={ language="Information One: Really loves animals, but she's naturally cat-proof, which really bothers her.\n\nInformation Two: Very upset after hearing the rumor [In the Arctic, people rarely bathe, only occasionally use snow to wipe the body.]\n\nInformation Three: Afraid of heat, the air conditioner in her room is on all year round."
},
	[47458]={ language="...Static...Static...Static...\n\n??: Testing, testing. Karentilo, you try it too.\nKarentilo: Testing~ No problem. What is this, Dad?\nDad: It's a universal answering machine. Today is Karentilo's first day leaving the research base with Dad, and according to the rules, anyone stepping onto the ice field must wear it.\nKarentilo: Ice field? Wow, I finally get to go to the ice field! It's been my lifelong dream!\nDad: What lifelong? You're only eight years old...\n...Static...Strong wind...Static...Static...\n\nKarentilo: Dad, where are you? Dad!\nKarentilo: So cold... Oh no!\nKarentilo: Ouch, ouch, ouch. This is...a cave? Furry...what is this?\nKarentilo: It's Snow Fox babies! So cute! But you're so skinny. Oh, I have some jerky here, want to try?\nKarentilo: Don't all lick my face, hehe, it's stinky.\nKarentilo: It's warm...so comfy.\n...Static...Static...Static...\n\nDad: Karentilo! Karentilo! Are you okay?\nDad: This is...a Snow Fox den?\nDad: Looks likethey're physically fine, just exhausted and sleeping. Thank goodness...\n...Static...Strong wind...Static...Static...\n\nKarentilo: Dad, Snow Fox mom is here!\nDad: She's already...frozen, with meat still in her mouth meant for the kids.\nKarentilo: Quick, quick, save her!\nDad: Let me take care of her.\nKarentilo: She's awake! Go find your kids. Huh, is this for me? No need, give it all to your children.\n...Static...Static...Static...\n\nDad: Seals die from hunting, ice bears lose their ice.\nDad: We're just like Snow Foxes, struggling and striving to survive on the ice field.\nDad: That's the beauty of life.\nKarentilo: Dad, I want to be a Snow Fox.\n————[Recording of Team Member Karentilo's First Ice Field Activity]"
},
	[47459]={ language="Information One: Always tirelessly promoting the use of renewable materials instead of animal fur, and scoffing at expensive fur coats.\n\nInformation Two: Regularly setting an example by collecting discarded plastic products, but accidentally sparked rumors of being poor due to collecting scrap."
},
	[47460]={ language="Vlog [About My Scientific Exploration on the Ice Field! VOL.60 [Final Episode!]] \n\nUploaded by: Snow Fox _Official\nViews: 1.8 million\nLikes: 230k\nSubscribers: 1 million\n\nHello everyone, this is Karentilo from code name Snow Fox! I'm part of the Arctic Science Expedition Team, living on the ice field long-term!\n\nThanks to everyone for your companionship and encouragement all along, this series has finally reached its 60th episode, thank you!\n\nAs the title says, this episode is the final one.\n\nFirst, I want to explain why I stopped posting for a while.\nIt all started with an accident. Originally, the scientific team thought it was just a regular storm until the Burksomi Navy Task Force arrived at the base, informing us of a breach in the arctic Skyborne Barriers. What followed was Anchor Space and Shogger.\n\nFortunately! The Task Force repelled Shogger, and the scientific team suffered no casualties, which is wonderful!\n\nHowever, the unfortunate part is that the creatures on the ice fields were invaded by Void Particles and mutated, necessitating biochemical processing. I will record every animal companion who left due to this in the cloud database.\n\nThis got me thinking about the current threats facing the ice fields and the road ahead.\n\nLong story short! To protect the ice fields and the base in the long term, I, Karentilo, made an important decision—to become a new version of myself.\n\nIn the upcoming days, Karentilo will leave the Arctic scientific base and go to Leistance for training.\n\nThis means that for a while, I will stop updating.\n\nSo, let's use this episode to bid farewell to the old Karentilo!\n\nPlease look forward to the new presence of Snow Fox·Karentilo!\n\nGoodbye!\n\n(All proceeds from this video will still be donated to the Global Animal Rescue Shelter Association!)"
},
	[47461]={ language="Information One: Remembers every partner's birthday and preferences.\n\nInformation Two: Likes all fluffy things, except spiders."
},
	[47462]={ language="Real Name: Cassolie Heracles\nIdentity: Leistance Security Bureau Auxiliary Staff\nInterests: Making handmade crafts for kids."
},
	[47463]={ language="[Cassolie, why are you bringing a camera out here?]\n\n[I promised the little daughter of the old Sui family to take some photos of wild rabbits for her.] \n\nCassolie was walking in the middle of the hunting party, answering her father's questions while carefully carrying a customized crossbow over a broken dry branch—it was light yet a bit cumbersome for Cassolie, who was only 10. \n\n[You actually made friends with the Sui family's little daughter? Isn't that girl avoiding everyone?] A clan uncle from the front turned back, looking at Cassolie in surprise.\n\n[She just ignores things and people that don't interest her. Actually, she's very curious about things outside the city. Dad, shall we bring her along next time?] \n\n[I'm afraid not, Sui is a city person, firmly refusing to step out of the city. If you take his daughter out of the city, he'll take us to court.] \n\n[Alright... Then I'll take more photos for little Sui, we should be about there, right? I remember seeing it here last time...]\n\nCassolie's father suddenly reached out to stop her, gesturing for silence, the whole hunting party halted altogether, watching fifty meters ahead. \n\n[Squeak squeak—] A slight sound accompanied by a faint bloody smell drifted in on the breeze.\n\nCassolie's pupils shrank suddenly, a bad feeling began to rise within her. She tried to step forward but was gently held back by her father's hand. \n\nThe whole hunting party held its breath for a moment, then saw a pair of eerie green eyes under a claw-like giant tree—a large wild wolf, laying under the tree, licking the blood off its paws with satisfaction.\n\n[Cassolie, you come—] [Mmm...]\n\nCassolie mounted the crossbow, aiming it in the wolf's direction, placing the arrow.\n\nHer breath was somewhat quick, fingers set on the trigger, at this moment, a hand settled on her shoulder.\n\n[Stay calm, breathe smoothly, don't grip the trigger too hard.] \n\n[Aim for the brow, show some mercy,] her father's words reached Cassolie's ear, she nodded, and her finger pulled the trigger.\n\nWith a soft sound, 10-year-old Cassolie Hercules claimed her first prey of the day—"
},
	[47464]={ language="Information One: A very patient and gentle big sister, approachable, and the kids love being close to her.\n\nInformation Two: Likes making handmade crafts for kids to play with, especially paper cranes.\n\nInformation Three: Possesses excellent wilderness survival skills and is said to survive for months in the Wilderness with just a small knife."
},
	[47465]={ language="1. Colored Paper: Ordinary colored paper, often used by Cassolie for crafting paper art, loved by kids.\n\n2. Family Crest: The crest representing the Heracles Family, made of precious metal, engraved with the family's symbol—a large bird.\n\n3. Exploration Kit: A personally selected outdoor adventure and survival kit that meets most outdoor needs."
},
	[47466]={ language="Information One: Her family totem is a large bird called the peregrine falcon, symbolizing freedom.\n\nInformation Two: Very protective, anything unfavorable to her family and friends will be fiercely dealt with.\n\nInformation Three: Has great people skills, almost always makes new friends wherever she goes."
},
	[47467]={ language="[Don't mess around, focus and watch your surroundings. There could be danger anytime outside the city, so stay alert.]\n\nHearing the playful noise behind her, Cassolie turned her head and warned the two young ones causing a ruckus.\n\nThe two half-grown kids quickly separated. One stuck out his tongue and whispered, [Cassolie, you didn't even turn around but somehow knew we were messing around.]\n\n[Ears can hear,] Cassolie said with a smile, pointing to her ear. When she saw the two kids behaving properly, she turned back around.\n\n[You're starting to act more and more like a future clan leader,] Cassolie's clan uncle teased behind her. [But considering ranks, you should call those two troublemakers uncle. What's with the way you're talking to your uncle?]\n\n[My father specifically told me safety first when leading,] Cassolie replied calmly, unfazed. [Regardless of rank and age, safety is most important. We're getting close to the forest edge, so please stay alert too.]\n\n[Yes, yes, future clan leader—huh?] Her uncle suddenly paused, then quickly turned, staring at the half-human height bushes on the left.\n\n[What's wrong?] Cassolie, sensing something was off, stopped and looked over.\n\n[Report...] one of the kids who was advised to be cautious raised his hand. [I accidentally flung my bracelet over there while playing...]\n\nCassolie let out a sigh of relief, [So that's it, you gave us a scare. It's okay, I'll help you get it back, but no more fooling around like this...] As she spoke, she started walking over.\n\n[Something's not right—] Her uncle suddenly pulled Cassolie back. Cassolie looked confused, about to ask, when suddenly a shadow darted from the bushes, mouth wide open lunging at her.\n\n[It's a mutant wolf!] someone exclaimed from the Ravend.\n\nCassolie's crossbow was useless in close combat. She wanted to dodge but realized the kids behind her were inexperienced—\n\nIn a split second, she decided to take the hit.\n\nBut before she could move, her uncle pushed her aside, swinging his hammer with precision and striking the lunging Mutant. They tumbled to the side, fighting fiercely.\n\nAhead of the hunting team, amidst the dim shadows, pairs of blue-green eyes glowed in the darkness.\n\nThe youngsters had never seen such a sight, screams erupted, and some couldn't resist running back the way they came.\n\n[This isn't going to work...] an uncle grabbed a runaway kid back into the group, frowning at Cassolie. [With them here, we can't fight properly. Later, we old geezers will clear a path, you guide them back to the temporary camp and wait for us there.]\n\n[But...] Cassolie wanted to protest, knowing the danger for those staying behind with so many Wolf Hunters around, but the sight of the terrified kids reminded her this was the best solution.\n\n[I understand.] Cassolie took a long look at the uncles battling the Wolf Hunters, then turned around. [Once the uncles clear a path to the southwest, everyone follow me and run forward. No fighting, no stopping, uncles and I will clear all threats.]\n\n[Yes...] The youngsters' voices trembled but were full of determination and trust.\n\n[Everyone, now, run!]"
},
	[47468]={ language="Information One: Very caring and nurturing, others can rely on her, which makes Cassolie very happy.\n\nInformation Two: Excellent cooking skills, often cooks for her younger siblings."
},
	[47469]={ language="[Cassolie, it's getting late. Let's leave the remaining missions for tomorrow.]\n\n[It's okay, Father. You go ahead and rest. I'll handle the rest.] Cassolie replied without turning to face her father, keeping her head buried in the screen.\n\n[Cassolie, something's off with you lately.] Her father pulled up a chair and sat opposite Cassolie, [Talk to me. Are you still blaming yourself for the team outing that got hit by the Mutant?]\n\n[Some uncles got hurt to different extents, and Uncle Anda even more so...] Cassolie choked up a bit, and there was a hint of tears in her eyes.\n\n[I've told you before, none of the scouting teams sensed anything wrong, and your response afterwards was the best possible solution, even upon review.] Her father sighed softly, [You don't need to stay in this self-blame anymore.]\n\n[I understand. But it still takes some time to let go of these feelings.]\n\n[Perhaps we don't have much time left... That Mutant attack might not have been an accident.]\n\n[What do you mean?] Cassolie stood up from her chair in shock, looking at her father in surprise.\n\n[Not just our family, many teams outside the city were attacked by Mutants...]\n\n[You mean...]\n\n[You've heard of that prophecy from a hundred years ago, right?]\n\n['A hundred years later, disaster will once again befall the continent'?]\n\n[Exactly. Although everyone dismisses it as fear-mongering rumors, lately… it's becoming more unsettling.]\n\n[If that day really comes...]\n\nCassolie touched the crossbow on the shelf with a somber look. [That day when we encountered the Mutant, I thought, if only I were an AIMBS Operator... with such power, I could protect everyone, ensure everyone's safe retreat...]\n\nHer father was silent for a moment, then raised his head and looked into Cassolie's eyes, [Cassolie, do you want to become an AIMBS Operator?]\n\n[…] Cassolie hesitated, [But I can't pass the national AIMBS Remodel test...]\n\n[There's a place that might be worth a try...]\n\n[Where?]\n\n[Leistance Security Bureau.] Her father also stood up from his chair, [Some people from there have talked with us before, and if you go there, it might be possible.]\n\n[Go to Leistance...?]\n\n[Will you miss home?]\n\n[No, just... leaving at such a critical time might put pressure on the family...]\n\n[I can manage.] Her father smiled, looking at Cassolie, [Going to Leistance, besides gaining power, you'll also get first-hand access to related information. If things really unfold as that prophecy from a hundred years ago predicted… you will be our family's last hope.]\n\n[…] Cassolie lowered her head in thought, then looked up with determination in her eyes.\n\n[I understand, Father.]"
},
	[47470]={ language="Information One: Every day there's a set time to contact family, but she often shares good news not the bad, to avoid worrying them.\n\nInformation Two: As soon as she encounters peppers and onions, she starts crying uncontrollably, and it takes at least half an hour for the symptoms to gradually improve."
},
	[47471]={ language="Real Name: Olivia Scheffel\nIdentity: Pioneer Cavalry of 3rd Kroward Cavalry Legion\nInterests: Executing tasks, working, exercising, learning to cook"
},
	[47472]={ language="The girl from Hararo, pure, kind, always full of energy and eager to help others, is everyone's first impression of Olivia.\n\nYou can see Olivia anywhere in the cavalry unit, even late at night, there's a high chance you'll find her in the Tutorial room, doing the same intense physical training she does during the day.\n\nAlways energetic and too lively to ever take a break, this is the second impression her colleagues in the cavalry have of Olivia. Because of this, most people in the unit really like this girl from the old industrial district. Some veterans nearing retirement even feel a familial fondness for Olivia.\n\n[It's been a long time since the cavalry had such a young person. These newcomers can't really chat with us old folks, but little Olivia always brings her homemade stews to drink with us, gathering around the campfire to tell us stories of her hometown.]\n\n[And her mother, every time she talks about her mother, this kid lights up—honestly, Hararo is really a small place, just an ordinary industrial town. Olivia's mother is simply an ordinary Kroward woman, over fifty, who's never left the town, but to raise someone like Olivia, I think she's truly remarkable, hahaha...]"
},
	[47473]={ language="Information One: Exercising day and night, her overly abundant energy once frightened colleagues.\n\nInformation Two: When first joining the cavalry, was called [Country Girl from Hararo] due to exuding a village girl vibe.\n\nInformation Three: Always talks about how great her hometown is, but hardly anyone listens; she doesn't mind."
},
	[47474]={ language="1. Cavalry Regiment Flag: The flag wrapped around the cavalry lance, a testament to the vanguard cavalry, and Olivia's pride.\n\n2. Earthy Hair Conditioner: Handmade conditioner from Olivia's hometown, used to care for her long hair.\n\n3. [Sluwaf]: A homemade spirit from Olivia's hometown, known for its spiciness, potency, and high alcohol content, one of Olivia's favorite [drinks].\n\n4. Small Flower Accessory: A little accessory given to Olivia by her mother before joining the cavalry regiment."
},
	[47475]={ language="Information One: [The Enthusiastic Musclehead] is what others secretly call Olivia, but it's not a derogatory term.\n\nInformation Two: Seems to have endless energy, but Olivia actually loves taking naps.\n\nInformation Three: Very strong endurance, able to move 30 kilograms of goods by hand for five kilometers even before becoming an AIMBS Operator."
},
	[47476]={ language="Within Kroward, there are countless towns and villages, established around Crystal ores or industrial facilities—relying on mining growth means eventually facing decline, which is the reality for these towns and villages, and for Kroward itself.\n\nOlivia was born in one of these towns. With her background, she was supposed to stay in the old industrial area her whole life—the town was her everything. But she passed the nominal [cavalry assessment] and became an active vanguard cavalry member at the Kroward border, which, for a village girl, is indeed a [miracle.]\n\nWhen Olivia first joined the cavalry, she was a bit uneasy and reserved—everything here felt so unfamiliar to her. However, this uneasy feeling only lasted for three days and was ended completely by a drinking party: Olivia drank down eight other cavalry members and took home the first-place prize. Although the party was abruptly ended when discovered by an officer and everyone was punished, Olivia built a reputation in the cavalry. To this group of drink-loving Kroward cavalry members, the fact that a girl could outdrink them was enough to dispel doubts and rumors.\n\nWhen it comes to lifestyle, Olivia's habits can be described as slapdash. Fellow AIMBS Operators have advised Olivia to be mindful of her image as a girl. Olivia appreciates their good intentions and tried to apply makeup, but it was best described as a disaster; the dress she bought was only worn once and felt far less comfortable than her uniform... So, please try not to discuss ladylike looks with Olivia—it will surely leave her downcast."
},
	[47477]={ language="Information One: Used to be a tomboy with short hair, but at her mother's request, she grew it long and has kept it that way till now.\n\nInformation Two: Although called a cavalryman, her riding skills are average, and she often chooses to fight on foot."
},
	[47478]={ language="...Is it recording? Okay, I'm starting...\n…\n…Yes, I definitely think it's necessary to re-examine the information related to Kroward.\n\nFrom the information revealed during this evacuation event, the situation in Kroward is on the brink of explosion— the conflict between the nobles and the workers is irreparable, and the impact of new technology on old industrial areas has brought more chaos and disorder.\nIf Kroward falls into civil conflict due to this, it will significantly increase the difficulty of executing our tasks within its borders.\n…\nWe don't have the authority to interfere in Kroward's internal affairs, but that doesn't mean I have a pessimistic outlook for Kroward's future—because young people like Olivia have emerged—especially within the country's most important military forces, which means Kroward's new blood hasn't disappeared, they just need an opportunity to unleash the country's power again.\n…\nAs for Olivia's stance... I'm positive about it. The evacuation event made her mature quickly, and Leone's death made her aware of what she truly pursues. Her stance has never changed; we don't need to worry about her becoming a tool for others. Belief is something that keeps a person from losing their way, and Olivia has her own beliefs. I'm honored to Campaign alongside such a person.\n…\nYes, if there's a chance, I'd like to visit Kroward again to see her—I believe when we meet again, her smile will be brighter and purer.\n—Mission briefing recording by Lionblade after the evacuation event."
},
	[47479]={ language="Information One: She is easily satisfied by the kindness of others and will return even more kindness.\n\nInformation Two: Her singing voice is terrible..."
},
	[47480]={ language="Real Name: Unknown\nIdentity: Agent of Joshburg Central Council\nInterests: Reading, music appreciation, browsing on phone"
},
	[47481]={ language="[Since the end of the Shogger War, nearly a century has passed, and the [Surrogate] system has been adopted by all countries on Tyno Star. Through constant iterations and upgrades, AI in data form is more capable of receiving negative emotions transmitted from an AIMBS Operator compared to the human brain's deterioration and unpredictability. AI offers more development possibilities and, most importantly, its open-source Feature give users the right to Remodel themselves.]\n\n[Therefore, as the first country to use the [Surrogate] system, Joshburg must ensure it remains at the forefront of this technology.]\n\n[I sincerely hope you will agree to the implementation of the 'Deuteron' plan.]\n\n[The [Surrogate] is no longer mere technological advancement. Since humanity freed itself from the shackles of Leistance and the Star Council, the significance of AIMBS Operator has undergone a massive transformation, sir.]\n\n[The ten people on the list, they are all handpicked subjects who have experienced events with profound mental impacts.]\n\n[We must ensure that the AIMBS Operator of the parliament is stronger and more intimidating than others—after all these years, you should understand who Joshburg's real enemy is.]\n\n[Shogger... only Shogger.]\n\n— Confidential meeting records of the Joshburg Central Council."
},
	[47482]={ language="Information One: Likes collecting records and has her own audio appreciation room.\n\nInformation Two: Among the collected records, Joshburg is the least, Burksomi and Lod Coalition are about the same, with the most.\n\nInformation Three: Has diverse music tastes but doesn't like RAP music."
},
	[47483]={ language="1. Glasses: Non-prescription, just plain frames, Lycosha has four or five pairs of the same style glasses.\n\n2. Monofilament: Lycosha's unique tool, not only for cutting but also for hanging, tugging, or... retrieving objects from a distance.\n\n3. Antique Pendant: A silver pendant that looks quite aged, carried by Lycosha, with the initials [L.M] engraved on it.\n\n4. Handmade Felt Doll: A handmade felt doll, a bit ugly but oddly charming, doesn't quite match Lycosha's style, yet she cherishes it."
},
	[47484]={ language="Information One: Occasionally says a few old-fashioned things when chatting with people.\n\nInformation Two: Surprisingly good at cooking, and sometimes spends half a day making a feast for herself on a whim.\n\nInformation Three: Familiar with some very old internet topics."
},
	[47485]={ language="■■■ Archive X0004-CT-6—\n[May 25, ■■■■, 02:33 AM]\n[Day 4, today's status: good。]\n[Conclusion: The individual ■■■■ has awakened, all bodily functions continue to operate normally, status is good, the first observation phase ends, can proceed to formal experiment。]\n■■■ Archive X0004-CT-17—\n[Day 116, today's status: good, but ■■ indicator did not meet standards, considering using ■■■■ and ■■■■ for enhancement。]\n■■■ Archive X0004-CT-44—\n[Day 322, ethical issue events occurred, between individual ■■■■ and individual ■■■■ resulted in ■■, eventually leading to ■■■■ happening—]\n■■■ Archive X0004-CT-112—\n[December 24, ■■■■, 01:16 PM。]\n[Day 6■■, ■■■■ indicator normal, ■■■ indicator normal, ■■ indicator overflow, will use ■■■ and ■■■■ for suppression and correction—]\n[Conclusion: Individual ■■■■ post-surgery recovery is good, can be put into testing。]\n(Massive gibberish)\n(Massive gibberish)\n■■■ Archive X0004-CT-343—\n[Day 7■■, evaluation of individual ■■■■ as follows, copied to ■■■■■■■■■■—]\n[Physical fitness: excellent, able to achieve excellent results in comprehensive physical tests。]\n[Combat skills: excellent, can use Campaign equipment freely and complete Combat Command。]\n[Combat will: good, may choose to relocate or execute the second plan when facing various predicaments。]\n[Team coordination: poor, has poor compatibility with partners, tends to complete tasks alone。]\n[Individual flaws: As a combat unit, this individual has no obvious flaws, all indicators are very excellent, but it is worth noting that this individual may enter Overdrive state during combat, in Overdrive state the individual tends to completely destroy targets, which may lead to undesirable effects when target preservation is needed, should avoid deploying them on such fronts。]\n(Massive gibberish)\n(Massive gibberish)\n■■■ Archive X0004-CT-604—\n[January 17, ■■■■, 07:06 AM。]\n[Day ■■■3, plan changes occur—]\n[Freeze ■■■■, destroy ■■■, ■■ and ■■, transfer individual ■■■■ to ■■■■■■, related data synchronized, work handed over。]\n[Conclusion: Individual ■■■■ functions normally, status is good, subsequent matters will be fully managed by ■■■, ■■■■ and ■ responsible, henceforth, ■■■ plan is terminated。]\n— Joshburg Central Think Tank, ■■■ plan record log"
},
	[47486]={ language="Information One: As a spy, she has mingled in the upper circles of multiple countries, is well-versed in various social etiquettes, and holds many different noble identities.\n\nInformation Two: She runs her own information network online, adhering to the principle of exchanging information for information."
},
	[47487]={ language="Lily Mauldor was born into a very traditional and conservative family in Uzyanta. She was raised to be a graceful lady, living up to her family's expectations by growing up as a well-behaved girl.\n\nBut when she hit puberty, Lily gradually realized there was a sadistic desire buried deep inside her—a desire that had taken root at some unknown time, occasionally whispering to her like a demon.\n\nInitially, Lily was terrified of this desire and sought ways to resolve it, seeking help from many but with little success, even worsening the problem. Her sadistic urges grew stronger, although she never expressed them outwardly, she felt she was losing control.\n\nTo address this issue, Lily decided to explore new possibilities in an unfamiliar world, breaking away from her family and leaving her familiar surroundings to do volunteer work in Joshburg, hoping her busy schedule would suppress her sadistic desires.\n\nAt nineteen, Lily found herself busy and fulfilled in Joshburg, volunteering at an educational institution. However, over time, she uncovered the true nature of the institution—it was part of a secret research project by the Joshburg government. The project's aim was to reform the AIMBS proxy system to [humanely] replace those deemed waste-linkers.\n\nAmidst a series of events whose truth was long lost, Lily volunteered for the research project. The initial instability of the reformed proxy system led to an incident where Lily lost control, killing everyone involved in the experiment and feeling—joy.\n\nAfter the incident, Lily was convicted of intentional harm and subjected to a body freeze sentence. Yet three years later, she was unfrozen as Experiment No. 4 in the improved AIMBS project known as [Deuteron].\n\nThe Deuterium Core project lasted years, with Lily undergoing numerous secondary remodel transformations and becoming one of only two successful products out of dozens of experiments. After the project was unexpectedly terminated, Lily's body was frozen again—her mind was now completely disconnected from her physical form, one of the most significant impacts from two remodel processes."
},
	[47488]={ language="Information One: As one of the first experimenters of the Surrogate system, Lycosha is actually much older than most AIMBS.\n\nInformation Two: Lycosha's profile in the Central Council is quite simple, with less than three senior officials knowing her true identity."
},
	[47489]={ language="Real Name: Dione Goya\nIdentity: Member of Zulu Mercenary Group\nInterests: Reciting poetry, telling legends, being close to nature"
},
	[47490]={ language="The beginning was a lonely land\nThe mother was a barren field\nFrom deep within, she shook with a gentle, unyielding call\n[From today, flowers and trees that embrace the sun will grow here]\n[Beasts and fish will be diverse, their destinies intertwined and merged]\n[There should be laughter, songs and dances, suffering and tears here]\nLife breaks through the soil from the mother's palm\nLike a flower, the first branches of a seed\nA baby's fresh cry comes from fingertips\nCreatures are nourished with the mother's flesh and blood, shoulders are mountains, hair strands are rivers\nBreath is the wind called [spring] in distinct seasons\nThose were the days before darkness eclipsed the sun and moon\nHere I sing to you this soon-to-be forgotten history...\n\n—— Dione's hymn to the Earth Mother [Creation Narrative]"
},
	[47491]={ language="Information One: Kids love her a lot and often ask her to tell stories or sing songs. \n\nInformation Two: Never gets angry, but has an aura that stops people from acting out. \n\nInformation Three: Highly talented in music, she has a unique classical style in playing compositions and reciting poetry."
},
	[47492]={ language="1. A book with Vintage Binding: Not a rubbing, but a rare pure handwritten book from this era, recording the bygone natural scenery—including plants, animals, and insects.\n\n2. Bone Flute: Made from an unknown animal's bone. Can produce simple, melodious tunes.\n\n3. Heavy Shield: Cast from unknown material, holds the power of life, seemingly embracing everything with its sturdy barrier, evoking thoughts of nature and the earth's vastness.\n\n4. A Poetry Collection: Records songs not belonging to this era."
},
	[47493]={ language="Information One: Has a strong ability to survive in the wild, almost knows everything about this land like the back of her hand.\n\nInformation Two: Often mentions Mother Earth, but is not keen on promoting her own sect.\n\nInformation Three: Seems to gather information from nature that others can't understand, and can even predict the timing of the next rainfall accurately."
},
	[47494]={ language="For those living in the fortress city, growing up in the wilderness is an incredible experience.\n\nThey might spend their entire lives within the city's strong walls without ever stepping out to see what has become of the earth, now shrouded in eternal night. No one mourns the plants and animals that have disappeared forever, even though the species preserved by the city are less than a tiny fraction of what existed before—after all, not everyone is a historian or a naturalist.\n\nLong-standing inequality in resources and living standards, along with the strange looks from city residents, often make the Wilderness dwellers struggle to cope—some grow angry, some become sad, and some fall into a fervent obsession. This is completely understandable; in fact, it's normal and reasonable.\n\nFew people can imagine that among the wilderness dwellers, there are people like Dione. She is calm and compassionate towards all humans. Some city folks don't like the way Dione looks at them: as if living in the city makes them seem pitiful.\n\nBut Dione simply feels that this land is not at its most beautiful time, and ordinary scenes from thousands of years ago now only exist in the hymns to the gods. In her lifetime, it's unlikely to return to such glory. Thus, both this world and the creatures living in it are worth a mournful sigh.\n\nDione is not a relic from the past; she was born in the wild, and thus has a chance to glimpse the traces of ancient times. As a result, she embarks on a journey of faith, treating it as her personal pilgrimage. She bears a sturdy shield, guarding all the weak, just as Mother Earth allows the smallest creatures to find their place in the ecosystem. On the battlefield, those around Dione almost represent [life.]\n\nDione never actively preaches; for her, nature has its own gravity. Those called by nature will naturally become her brothers and sisters. So, even if you can't quite understand what she's pursuing or what she believes in, as long as you truly enjoy the songs she sings and the stories she tells, that's the best you could hope for."
},
	[47495]={ language="Information One: Tech illiterate. Can't really use anything that's powered up.\n\nInformation Two: Doesn't like staying indoors for long periods and isn't fond of overdeveloped cities."
},
	[47496]={ language="Miss Dione is of course an indispensable part of the Zulu Mercenary Group.\n\nBut that's just my own opinion. Maybe to Miss Dione, we are just companions she met on her long journey. Yet we resonate so well: the ballads we sing, the tomes we hold, we strive to look back at the times gone by, unable to see the vanished splendor of nature... On many nights, the whole mercenary group listens by the campfire to her songs about the animals, plants, sun, moon, and stars that no longer exist, and we feel a shared familiarity and the ensuing overwhelming sadness.\n\nOften, Miss Dione gives off a... motherly vibe. Especially when she looks at you gently, as if she forgives all your mistakes, watching you until you grow and then move on... Does that sound strange? But that's truly how I feel. Even though she has a stern side sometimes—of course, I've never really seen it, no one has seen Miss Dione lose her temper. But you can vaguely feel that if something were to really make her angry, it would certainly be a major event...\n\nThe leader once mentioned that Miss Dione actually has a sword of her own. But we have never seen it. In combat, she always raises her sturdy shield, standing in front of everyone, and then uses the power of nature to heal our injuries. Honestly, even if I'm curious, I secretly hope that Miss Dione would never have to draw her sword. I have a feeling that would signify immense pain and sorrow... When Miss Dione removes those barriers that seem to block everything, they would crash down like a tidal wave, overwhelming anyone.\n\n—A member of Zulu Mercenary Group, who wishes to remain anonymous"
},
	[47497]={ language="Information One: Has their own schedule, reportedly following the pattern from when they could see the [sun,] working at sunrise and resting at sunset.\n\nInformation Two: Good at making soup, and it tastes great, but its appearance leaves much to be desired."
},
