	[78291]={ language="You and your team step into the edge of the Valor Desert. This was once one of the main battlefields where humanity fought bravely during the Shogger Invasion. Now, it has become a highly polluted war machine graveyard, with various mechanical wrecks buried in the endless sand. Your target is the area in the center of the Desert with the highest pollution level, where the wreckage of the super space battleship [Saladin] that fell during the great war is located."
},
	[78292]={ language="You advance deeper into the Desert. As the pollution level rise, the monsters become increasingly troublesome. Fortunately, you are not alone on the journey—the survivors who have lived in the Desert for generations offer you and your team much help, ensuring you are not isolated."
},
	[78293]={ language="[Saladin], the original ark-class space battleship flagship, fell here in the worldwide war known as the Shogger Invasion. Over two hundred years have passed, and today, it welcomes a new visitor—you are about to step into a history two hundred years old."
},
	[78294]={ language="The size of the [Saladin] far exceeds your expectations. Even after two hundred years of rust and weathering, its remnants are still as large as a town. You step inside, searching for any clues you might find, but the monsters will not let you easily find valuable information..."
},
	[78295]={ language="Can you make the long-deceased speak? That's probably impossible. But can the long-deceased warship wreckage speak? Unless you try, you'll never know. Target: [Saladin] core bridge."
},
	[78296]={ language="The [Saladin] No.4 power reactor has been activated. If it is not shut down in time, exceeding the critical point will turn this area into a void erosion region. There is no time, you must act urgently."
},
