	[80014]={ language="Unknown"
},
	[80015]={ language="A young nation that really encourages innovation and development, advocating for all measures beneficial to economic growth and technology development."
},
	[80016]={ language="Composed of Kroward, Liboselle, Hissrich, and four other small members, with diverse development within the Union."
},
	[80017]={ language="Home to some primitive villages"
},
	[80018]={ language="Located in the northern continent, rich in metal resources and developed heavy industry."
},
	[80019]={ language="Unlocked after obtaining Operator"
},
	[80020]={ language="Character"
},
	[80021]={ language="Item"
},
	[80022]={ language="A mysterious union on another continent, with entirely different research and techniques for studying Stellar Crystal than those used in the homeland."
},
	[80023]={ language="An international campaign agency established by Star Council, responsible for handling Shogger and various events triggered by Shogger."
},
	[80024]={ language="Includes Uzyanta, Vilatria, and Selevie, three countries with abundant natural Resource and Stellar Crystal Resource."
},
	[80025]={ language="Unknown Affiliation People"
},
	[80026]={ language="Sigil not yet unlocked"
},
	[80027]={ language="Recently, a series of abnormal events have occurred in the port city Lissugen, including communication failures and Mutant sightings. To investigate the truth, the Leistance Security Bureau Lissugen branch sent a request to headquarters—a young Linker and his partner Alicia are assigned the task, but little did they know, the mission begins with a plane crash..."
},
	[80028]={ language="The explosion at the Neoscope Building catches the attention of Lissugen's superiors in the Central Council in Joshburg. They believe it was done by an organization called [ULFT,] whose next target might be [Neoscope Park.] To deal with ULFT's threat, the Central Council dispatched an agent named Karanissa to assist, but no one expected another group to be active in Neoscope Park..."
},
	[80029]={ language="No one could have predicted that Neoscope Inc was behind the park incident, and Jools must be found and brought to justice. To capture Jools, Linker and Alicia head to an abandoned mine outside Lissugen, while the Central Council sends another agent named Lycosha to join the mission—unaware that deep in the mine, a terrifying entity is slowly awakening..."
},
	[80030]={ language="After barely escaping the mine alive and taking little time to rest, Linker learns of a new situation—the dangerous items recovered by the Coordinator Sect from the mine may have been transported back to Lissugen. To prevent possible dangers, Linker and Alicia must head to Lissugen's underground city—where they are greeted by the local force known as [Ant Tribe,] and possibly lurking ULFT and the Coordinator Order..."
},
	[80031]={ language="The incident in the underground city caused a severe impact, but it's not just the underground city that needs addressing now—some disturbances have appeared on the surface as well. As the last day of Lissugen's festival [Resurrection Day,] in the chaotic city of Lissugen, disasters are quietly growing..."
},
	[80032]={ language="The Skyborne Barriers base has been blown up, massive anchors appear in the sky, and a terrifying entity named [Scorpio] emerges from them, with Lissugen's destruction looming—only fifteen minutes remain to end it..."
},
