	[91101]={ language="Real Name: Dawalin \nIdentity: [Spirit Deer Priest] of the Sleipnir tribe\nInterests: Plant care, playing with small animals"
},
	[91102]={ language="For a long time, different countries have their own understanding of Shogger, Void Particles, and even AIMBS. Selevie, where Silvia lives, was famous long ago for its pristine and complete ecological environment. [Nature] was the first word Selevieans encountered as they grew up on this land. They built totems, established tribes, and developed their civilization within forests and swamps.\n[However, that history is so distant for present-day Selevie that many locals doubt whether vast forests and lakes really existed.]\n[That's understandable... Since the establishment of the fortress city and Skyborne Barriers, Selevie has joined the [Ring of Pledge], and must contribute to enjoy the protection of the Skyborne Barriers.]\n[What contribution? It's what I just mentioned—forests, lakes. See those artificial plants in the capital of Selevie? Without those things to embellish, the name Selevie would lose much of its significance.]\n—Leistance World Culture Survey Records, Thirteenth Report."
},
	[91103]={ language="Information One: Simple-minded, pure-hearted.\nInformation Two: No parents, according to the [Aunu] (Aunt) who raised her in the tribe, she grew up from flowers and grass.\nInformation Three: As a child, she once mimicked walking on all fours like a deer for fun."
},
	[91104]={ language="1. Sleipnir: The spirit deer that stays by Dawalin's side. It usually exists as a spirit form and rarely becomes physical.\n2. Dried flower wreath: A wreath woven with grass and flowers. Although it's dried, it's cherished because it was a gift from an old friend.\n3. [Sunshine Bee]: A potted plant cultivated by Dawalin herself, named for its yellow flowers with black stripes on the petals, resembling a bee."
},
	[91105]={ language="Information One: Loves singing, but is tone-deaf.\nInformation Two: Likes sleeping on grass and big rocks, and falls asleep easily.\nInformation Three: Although a Priest, doesn't do fortune-telling."
},
	[91106]={ language="Silvia's Crystal Weapon is different from Leistance or most other Crystal Weapon, and she holds a basic hostility toward anyone trying to touch her weapon. This isn't due to Silvia being afraid of strangers; it's a genuine warning. Whenever Silvia is asked for a reason, she always responds with: This staff carries the obsession of the Deer Deity, and unless touched by the one chosen by Deer Deity, punishment from the Deer Deity is certain.\nIf possible, my team and I really want to analyze what exactly Silvia's staff is made of. Judging from its appearance and material, it's clear that the staff has been technically upgraded. As for the [Deer Deity's punishment]... I guess it has to do with Void Particles, because in this world, there's no such thing as magic, curses... probably.\nWhether it's Vilatria's [Fate Star,] or Selevie's [Deer Deity,] everything can be explained through Void Particles. Otherwise... it's related to Shogger.\n—Gomia from Leistance Engineering Department records."
},
	[91107]={ language="Information One: Used to be very timid and didn't dare go to very dark places.\nInformation Two: Really wanted to see the outside world to find old friends."
},
	[91108]={ language="Information One: Using the power of Deer Deity for a long time can cause temporary memory loss... so she often forgets what happened during battles.\nInformation Two: Likes full moon, doesn't like crescent moon."
},
	[91109]={ language="She was born from the flowers, arriving in the world with blessings and prayers.\nThe earth is her cradle, and rain provides her with nourishment.\nSleipnir, the homeland of the ancestral spirits.\nShe will lead the people of Sleipnir to seek\nThe pure land of eternal joy, our homeland...\n—Fragmented tribal blessing."
},
	[91110]={ language="Real Name: Tiya Asteria\nIdentity: Acting Leader of Vilatria Stellar Knights\nInterests: Studying celestial bodies, reading"
},
	[91111]={ language="[Asteria Family Alchemy Introductory Course-Assignment Report for Issue 12]\nMaterials: 2g of raw eggs, 3 starry petals, 1 sprig of sage, 5g of black ore from the southern region\nAdditives: Pure water, cake flour, sugar\nSteps: Mix the materials, crush and put into a rice cooker, stir on high heat until melted, simmer while injecting magic, let stand for three days to separate impurities, refrigerate at low temperature until the color changes\nCompare with the color chart to confirm the color is correct\n——\nThis week's alchemy class potion assignment has been submitted along with the formula for your review.\n——\nComments: Tiya Asteria! I know the Knights' work is busy and you have limited time, but I also recall mentioning many times that alchemy and cooking are two different things! Alchemy is a serious discipline, don't assume it's as simple as cooking! Also, do not conduct alchemy assignments in the home kitchen, and do not mix recipes with textbooks! Both your uncle and I find such a careless assignment unacceptable!\nPS: Redo it in the family alchemy workshop when you return from the holiday!"
},
	[91112]={ language="Information One: Was once forced to learn the family's inherited alchemy, but really couldn't get it, so she gave up.\nInformation Two: Occasionally practices astrology magic by helping people with fortune telling, worried about getting caught, so always wears different disguises each time.\nInformation Three: Always makes people feel like there's more to what they say, and some decisions are often over-interpreted by subordinates."
},
	[91113]={ language="Notebook: The contents are unknown. She flips through it every time she makes an important decision, leading other members of the knight order to suspect it's some kind of secret weapon of Tiya's.\nStar chart: Made by Tiya based on ancient texts. It's said to recreate the true starry sky, but no one has seen the real starry sky, so who knows if it's true or not.\nSome old books: Neatly placed on the bookshelf, with titles like [Complete Guide to Constellations,] [Gazing at the Stars,] [Reaching for the Stars,] [The Demise of a Star,] and so on..."
},
	[91114]={ language="Information One: Only has a very poor posture habit while reading, always worried about becoming nearsighted, then continues to anxiously read while lying down.\nInformation Two: Many people have some misunderstandings about her star magic, thinking it's related to fortune telling. She is not offended by the term [fortune teller].\nInformation Three: Wants to open a fortune-telling shop after retirement to help young people with love divination."
},
	[91115]={ language="At first, taking on Stellar Knights was just the result of some simple persuasion.\nThe esteemed Pope privately approached her, saying: \n[The work of the knights is quite simple, and you're definitely capable of handling it.]\n[More importantly, there are books there that rival those in the Asteria family library; you can read them for a long time.]\n[If you're working, your family elders won't force you to study alchemy, and you can do what you want.]\nFor Tiya, who was struggling to meet her family's expectations at the time, it was a pretty enticing opportunity.\n[Since you put it that way, I'll take it.]\nBut now... if she had another chance, if she'd known it would turn out like this, Tiya isn't sure she would've agreed to the Pope so easily back then.\nUnfortunately, what's done is done. People of Vilatria believe that everyone's destiny corresponds to a star in the sky, and the trajectory of those stars is set from birth. Even if she hadn't agreed now, she would still have ended up on this path in the future.\nTaking charge of Stellar Knights meant standing at the pinnacle of power in that country, and she wasn't certain she could do it well. Her initial decisions often wavered, leading to instructions and decisions being somewhat vague, but the knights' management always managed to get things done, even if they occasionally over-interpreted her orders, the outcomes were still okay.\nWhenever she looked at the mountainous piles of files, Tiya wondered what kind of person the previous knight commander was, managing all this complex work so smoothly.\nShe was definitely misled by the Pope; the role of knight commander is not simple at all."
},
	[91116]={ language="Information One: Her office is spotless, but books can appear anywhere in the room.\nInformation Two: Has no talent for alchemy, but she likes alchemical items. She goes everywhere to collect them and display them at home, though many are actually fakes and dangerous goods."
},
	[91117]={ language="[Stellar Knights Work Plan for This Quarter (Partial)] (Draft)\n\n1. Civilian Area Street Repair: Address the issues of road collapse and debris accumulation on civilian streets in the east area of Stardom by deploying Quasar Knights for weekly cleaning and maintenance.\nNote: For road collapse issues, find the contractor responsible. Debris in alleys will pile up again after cleaning; hold the street manager accountable and have Quasar Knights conduct regular inspections and issue immediate penalties upon discovery.\n\n2. Knights' Regional Division Report: The time for division captains to report is scheduled for next week, lasting three days. See the attachment for banquet arrangements and detailed gift lists.\nNote: Reporting is just reporting, don't mix it with noble etiquette. Cancel the banquet. The Knights' headquarters will not accept any gift lists; they should come to see me with their brains and work reports only.\n\n3. Star Expedition Tour Process: This year's Star Expedition route has slight changes compared to previous years, adding some noble autonomous territories, with slight alterations in the Wilderness route. Details are in the attachment.\nNote: No issues with noble territories, remove the Wilderness inspection route. Also, send the Star Expedition Supply demand list to the nobles along the route. Since they need protection from the Knights, they need to provide expedition supplies to the Knights."
},
	[91118]={ language="Information One: The notebook, rumored to be a [secret weapon,] is actually filled with anxious doodles.\nInformation Two: As a privileged class member, who seldom uses their privileges, sometimes conflicts with other nobles due to concern for commoners' interests, but never suffers losses due to their strong family background and capabilities."
},
	[91119]={ language="Real Name: Chloe Schmitt\nIdentity: Vilatria Convicted Prisoner\nInterests: Sewing Puppets"
},
	[91120]={ language="As a prisoner, Chloe had spent a long time in jail. The transition from being the Star Knight who completed the pilgrimage to a prisoner didn't deeply affect her. The reason, after all, was that she was no longer the same person she used to be. She doesn't remember what kind of life she once lived, nor does she wish to remember; she just guards a dream according to the wishes of that girl.\nThe longer time passed, the more Chloe felt that her fate might have been predetermined, so she began to seek some fun for herself.\nShe took out sewing tools and cotton to make a puppet. The tools and materials came from a superior who visited her in the cell. After a while, Chloe made her first puppet. This puppet had no name, and Chloe didn't plan to name it, because she believed a puppet is just a puppet.\nBut Chloe wasn't satisfied with just that, so she gave the puppet a part of her own soul. From then on, Chloe had her first friend.\nLater, Chloe met the person who changed her destiny, the one who removed the shackles and unlocked the bindings on Chloe's world.\nNow, Chloe not only has a friend but also someone important to care about. She is working hard to meet that person again and eagerly awaits the day they reunite."
},
	[91121]={ language="Information One: Chloe often dreams, mostly good ones, but her nightmares are really terrifying.\nInformation Two: Chloe's hobby of sewing puppets started after she was imprisoned in an underground cell.\nInformation Three: Chloe spent a very long time in the cell, but she wasn't lonely because He was with her."
},
	[91122]={ language="Personal items: Tools for sewing puppets."
},
	[91123]={ language="Information One: [He] is the first Puppet sewn by Chloe, and is Chloe's friend.\nInformation Two: There's a chessboard, and playing chess with the Puppet— [He] is one way Chloe passes time.\nInformation Three: Chloe actually doesn't know how to play chess, but she always wins."
},
	[91124]={ language="Fragmented Memories—\n\nBefore becoming a member of the Stellar Knights, the girl doesn't remember much besides the orphanage and the sewer. The sewer is where she believes she was born, and the orphanage is where her entire childhood was spent. Later, a powerful knight came to the orphanage and took her away, giving her the name Chloe Schmitt.\nAfter leaving the orphanage, the place in her memory became an old but complete library. The powerful knight told Chloe that this library was her home, and she must organize all the books there, ensuring none are lost. The knight also told her that she would visit her often, and from then on, Chloe would become a Quasar Knight.\nChloe didn't love reading; in fact, she couldn't even write her own name as she had never been educated. The powerful knight discovered this and started teaching Chloe at night, beginning with writing her name. The days of learning accompanied Chloe's growth, and the knight's visits to the library gradually became less frequent, making each return something Chloe looked forward to.\nThe knight never asked Chloe to correct the way she addressed her and never revealed her real name to Chloe. She wanted Chloe to call her [Lord Knight], and she adhered to this. Later, Chloe learned that [Schmitt] in her name came from the powerful knight, symbolizing tenacity and stubbornness.\nChloe never called the knight [mother], as the knight didn't want her to. Chloe believed there was no need to do so; she felt their life together was enough to prove their relationship.\nUntil one day, Chloe felt overwhelming sadness because of this regret.\nSince then, Chloe has had nightmares every night."
},
	[91125]={ language="Information One: Chloe has never learned sewing skills. According to her, she suddenly mastered the technique to sew puppets one day.\nInformation Two: Chloe's sewing tools and cotton were gifts from others."
},
	[91126]={ language="One year after the completion of the Star Pilgrimage—\n\n[You're here again, Lord Knight Commander.]\n[Get some rest. I've got it from here.]\nAfter dismissing the Quasar Knight standing guard, she stood at the door with a heavy box, inserting a key into the lock with practiced ease.\nWith a grating squeak, she entered. The room was dim and dark, as the lighting had long since failed, and the bookshelves were covered in a thick layer of dust from neglect.\nShe placed the box down and opened it, retrieving a backup lamp and a set of cleaning tools. Following the correct cleaning process, she meticulously cleaned every corner of the room.\nOnce done, the room returned to its former appearance. She hung the lamp beside the clock on the wall, its light illuminating the room and casting a long shadow of her figure.\nShe sat at the desk, feeling along the desk leg until an inner compartment opened. She rose and fetched a bottle of wine from the box, swiftly drinking it down. She then placed something into the bottle and returned it to the compartment.\nWith that completed, she moved to the bookshelf, looking for a particular book. Soon after, she was at the desk, reading a book titled [One Hundred Interpretations of Astronomical Signs], going through page by page.\nUntil midnight, she closed the book, murmuring.\n[I still don't enjoy reading like you do.]\nShe returned the book to the shelf, took the box outside, and locked the door with the key.\nHowever, rather than pocketing the key, she crushed it.\n[...It's time to begin,] she muttered softly, adjusting her armor and sword before leaving the room."
},
	[91127]={ language="Information One: Although she has the cute appearance of a little girl, her mental age has surpassed that of an average adult woman.\nInformation Two: Chloe sewed a dress based on her impression, and this dress has been with her till now."
},
	[91128]={ language="Real Name: Elsida\nIdentity: Prosthetics Merchant in Foden City, Uzyanta \nInterests: Creating mechanical gadgets, managing own prosthetics"
},
	[91129]={ language="Isis will never forget the day she first met Elsida.\nAt that time, as the deputy director, she was in a meeting when a subordinate rushed in and informed her about an illegal intruder who insisted on seeing the Boss.\nAfter confirming there was no immediate threat, Isis approached the intruder with two AIMBS and several security personnel, only to find the woman waving an order in her face and asking if she wanted to take on a big job.\nFortunately, Isis was not some naive girl, but a mature and dependable member of the security bureau management, and she calmly and kindly asked Elsida if she had submitted any paperwork to liaise with the bureau. When Elsida's responses were all just head shakes and complete ignorance, she couldn't suppress the twitch at the corner of her mouth. \n[So, you just barged in like this?]\n[Yeah, someone told me the direct way to meet you was this, and I'm quite busy myself.]\n[Who?]\n[How about we talk business first? I promise you're going to be interested, dear deputy director...]\n[Even for business, there's a proper procedure. The security bureau isn't a place you can come and go as you please.] \nEventually, Isis did sign a series of prosthetic supply orders with the cyborg merchant from Foden City, but only after Aercida completed all the required procedures. The reason for doing this was that Isis didn't want similar imitators appearing in the future."
},
	[91130]={ language="Information One: Once a family heiress surrounded by countless bodyguards.\nInformation Two: After losing the family's support, she used her own abilities to establish a Stellar Crystal mine in Foden City.\nInformation Three: Elsida's prosthetic parts are stored in a depot, featuring various models."
},
	[91131]={ language="1. Prosthetic parts: High precision custom parts personally adjusted by Thunderock, available in different colors to match the user's current mood.\n2. Photo: A picture of Thunderock and a slightly haggard-looking woman, both appearing very happy.\n3. Giant shield: Thunderock's weapon, featuring multiple Model-ized advanced metal components, capable of transforming according to battlefield situations."
},
	[91132]={ language="Information One: All of Elsida's prosthetic spares are stored in a depot, including various models.\nInformation Two: Elsida was not born with Stellaron Resonance.\nInformation Three: Although Elsida is a prosthetic dealer, her expertise isn't specifically in prosthetic research; selling prosthetics is more to subsidize the mining operation."
},
	[91133]={ language="When talking to Elsida, one word always comes up: Foden City. Whenever this city is mentioned, talkative Elsida becomes even more animated. She always starts with a big affirmation, praising her hometown, then seriously debunks rumors to others.\n[I get why everyone wants to strike it rich in Foden City, but honestly, it's not a place where gold and Stellar Crystals are lying around... Okay, there's a fair bit, but not enough to find in the trash.]\n\n[There are big families, gangs, cops, robbers, beggars, people jumping off buildings, and all sorts of street performers.]\n[Got it? It's not much different from most cities, you've just been brainwashed by those tricky ads. I see tourists getting scammed all the time at the police station, and some of them don't even have money to get home.]\n[As for what's different... probably the widespread AI. You know, robots, smart systems, and stuff. People in Foden City love taking it easy, so they come up with these things to make life easier.]\n[Me? I don't get those things. I'm just a small vendor in Foden City. By the way, if anyone's got mobility issues, you can buy prosthetics from me. Everything except your brain can be replaced!]"
},
	[91134]={ language="Information One: Elsida provided the blueprint for the shield, but its construction was completed by another craftsman.\nInformation Two: Besides Elsida, no one else can pick up her shield for reasons that remain unknown."
},
	[91135]={ language="Deputy Director, this is Moonlight Kiss reporting the latest information collected in Foden City.\nFirst, there's the press conference from the Latif family. The spokesperson announced that they will fully launch all of [Genesis Hand's] operations in Foden City, and all executive roles will be handled by the founder, Turania.\nYes, this is unprecedented news. Considering the Latif family's methods, the company [Genesis Hand] should have been acquired and then have the founder replaced by someone from the family, turning it into a cog in solidifying Latif's position in Foden City. But it seems that Latif has no such intention and is preparing to shift their operational strategy, intending to make [Genesis Hand] a core family business.\nI had people investigate [Genesis Hand.] Apart from its standout performance in AI and intelligent machines, there aren't any other noteworthy aspects—these two businesses aren't even operated by [Genesis Hand.] This raises curiosity about what could make the Latif family willing to gamble everything on this company. It seems more like a gamble.\nHowever, it is noteworthy that Latif started frequent interactions with [Genesis Hand] many years ago, but we can't know the specific details. With Moonlight Kiss's capabilities, we shouldn't be left without leads, but that's the case. Perhaps we overlooked something.\nMoonlight Kiss will continue to investigate, and of course, you're welcome to come to Foden City for a drink, Deputy Director.\n\n— Grenache."
},
	[91136]={ language="Information One: Elsida is quite famous both above and below ground in Foden City, even the police sometimes need her help to get things done.\nInformation Two: She's a super carnivore, and only feels life is meaningful when she's eating meat."
},
	[91137]={ language="Real Name: Huai\nIdentity: Debuted during the Void Particles incident at the Spark Garden Fair, Yan's senior\nInterests: Calligraphy (exceptionally skilled), tea tasting, antique appreciation (but not demanding ownership), gardening"
},
	[91138]={ language="In a way, Spark is a country that values lineage.\nThe day before Huai participated in the sect competition, she had a conversation with her master about this matter.\nWith her talent and diligence, standing out in the competition wouldn't be hard for her. But it also meant her past would be more exposed, and so-called [ominous] rumors would resurface.\nIf the price of showcasing her skills was criticism, her master would rather she continue hiding her true self.\nAfter hearing her master's concerns, Huai replied seriously, [But as I've grown up, you've never hidden my background from anyone, so I think you'd want me to face it head-on.]\n[You told me it's not my fault, so why should I let myself be buried under the fear of others' opinions?]\n...\nJust as they anticipated, Huai easily defeated her opponents and made it to the final round. People were astonished by the genius girl's prowess, and soon her background became known.\n[An ominous girl? I didn't see it. Her master seems to be doing well these years.]\n[What's all this about luck? That family was quite foolish. Good thing there's no contact now.]\n[If my child turned out like Miss Huai, I'd be thrilled! Those red eyes are beautiful!]\nSuch comments poured in, and Huai heard every word. She looked at her master and fellow disciples, her expression unchanged from before, [Don't worry, I won't be affected.]\nIn the upcoming final battle, she would continue to win and use her strength to prove the absurdity of those claims.\nAs for what happens after the victory? Huai hadn't thought much about it. If she had to say, she'd hope to see the peonies planted two years ago bloom when they return to the sect."
},
	[91139]={ language="Information One: Can't handle spicy food, usually stays away from it, but for social etiquette, will politely try a small bite.\nInformation Two: Likes to collect snow, dew, etc., and it's said that tea brewed with different kinds of water tastes quite different.\nInformation Three: Practices calligraphy in her spare time and once gave Linker a piece of writing she did herself, which she called a [couplet]"
},
	[91140]={ language="1. Master's Portrait: A portrait of the entire guild, hung in the most prominent spot in the room.\n2. White Jade Box: An ancient item given by the master when leaving, used to store precious flower seeds in daily life.\n3. Celadon Tea Set: A tea set that's been used for a long time, reserved for important guests.\n4. Seemingly Ordinary Porcelain Jar: It's said to contain snow collected from bamboo leaves years ago, preserved using [inner force] magic.\n5. Rouge: Said to be a makeup product with thousands of years of history."
},
	[91141]={ language="Information One: Using honey and petals to make desserts is a unique romance of the Spark people. \nInformation Two: She doesn't have a strong desire for material things; appreciating antiques is one of her ways to maintain a peaceful mind. Those items eventually end up in the hands of her junior sister.\nInformation Three: After learning how to use the internet, she has always surfed the web under her real name."
},
	[91142]={ language="After leaving the sect, Huai encountered a strange woman.\nShe looked like a normal human female, but the tips of her hair resembled bird wings, so perhaps in some sense, she isn't entirely human.\nSpark called all kinds of Mutants [demons,] and Huai had killed quite a few on her journey, but this was the first time she'd seen such an oddity, making her want to get closer.\nThe seemingly sleeping woman suddenly opened her eyes when she sensed someone approaching and backed away, [Who are you?]\nHuai friendly tried to convey her harmless intentions, but the woman showed a mocking smile, [How do I know if what you say is true? Who would believe it?]\n[Save your pointless kindness! No one needs it here, maybe someone will stab you too, who knows.]\n[Thanks for the warning, I'll be careful,] Huai replied, noticing the woman seemed somewhat surprised... even disappointed?\nBefore she could say more, the woman, almost like a bird, spread her wings and flew away, disappearing to somewhere unknown.\nWhat a strange person, Huai shifted her gaze to the monster corpses on the ground, which were rapidly turning to dust in the air.\nHuai wondered if these monsters could still be called life; everything is too marvelous, and no one can easily define it.\nAnd she wanted to explore this mystery."
},
	[91143]={ language="Information One: She's very concerned about her appearance, and to maintain a refined look, she gets up at least an hour early every day.\nInformation Two: She believes that flowers blooming to wilting is the natural evolution of life, and she grows flowers just to enjoy this process."
},
	[91144]={ language="Huai doesn't dislike socializing; for her, it's a required course.\nWhen she first arrived at Leistance, everyone assumed she was like Yan, introverted and not fond of socializing, so they tacitly avoided visiting her to prevent awkwardness.\nHuai wouldn't socialize unless necessary, and the change came when she met an AIMBS named Snow Fox.\nUpon discovering there was a new face she had never seen before from the distant far east, she excitedly brought her treasured snacks to knock on the door—never mind the fact that Frost Jade was brought to tears by the spicy snacks, they really enjoyed chatting and could have continued if Snow Fox didn't have to leave for something urgent.\nEven Snow Fox mentioned it was the first time she chatted with someone for so long, though Frost Jade later stopped eating the snacks she brought.\nThis kickstarted Huai's social life in this unfamiliar region, and after consulting her opinion, a post titled [Miss Frost Jade and Sparks: Things You Don't Know] appeared on Leistance's intranet and went viral.\nMany participated, including regular online visitors, Huai herself, and even Yan joined the discussion.\nEveryone's enthusiasm for Sparks was evident; hopefully, one day, they can see it with their own eyes!"
},
	[91145]={ language="Information One: Even if she participates in the campaign, she rarely shows any obvious signs of attacking. Her true combat power is a mystery.\nInformation Two: Admire Neon's magic, considering it a form of fairy magic."
},
	[91146]={ language="Real Name: Ifrit \nIdentity: Patrol ranger in Sleipnir area, Selevie \nInterests: Chilling, shopping, eating, drinking, and having fun"
},
	[91147]={ language="Regarding becoming a ranger, Ifrit initially refused.\nAs a wealthy young lady who never worried about food or clothing, she thought there was no need for her to work; enjoying life was her only concern.\nThe latest cosmetics? Buy them!\nAntique records not yet in her collection? Buy them!\nIfrit's spending was like a drop in the bucket for the Incubator Company, not even worth mentioning. Her grandfather was more worried about the future of his precious granddaughter—in this crisis-filled era, even if Ifrit could spend her life under the family's Sanctuary, she still needed to develop the ability to live independently and cope with crises.\nThis issue was brought up repeatedly and was often rejected by Ifrit, delaying again and again, until a family business partner was wiped out by the mechanical civilization. Ifrit was finally ordered to stop her indulgences and had to find a job on her own to support herself. Until then, the family wouldn't provide any financial support.\nSeeing that the decision was final, Ifrit gritted her teeth and set her own conditions: if successful, her allowance would need to be increased, and she would require a one-time bonus as compensation. Her grandfather agreed without hesitation, and then this young lady embarked on a difficult job search.\nBecoming a ranger was an unexpected turn—Selevie's jungle was humid and rainy, with harsh conditions, but many people were eager to apply due to the generous salary and the position's direct employment with the Incubator Company.\nIfrit wasn't enticed by the money; what interested her was the future prospects of being a ranger: after serving a certain number of years, she could apply to work in a core city, which would be a light-duty job—even though everyone competed for this position, Ifrit believed that as a family heiress, she would certainly be prioritized."
},
	[91148]={ language="Information One: Loves all kinds of novel foods and is naturally unable to gain weight.\nInformation Two: Still a kid at heart in some ways, not fully mature psychologically.\nInformation Three: Surprisingly good at photography; taking pictures is one of her ways to slack off."
},
	[91149]={ language="1. Custom-made headphones: Ifrit personally designed and supervised the production of these headphones, making them priceless to her.\n2. Compressed fuel reserve device: Provides energy for the portable rocket launcher, with a usage duration of up to ■ hours.\n3. LY brand high-end custom shoes: Handmade for her after becoming a ranger by a family-appointed craftsman, designed for comfort with reportedly several pairs of the same style.\n4. Old photo album: A photo album as old as Ifrit, containing her pictures from childhood to present.\n5. Ranger employee badge: Proof of identity as a ranger."
},
	[91150]={ language="Information One: Collected a lot of rare old records, which she placed in her home in Selevie City.\nInformation Two: Always on the cutting edge of fashion, with many fashion magazines on the bookshelf.\nInformation Three: Music is always playing in her headphones, but it doesn't affect her communication with others."
},
	[91151]={ language="[Hi Chairman, I didn't expect you to personally inquire about the onboarding situation of this batch of newcomers.\nHere is the list of newcomers:\nLouise, adaptability S+, physique S, observation S, written test S, overall S+\n...\nIfrit, adaptability A, physique S, observation B, written test A, overall A+\n...\nThis batch of newcomers is extremely outstanding as a whole. I believe they will become the Defender force of our Incubator Company in the future. I will do my best to train them and not disappoint your trust in me...]\nIfrit suddenly appeared, closed the report email that her grandfather had read over and over, and then dragged it into the trash.\n[How many times has Grandpa read this? I'm going to work in the jungle next month.]\n[I won't come back halfway, just wait and see. I'll definitely complete the task successfully and return here on my own... Of course, if you miss me, just remember to call me back anytime.]\n[If you don't believe me, let's make a bet. If I succeed, you will no longer interfere in my life...]\nAfter negotiating the terms, Ifrit finally left to pack for her job, saying she'd waste her prime in a lousy forest.\n[Why didn't anyone ever tell me! Getting promoted is such a difficult thing!]\nMiss, keep pushing forward."
},
	[91152]={ language="Information One: Her dream is to eat, drink, have fun, and be a lazybones, but sadly reality won't allow it.\nInformation Two: As one of the conditions for gaining grassroots experience, her family deposited a huge amount of money into her card."
},
	[91153]={ language="The ultimate meaning of life is enjoyment; it shouldn't be destroyed by work.\n Ifrit always follows this motto, and often does things that bewilder colleagues—like taking a nap on a clean, quiet boulder during a break; or finding a tall enough tree to sit on with headphones on, blocking out distractions, and enjoy a game; or, during some leisure holiday, going back to the city for some revenge shopping.\n The low scores at the end of the season were a wake-up call for her, forcing Ifrit to take her work seriously, painfully cutting down on goofing off and leisure time, achieving good results in the second season's assessment, and landing an unexpected task—an assignment to the areas surrounding Sleipnir, responsible for local environmental investigations and pollution control.\n Harsh jungle environments, local residents who are rustic and difficult to communicate with, and an economic level far behind city standards, each one is unbearable.\n I can't waste a lifetime in the forest; I have to reach the promotion goals as soon as possible.\n With this ideal in mind, Ifrit finally started working hard."
},
	[91154]={ language="Information One: Although she often jokes that Dawalin is silly, deep down, she's already considered Dawalin as a friend.\nInformation Two: She was once discovered by a talent scout and invited to debut, but she turned it down, thinking it would be too hard and tiring."
},
	[91155]={ language="Real Name: Eucaly\nIdentity: Void Hunter-Sequence Three\nInterests: Self-performance"
},
	[91156]={ language="The Arctic Void Expanse is one of the three major Void Particles Contaminated Expanses on Taino Star that has not been eliminated since the rise of the Skyborne Barriers. Due to its extremely high concentration of Void Particles pollution and inherently barren land, it was abandoned by humans, like a [thorn] embedded in the planet.\nAccording to records stored by Leistance, the Arctic Void Expanse shows traces of Shogger activity. These creatures depend on Void Particles for survival and have mutated due to the Void Particles Remodeling the ecosystem, becoming a biological category within the ecological community. It is rumored among northern human societies that there were once Shoggers in the Arctic Void Expanse that were not hostile to humans, but these claims eventually became unfounded and absurd stories.\nTo prevent the spread of the Arctic Void Expanse, under the guidance of the Star Council, the northern nation Burksomi established a fortress city near the Arctic Void Expanse as a human blockade point to guard the north.However, this fortress city was soon abandoned due to various reasons, including Supply issues, and became a large ruin closest to the Void Expanse.\nYet the Arctic Void Expanse hasn't expanded further, maintaining a distance from the ruined fortress city without change to this day. Most scholars believe this is because the concentration of Void Particles in the expanse hasn't increased, so expanding further would reduce the concentration inside the Void Expanse, affecting its ecological role as an [environment.]\n[Basically, these people think that the Arctic Void Expanse has become a natural environment on Taino Star over the years, so humans don't need to conquer it, coexisting with the environment is the right approach.]\n[In truth, it's because the fogged Void Particles can block almost all detection equipment, no one knows what's really going on inside, so they just find a convenient reason to conclude.]\n[Is it just an excuse to cover up some secret activities? Do you think others haven't thought of that? How do you prove it? Go there and find out? Would you dare?]\n[Believe it or not, friend.]"
},
	[91157]={ language="Information One: Eucaly's weapon is an ultra-long blade made from special materials, which doesn't fall under the category of Crystal Weapon.\nInformation Two: Eucaly named her sword [NO.1]\nInformation Three: Eucaly always carries a notebook that records the various achievements she has accomplished."
},
	[91158]={ language="Record book: A book that keeps track of one's unparalleled achievements\nA voice replay device: A small replay device, containing various people's praises for Eucaly, Eucaly's spiritual nourishment\nA broken sword: The weapon Eucaly used before becoming a hunter, broken by Shogger"
},
	[91159]={ language="Information One: Eucaly can't remember past memories clearly, but she doesn't mind and is very satisfied with the present.\nInformation Two: She built a camp with other hunters in the [Third Zone] phantom erosion domain, and they treat this place as home.\nInformation Three: She aims to become the number one in Leistance in terms of military power and is working hard towards that goal.\n"
},
	[91160]={ language="[Phase Report on Handling the Arctic Void Expanse]\nDate:\nJuly 29, 2120\nLocation:\nZone 3\nAction Force:\n■■■■\nMembers Assigned:\nSequence ■■, Sequence 03, ■■05, Sequence 07\nReport Content:\nA lord-level Shogger launched a [Void Particles Tide] attack on Zone 3's intercept zone. Sequence 03 and Sequence 05 successfully killed it, stopping the tide from entering Zone 3.\nSequence 02 and Sequence 07 encountered an attack by five lord-level Shoggers while searching for the [anchor] in Zone 3. They killed three, severely wounded one, and drove one away.\nSequence 02 sustained 60% body damage and was taken back to the unit base by Sequence 07 for repairs. Sequence 07 reported that the anchor in Zone 3 was not found, so the void erosion threat in Zone 3 cannot be completely eliminated for now.\n————————————————————————————\nApproval: ■■■■ will continue to station in the Arctic region, and all requests to leave the base will be rejected.\n"
},
	[91161]={ language="Information One: She can't stand anything more dazzling than herself, so she often gets stuck in a stubborn mindset.\nInformation Two: Has a peculiar habit of [surpassing and destroying what others are most proud of.]\n"
},
	[91162]={ language="After the [War to End All Wars] ended, Taino entered a period of rest and recovery, lasting several hundred years. The terrifying phrases once feared by all gradually fell out of use, as the scars left by the war slowly healed.\nThe leaders of this world aimed to bury that era of despair and hope, alongside time, to ensure that all life on the planet no longer lived in pain and sorrow.\nHowever, a rebel appeared, convinced that enemies still lurked in the shadows, waiting for the next chance to completely destroy humanity.\nThe rebel hid in the shadows, keeping secrets from the world, and revived things buried in the graves of time.\nHe held up the corpse of hope, opened what was considered a forbidden Pandora's box, and created the machines that ended the war once more.\nTo him, the [War to End All Wars] was merely a tool for humanity's self-deception, which the leaders knew but chose to ignore, plunging all of humanity into a fantasy of happiness.\nThe [Prophecy] has now arrived, and he believes he is the savior.\n"
},
	[91163]={ language="Information One: Known by other hunters as the [elegant princess bathing in the Void Expanse,] but she's unaware of this.\nInformation Two: Her [Void Hunter] unit has minimal contact with Leistance, and is active in extremely dangerous large Void Expanses.\n"
},
	[91164]={ language="Real Name: Poharu\nIdentity: Head of the Security Department, Divinelight Heavy Tech Lavox Branch\nInterests: Playing horror games, reading ghost stories, working out"
},
	[91165]={ language="Every security officer at the Divinelight Heavy Tech Lavox Branch wholeheartedly trusts and supports their leader, a young girl named Poharu.\nTwo-thirds of the people here are Lavox locals, with their families working here since their grandfathers' time. Although the town doesn't have the noble and commoner distinction typical of other countries, the prestige accumulated over the years naturally gives them an edge over the remaining third who are outsiders. So when they heard that their new Boss was a young girl who left the town and returned from the capital, everyone was ready to give her a hard time, determined to show her that Lavox isn't a place you can leave and return to as you wish.\nPoharu joined under such circumstances, completely unaware of the situation.\nOn her first day, fewer than ten people showed up at the tutorial field.\nThe young girl, under the worried gaze of the neighboring research department head, kicked open the lounge door and dragged those self-proclaimed locals out from beds, sofas, and even next to game consoles. Intimidated by her force, most people, after exchanging glances and whispers, chose to comply, obediently accepting punishment and going out in the freezing cold wearing shorts and T-shirts for a run.\nAs for the remaining few?\nThey didn't hesitate to Challenge the new Boss but ended up being beaten and had to endure double punishment.\nAfter several such incidents, most people were subdued by Poharu's strength. However, it wasn't until the later Mutant invasion that she secured her unequivocal position in the security department.\nOne late night, a Mutant broke into the testing field from the mountains. Poharu, without any backup from the security department, managed to hold off for an hour, successfully safeguarding Shen Guang Heavy Industries' valuable equipment and protecting the lives of the research staff.\nPoharu became a legend after that battle, and the employees were genuinely convinced of her capabilities.\n[Haha, it's all thanks to everyone. What was I thinking at that time? I had to fulfill my duty, of course... You want to know what I think about them calling me 'Big Sis'? Such words can affect the image of Shen Guang Heavy Industries. I should go back and warn them, and I'll head back to the tutorial now.]"
},
	[91166]={ language="Information One: Her hair isn't really suited for dyeing; that green tuft is natural.\nInformation Two: Her immense physical strength makes her unbeatable, until she discovers the existence of an intangible entity called [ghost]...\nInformation Three: She's strict about her diet, making dining with her quite challenging."
},
	[91167]={ language="Customized hand armor: Divinelight Heavy Tech creates custom campaign weapons for all members, tailored to individual characteristics, perfectly matching Crag's Campaign habits.\nSchedule: A strictly followed schedule recording daily diet, caloric intake, and fitness plans for the day.\nLedger: Documents debts owed to the research department and pending revenues, roughly estimated to be in balance.\nE-book reader: Rumored to contain various horror novels, movies, and game recordings, but she only opens it in Ravended places, suddenly letting out a frightened scream.\nAntique camera: A collaboration product from a famous horror game, rumored to be a ghost-repelling tool, and she's always looking forward to the day it becomes useful.\n"
},
	[91168]={ language="Information One: Sports events are a traditional family gathering activity, even though it seems unbelievable to everyone.\nInformation Two: Only drink two beverages: water and black coffee.\nInformation Three: Occasionally has some off-the-wall ideas and will knock on the R&D department's door the next moment to communicate with the director.\n"
},
	[91169]={ language="The head of the R&D department is named Nova, a native of Lavox, who grew up with Poharu until Poharu experienced a Stellaron Resonance at the age of fourteen and left for higher studies in the capital.\nA few years later, when Poharu returned to Lavox as a special envoy from headquarters, Nova was the first in the Lavox branch to welcome her and privately offered her a lot of extra work support.\nHowever, Nova also has her own worries.\n[How many times do I have to tell you, Burksomi's current level of technology isn't enough to support your wild ideas.] Nova wearily refused Poharu's request for an upgrade to her wrist weapon, [I can help you enhance the structure and durability system of your climbing shoes, and the visibility and clarity of your diving goggles can also be improved.]\n[But.] Nova tapped the table, raising her voice two degrees, [The wrist burning function you mentioned is unrealistic from the perspective of fuel or sustainability, and it contradicts your Stellaron Resonance attribute. Researching it according to your plan will offer no benefit to your combat.]\n[But think about it, if my gauntlet could shoot flames, it would greatly increase its power in battle, and ghosts in many games and movies are frightened by fire, achieving it would be a highlight in your career history too.] Poharu squatted in front of Nova's desk, giving her starry eyes, [As amazing Nova, you surely can do it, right?]\n[No, it's not realistic, neither your proposal nor your imagined enemies.] Nova refused again but proposed another idea she had thought of, [But listen, for your upgrade plan, I have a better idea, though it might not help your ghost-hunting plan.]\n[Eh, what is it?] Poharu stood up suddenly, excitedly pressing against the table, and in her Overdrive excitement, accidentally dented the table, [Truly amazing Nova, quickly tell me.]\n[Recently, the headquarters sent a batch of minerals collected from lava, reportedly contaminated by Void Particles, for new material R&D here in Lavox. I'm thinking about making something for hardness testing, but funds are limited... What I mean is, maybe we could finance the research ourselves, and later consider large-scale development for defensive uses... though there's a risk of failure.]\nPoharu looked at her friend expectantly, [So, how much would the initial research funds be? My salary should be enough, right?]\nNova gave her a figure, unsurprisingly seeing the astonished look on her friend's face, so she opened a form and pointed to the information to explain, [If the test is successful and meets the requirements for mass production, based on the company's compensation standards, besides a one-time research grant, we could receive about five percent of the total profits over three years as a bonus, which would be a considerable income, and I'll jointly bear the basic R&D funding with you.]\nPoharu's eyes lit up, [Five percent, which means once successful, I won't have to worry about not having money to upgrade equipment.]\nNova happily agreed with her, [Exactly, but there's another matter now.]\n[Pay for the repair of my desk first.]\n"
},
	[91170]={ language="Information One: Although she has a high salary, she's actually a bit short on money because she spends most of it on upgrading and replacing her gear.\nInformation Two: Her skin tone is natural, often misunderstood as being from too much exercise and forgetting sunscreen. Later on, she just got lazy to explain.\n"
},
	[91171]={ language="Lavox is a seaside town in the northeast part of Burksomi, often visited by merchant ships from Supply. The town also has many Stores run by outsiders.\nPoharu was fearless from a young age, until at six, a relative visiting their home brought her sister a gift—a collector's item of a famous horror game. Curious Poharu watched it and was terrified, crying out loud. The incident ended temporarily with her sister's game taken away, and no one expected that Poharu would develop a fear of such things.\nEven so, she still tries hard to overcome her fear—as bravery Poharu, she cannot and should not be afraid of something.\nThe more she gets involved, the more Poharu feels powerless: she can knock down a fierce Mutant with one punch and kick over a scary monster with one kick, but when it comes to ghosts—let's assume such creatures truly exist—she can't do anything, no amount of punches helps.\nThe first step to defeating an enemy is understanding it, which Poharu also considers a truth, thus she forced herself to watch various horror movies, bought a lot of game cartridges, and under her sister's resentful gaze, she repeatedly completed the collector's edition game and even memorized every step.\nUnfortunately, Poharu realized she still couldn't comprehend this thing called [ghost] scientifically, and the more she learned, the more elusive it seemed.\nProbably before finding a true way to deal with it, the seed named fear wouldn't be easily uprooted.\nIf you ask those in Lavox about Bravery's Poharu, everyone praises her courage. If you ask what she fears, you'd get a common understanding: Bravery's Poharu is determined and fearless.\nIf you ask her personally, well, before you become well-acquainted with her, she likely wouldn't reveal this secret."
},
	[91172]={ language="Information One: There are video tapes of her crying from being scared by horror games as a child, which she keeps as a top secret.\nInformation Two: She was once tricked into buying something called [ghost-repelling talisman,] and later beat up the con artist badly.\n"
},
	[91173]={ language="Real Name: Rose \nIdentity: Uzyanta bounty hunter\nInterests: Investing, growing roses"
},
	[91174]={ language="Rose, whose Real Name is Diana, is a freelance bounty hunter from Uzyanta. She makes a living by completing bounty commissions for various organizations in Uzyanta. Whether it's helping to open a safe or hunting down the top wanted criminal, as long as the reward is high enough, it's part of her job scope, and she delivers perfect results to her clients.\nThe communication between Rose and Leistance began with the Foden City incident. According to Rose herself, she has a large client in Leistance, so she can offer the security bureau some special considerations: like providing an irresistible discount, or offering small pieces of Information that are trivial to her but very important to the security bureau.\n[Although her fees are ridiculously high, she truly provides value for the cost.]\n[I must admit, with Rose's help, the security bureau's operations in Uzyanta have become much easier.]\n[The only issue is...she only acknowledges that so-called large client, no one else can make it work with her. Yes, you know who I mean, our big Linker!]"
},
	[91175]={ language="Information One: Rose's Crystal Weapon is expensive, and she named the gun [Carolla] and the energy box [Margaret.]\nInformation Two: Among the various bounty missions, Rose prefers hunting down criminals because it often pays well and is exciting.\nInformation Three: She is extremely fond of investing and believes in her unique vision, but in reality, all her ventures end up losing money."
},
	[91176]={ language="Taino Coin: The bounty Rose got after completing her first task, just one coin, marking the start of her hunter career.\nRose perfume: A perfume Rose blended herself, with various rose petal essences added."
},
	[91177]={ language="Information One: In each of her private estates, there is a flower field used for planting roses.\nInformation Two: [Spend a life doing nothing] is Rose's wish, but she has never worked towards it.\nInformation Three: Skilled at communicating with people and finding their flaws, eventually gaining an advantage in negotiations."
},
	[91178]={ language="Rose is known in the Uzyanta bounty hunters community for her high demands and 100% success rate. Most peers have never seen her in person; they usually just see the commission slip taken and a rose left behind to prove the woman accepted the task.\nSuch high-profile actions naturally draw some dissatisfaction from peers, who complain of losing clients and thus challenged Rose to a traditional duel at the capital's arena. To everyone's surprise, Rose accepted, causing a stir in the bounty hunter circle, with arena tickets selling out in three days. Vendors quickly set up stalls at the entrance, and underground casinos started betting. People said this duel's popularity rivaled Uzyanta changing a [chief,] showing just how famous Rose is among bounty hunters despite the joke's dark humor.\nOn the duel day, challengers and spectators awaited Rose's arrival, and she entered the arena as expected. Just before the referee announced the duel's start, Rose stopped them and asked the challenger,\n[How much are you offering for my presence? You know I never do unprofitable deals.]\nThese provoking words fueled the challenger's anger, as he shouted he'd bet all his wealth, demanding Rose do the same. The woman nodded in satisfaction and told the referee the duel could begin.\nThen, the referee waved, a gunshot rang out, and the unaware challenger fell.\nIn under two seconds, the duel ended. The woman removed the rose from her eyes, tore off a petal, and placed it on the pierced hole in the fallen forehead.\nThough lasting only seconds, the duel ignited a wave of cheering. Peers chanted Rose's name as she quietly exited the scene.\nSince that day, few have seen Rose again, but her business flourished, and no one dared challenge her strength anymore."
},
	[91179]={ language="Information One: Her hobby is soaking in the huge bathtub at home and having a glass of wine that's over 5 years old.\nInformation Two: She's a regular at various bars in Foden City, and her favorite is a traditional tavern."
},
	[91180]={ language="After becoming an Elite agent, Diana had thought about many ways she might die. Perhaps sacrificing herself during a mission for her country, or dying in battle while protecting the people of Joshburg—no matter which way, even if she couldn't be buried under the Joshburg flag due to her identity, at least her tombstone could bear the words [Sacrificed for Joshburg] to prove that her life had meaning.\nUntil the outbreak of Void Particles contamination in the capital of Uzyanta, death arrived as expected, marking the end of her first life and the beginning of the second.\nBefore that day, Diana took pride in Joshburg, looking forward to dying for Joshburg.\nAfter that day, the chains of the Exemplar system broke away, and she completely split from Joshburg, becoming a traitor.\nFate revealed the truth to her and cast her into the endless sands for rebirth.\nFrom then on, Joshburg's Elite agent Diana was executed for treason, yet the Desert of Uzyanta gained a new bounty hunter."
},
	[91181]={ language="Information One: Taino Currency and Crystal Ashes are prerequisites for accepting the commission, but if other rewards are appealing, Rose will also consider them.\nInformation Two: Skilled in disguise, well-acquainted with the characteristics of most social identities."
},
	[91182]={ language="Real Name: Alicia Klein\nIdentity: Special Operator directly under Leistance Headquarters\nInterests: Decorating Danchey Puppet and Star Corner"
},
	[91183]={ language="File Update—\nFile Owner: Alicia \nReason for Update: After the battle at the Foden City anchor, an anomaly occurred in Stellaron Resonance.\nResult Explanation: Tests completed on divine blood, physical body, and Void Particles adaptability, revealing no rampage phenomenon due to abnormal activity of Void Particles in Stellaron Resonance. The Operator can use this Stellaron Resonance while maintaining self-will.\nDetailed Explanation: Strictly speaking, I don't think this can be called a mutation, because I've seen what Stellaron Resonance mutations look like. Those non-human monsters in the Arctic are the strongest evidence. Miss Alicia's Stellaron Resonance is more like an evolution. Although it cannot be explained by Leistance's current divine blood technology, it is indeed a special situation arising from her divine blood... I must say, sometimes it really makes you wonder if it's a miracle.\nFile Access Permission: Maximum\nApproval of File Update: Harper Klein"
},
	[91184]={ language="Information One: Very sensitive to changes in Void Particles, but feels much better after linking with Linker's divine blood.\nInformation Two: Really likes symmetrical things.\nInformation Three: Changed the perfume for danchey Puppet, supposedly the brand of perfume comes from Linker's preference."
},
	[91185]={ language="1. New-style Crystal Weapon-Abyss Type 1: A Crystal Weapon birthed from Alicia's new Stellaron Resonance, designed in the form of a greatsword and battle skirt. It was later modernized by the Leistance logistics department to make it more suitable for Alicia's use.\n2. Danchey Puppet: Alicia has placed all her Danchey Puppet collections in her room and Star Corner, with the ones given by Linker carried with her.\n3. Photo Album: A gift from Alicia's father, containing group photos of Alicia at the Leistance headquarters, with the last one being a photo of her with Linker."
},
	[91186]={ language="Information One: Thinks she has a talent for naming, but really doesn't.\nInformation Two: Eats a lot, but decided to control her diet with Linker.\nInformation Three: Although she's a colleague, most members of Leistance Headquarters see her as a younger sister."
},
	[91187]={ language="After returning to Leistance, the first thing Alicia did was go to the [Star Corner] where she and Linker made a promise.\nLuckily, even though the surrounding corridors had been renovated, the grassy area remained lush, and the stars above still shone brightly.\nLater, Alicia and Linker tidied up the Star Corner together and added some furniture, turning it into a place they could actually live in.\nThough building a private dormitory violated Leistance's administrative rules, Linker informed Isis using their authority that the Star Corner could help Alicia regain her memory. This lone [illegal structure] on the mothership remained due to the tacit approval of others.\nSince then, the two have carefully maintained this secret base of theirs, and gradually, the Star Corner felt more like a [home] than their individual dorms.\n[Even though the Security Bureau doesn't mind you making this place homey, you two have nearly made it more luxurious than other Operators' dorms. Just look at this furniture and the ceiling projection device. How much money are you planning to pour into this place?]\n[Doctor sister, if it's about money, don't worry. I have plenty of funds in my account.]\n[True... you are the director general's daughter, so money shouldn't be an issue... wait, what about your father? Does he approve of this?]\n[Since it's my daughter's request, I won't stop you, but you can't keep running there all the time. You still need to complete your AIMBS tasks—those are my father's words.]\n[Huh, even the director general said that...]\n[Doctor sister, would you like to come in and sit for a while? Linker got some tea from Starlight, and it's said to have calming effects, perfect for you, doctor sister.]\n[Well... then I won't impose...]"
},
	[91188]={ language="Information One: When she was a kid, she had no sense of clothes and makeup until she met Linker and started learning gradually.\nInformation Two: Among the Danchey Puppets, the one that Linker gave her in Foden City is her favorite."
},
	[91189]={ language="On quiet nights, a young girl dreams of sinking with the waves, descending into the depths of the ocean.\nShe seems to hear someone calling her name, a distant voice, deep and faraway, yet it feels familiar.\n[Who are you?]\n[The most hated thing by humans... what is that?]\n[You mean... my mom?]\n[I don't know my mom, I... miss her very much.]\n[Can't see me... why do this...?]\n[When I wake up, I'll forget...?]\n[No, I don't want to...]\nThe girl murmurs until tears gather and fall. She then wakes up, and that dream shatters like a bubble, leaving nothing in her consciousness.\nFrom that day on, in the girl's eyes, there was an invisible [chain] that no one could see."
},
	[91190]={ language="Information One: Always keeps her hair tidy, considering whether to change hairstyles.\nInformation Two: Sneaks away to meet Linker at Star Corner in the dead of night."
},
	[91191]={ language="Real Name: Cynaca\nIdentity: Traveling merchant doing business at Selevie\nInterests: Making money, traveling, collecting business information"
},
	[91192]={ language="The reception at Leistance has been dealing with quite a few packages lately.\nFrom Selevie, Burksomi, some undeveloped areas, and even things sent across the sea from distant Spark.\nAll are expensive luxury items, and have two things in common: the recipient is [Dad] and they've been stored for a long time.\nIf not for the hefty storage fee that came with the delivery, the staff wouldn't have kept these items for so long. The mysterious recipient's identity has been a topic of fascination in the logistics department for quite some time. Their speculation led them to believe the recipient is a wealthy, refined middle-aged man, and he has a very loving daughter.\n[Silk pajamas from Spark, natural plant incense from Selevie, handcrafted gemstone brooches from Uzyanta, oh, and these two bottles of wine, seem to be from Burksomi, a small cup probably costs my monthly salary.] The young temp carefully arranged the newly arrived packages on the metal rack for pickups, expressing his envy to his colleague, [Not to mention, this is the third silk pajamas this month! I hope by the time I reach this gentleman's age, I'll have such a daughter too.]\nHis colleague shook his head and responded, [We still haven't reached the recipient, just an address but no contact information. It's really odd, who would only write the word 'Dad' as the recipient? Makes it impossible for us to track him down.]\nOn a sleepy afternoon, while they were idly doing reports, they saw the high-profile Linker return from a mission, appearing there, borrowing a cart, and calmly taking away those packages addressed to [Dad.]\nStaff: […?]"
},
	[91193]={ language="Information One: Due to historical reasons, after joining Leistance, she's still considered a destabilizing factor by Joshburg National Security Department.\nInformation Two: Believes that interests are paramount between people, and money is the most direct and convenient representation.\nInformation Three: The assets actually owned by her are a rather terrifying number."
},
	[91194]={ language="1. [Argo]: The high technology backpack that Cynaca carries with her, which she later uses as her name outside.\n2. International Passport: A universal passport guaranteed by Linker, endorsed by Leistance, and specially issued by the Star Council.\n3. Void Particles Filter Equipment: A complete set of high technology gear allowing Seneca to move easily in areas filled with Void Particles.\n4. [Linker Observation Notes]: Contains photos of Linkers taken by Seneca and some insights from her interactions, which she generously shares with other AIMBS.\n5. Lucky Piggy: A charm hanging on Seneca's bag that brings good luck, especially in finances."
},
	[91195]={ language="Information One: Wearing a protective mask has long become her personal habit due to frequent visits to dangerous areas.\nInformation Two: Has connections or agents everywhere on Taino Star.\nInformation Three: Takes breaks regularly, often calling on Linker to manage the business."
},
	[91196]={ language="File 1: [Resolution on Prohibiting Traveling Merchants Cynaca & Argo from Entering Joshburg]\nFile 2: [New Loan Regulations for Joshburg State Bank]\nFile 3: [Lod Coalition Entry Management Protocol]\nFile 4: [Regulations on the Import and Export of Unlicensed Goods]\n......\n[Please hold on, Ms. Cynaca.] The Leistance registration officer pressed their temples, [May I confirm again, you were once restricted from entering Joshburg, correct?]\nCynaca sat upright in the chair, [That's all just rumors. I have done nothing to jeopardize Joshburg's national security, and I can provide complete tax records and product lists. I genuinely love Joshburg, such a vibrant country full of opportunities.]\nThe officer carefully flipped through the thick pile of files, [But I also believe my country wouldn't sanction an honest merchant without reason, and as a long-term high-profile business talent of the Lod Coalition, it's understandable that Joshburg can't trust you.]\n[You know, Leistance as a borderless organization, shouldn't focus on such a matter.] Cynaca gave a kind smile, placing her hand over something, pushing it forward, [I sincerely wish to join Leistance, wanting to contribute to Tainos's resistance against Shogger and the eradication of Mutants.]\nShe withdrew her hand, leaving a shiny gemstone pendant there, [Surely you can't refuse such a genuine wish, can you? It's good for everyone.]\nThe officer glanced at it, smiling and shaking their head, [Ms. Cynaca, please take our scrutiny seriously. Before being a Leistance staff member, I'm a Joshburg citizen first.]\n[Alright then.] Cynaca shrugged, slumping back in the chair, [But I am indeed innocent. If you don't believe me, you can ask my dear investor, as one of your Linkers, his guarantee ought to carry weight.]\nThe officer suddenly felt more troubled, [Listen, Ms. Cynaca, this is a public place. Please cooperate with my work; it will be better for all of us.]\n[And.] She knocked on the table, emphasizing seriously to Cynaca, [Regardless of your relationship with our Linker or whatever deal you've reached, you may call it whatever you like privately. But here in Leistance, you need to be mindful of the impression. You wouldn't want the Linker's personal image to be damaged, would you?]"
},
	[91197]={ language="Information One: The way she addresses Linker depends on her current mood, regardless of the occasion.\nInformation Two: Dragged Linker along to enroll in the Economics and Trade course at Lissugen Central University, but hardly attended any classes."
},
	[91198]={ language="Cynaca grew up in an orphanage in the capital of Libosellele—due to a tragic Mutant attack, she lost all of her family as a baby. The Liboselle government stepped in to properly place her, and over the years, she frequently appeared in front of the camera, sharing her childhood with the media and public, expressing gratitude for Liboselle's humane care.\nHowever, despite being the unofficial spokesperson for Liboselle, she seldom returned after gaining fame. She traveled all over Taino with her high Technology travel bag named Argo.\n[Why don't I want to go back?]Cynaca lay in a hammock, asking Linker to bring her the grape juice from the fridge. [You should drink some too. This is from Selevie, and if you don't drink it soon, I will finish it all.]\n[Just so you know, the next batch won't be until next year!] She plugged in a straw and took a big sip. [Every time I go back, even before passport control is done, reporters are waiting outside, and those bigwigs from the capital, they invite me to dinner under the guise of hospitality, but each has an ulterior motive. They all want to take a big cut from me.]\n[In every sense, I am lucky, but I'm also a businesswoman. It's my nature, or rather my goal, to secure enough benefits. I appreciate them, but I won't accept their limitless demands.]\n[I remember last time I went home, the old lady from the military department visited, wanting to dig some money out of me for some secret project.]\n[After I refused, she said I was too cold-hearted, that I could abandon the Liboselle which raised me, and if I continued like this, I'd eventually lose everything, ending up with just the money.]\n[How sad! She used to be such a kind lady.] Cynaca sighed. [But upon thinking about it, if I had lots of money, I would just have whatever I want, and that doesn't seem so bad.]\nShe put down the glass bottle, sat up, and reached out for a hug from Linker. [Besides, I don't just have money. I have you too, my dear Linker.]"
},
	[91199]={ language="Information One: Claims to be an honest businessman, though her business deals have some ties to the black market.\nInformation Two: Doesn't like living in Leistance dormitory and has a long-term stay package on the 42nd floor of the Lissugen Holiday Hotel."
},
	[91200]={ language="Real Name: Lorraine Selene\nIdentity: Star Knight of Vilatria Stellar Knights\nInterests: Reading novels"
},
	[91201]={ language="People often say that each of Vilatria's Star Knights represent a facet of the knighthood. Take the current generation of knights for example, Knight Lumen symbolizes wisdom and foresight, while Knight Flicker represents guard and order. But the third knight, named Luna… seems to be an anomaly.\nSince almost no one in Vilatria has seen the Luna Knight appear, it's impossible to determine which aspect of the knighthood Luna represents. People often ask, [Who is Luna?] Some suspect that this Star Knight doesn't even exist, and there are rumors that the so-called Luna Knight is actually a ghost, only appearing at night to silently guard Vilatria.\n[People are actually half right; Luna does prefer to appear at night. But as for the reason… you should know better than I do, Flicker.]\nTiya glanced at the attendance sheet Flicker handed over, noticing Luna's poor attendance record, and responded with a retort.\n[I did tell her that if she felt burdened inside, she could relieve it by reading novels, but she… clearly misunderstood my words.]\n[She treats novels as a part of her life, no, you could say it's the majority. She spends almost all day repeatedly watching them, completely going against my original intention.] Flicker explained helplessly, not expecting a simple suggestion to change Luna's lifestyle.\n[But she has indeed eased a lot. At least now she shows clear emotions because of the novel plots. Would you really want to see the old Luna, who was almost emotionless, no different from a puppet?]\n[...I just meant she should read the knight novels I recommended, not those… ahem, those focusing on romance.] Flicker coughed twice, turning her head awkwardly. She once visited Luna's home and saw some books in her room that shouldn't be openly placed on the bed, making her blush.\n[You mean… that kind of book?]\n[Don't act clueless, Tiya.]\n[Hehe, it's just a personal hobby. After all… everyone has certain desires.]\n[However… her fantasies seem to be getting more intense. Besides making her eyes extraordinarily sharp, the Fate Star also seems to amplify her desire to express emotions.]\n[Meaning what?] Flicker asked curiously.\n[A symptom of self-insertion deficiency, perhaps. When you watch too much, naturally you start imagining yourself as the characters. Haven't you ever imagined being the great shining knight in your novels?]\n[Let's not mention that anymore.]\n[Alright, alright, simply put… this kid is so engrossed in novels that she wishes she could have a beautiful or bittersweet romance like those heroines, even starting to fantasize.]\n[Is it serious?]\n[Well, it's serious, but not that serious.] Tiya placed her hands on the table, fingers intertwined, as if everything was under control.\n[Letting her truly experience it might just fulfill her dream and make her abandon her fantasies—though, it might make things worse, but it's worth a try.]\n[A real-life version of a novel hero?]\n[Luna isn't reading anything beyond reality, so such a person might exist. In fact… I already have the perfect candidate.]\n[We'll wait and see once Luna meets him.]"
},
	[91202]={ language="Information One: After becoming a Star Knight, Luna rarely shows up in the knight group, only appearing when she is needed for tasks.\nInformation Two: Luna's weapon, [Infinity Moonlight], is composed of twelve Moonblades, controlled through her telekinesis generated by Stellaron Resonance.\nInformation Three: The reason why Vilatria is little known is probably because Luna doesn't like to go out and dislikes socializing."
},
	[91203]={ language="1. A Bunch of Romance Novels on the Bookshelf: Luna's personal collection, all of which she's read over twenty times.\n2. An Unfinished Work: A novel Luna is writing featuring herself and Linker as the main characters, and they are currently gathering material together."
},
	[91204]={ language="Information One: It's said there's a wall in the room that's all bookshelves, filled with romance novels of various tastes and styles.\nInformation Two: Most of the novels Luna likes come from the Vilatria folk, and can often be bought at street stalls.\nInformation Three: In terms of novel taste and pursuit, Luna and Flicker are completely opposite; Flicker treats it as a hobby, while Luna treats it as life."
},
	[91205]={ language="Luna still vividly remembers the moment she deeply linked with Linker. \nIt was a feeling she'd never experienced before—satisfaction, joy, excitement... As she realized she'd remember him for the rest of her life, an idea began to form in Luna's heart.\nMaybe... she could try writing a novel, one that belonged to just the two of them.\nBut with this idea came the frustration—not enough material to tell the story, perhaps it was more of a longing for him.\nThe great emotional gap brought by the desire to create and her limited experiences made Luna feel annoyed, restless and uneasy.\n[Well then, let's start accumulating now.]\nWith this answer, Luna felt a sense of clarity within her heart.\nSince they hadn't experienced the past together, it wouldn't hurt to start from now. As long as they create memories together, little by little, and transform them into words on page after page... until it turned into a book with depth, the story would surely become unforgettable.\nAnd such a story would be uniquely hers, irreplaceable.\n[So, this wouldn't be a fantasy anymore, but a real-life story... Where should I start?] \nAt this moment, she's already the heroine of the story, with the hero extending an invitation.\nShe removes the veil from her eyes, her bright gaze like the moon, and happily takes his hand.\n[Let's start... with a date. My hero.]"
},
	[91206]={ language="Information One: After hearing from Tiya about who Linker is, Luna has been spending less time in the Knights' Order, possibly practicing social skills at home.\nInformation Two: Made quite a few handmade bookmarks, with more than half designed based on Linker's traits."
},
	[91207]={ language="Fifteen years ago—Private letter.\n[Dear Pope, going to Leistance will be my last step of Layout.]\n[After this, I will completely abandon myself to find His location.]\n[Even if I die, I will have no regrets, as I've left the future hope to these two children, one leaving Vilatria for Leistance, the other leaving Leistance for Vilatria, please take care of them.]\n[And Tiya and Clarence, they will be Vilatria's trump card against Him.]\n[Even if this causes our people to question and feel pain from zealous faith, we must face that disguised deity and tear off His mask.]\n[Vilatria's lie will someday end, I have done all possible remedies, next is your decision.]\n[I always believed Vilatria is still that nation blessed by the stars, Vilatria will flow with time and the stars as witness, never fading.]\n[Even though I might not see this day, I believe with these children, this day is not a fantasy but a tangible reality.]\n—Danica"
},
	[91208]={ language="Information One: After reading too many novels, she became increasingly envious of the love between the main characters and secretly wished she could have the same, and the moonlight responded to her prayers.\nInformation Two: She started trying to write, wanting to create a love story where she is the heroine and Linker is the hero."
},
	[91209]={ language="Real Name: Lithe Crianca Rogue\nIdentity: A person involved in the Lissugen network intrusion incident\nInterests: Contemplating life, reading news reports about Linker"
},
	[91210]={ language="The following is part of the interrogation record for HEL-9415:\nInterrogator: Isis Endaric\nInterrogation subject: Lithe Crianca Rogue\nAccompanying personnel: Linker\n…\n[Lithe Crianca Rogue, nationality: Hissrich... original name... HEL-9415, nationality unknown, age about 20, originated from the Onifer Laboratory, Type VII body.]\n[Type VII refers to human mechanization test subjects, transforming the human body into a special new material through the injection of specific gene drugs Remodel, while preserving personal consciousness... the meaning of 9415... quantity number, the 9415th test subject, the only successful one, with a mechanization level of 99%, the heart is still human, no attempts made in this aspect yet... there are three derivative clones, HEL-9415-III has been destroyed.]\n[My kind of body, none, at least not yet, that's why they let me go.]\nAnnotation: The interviewee has a strong identity with Crianca, further investigation into gene drugs and special materials is needed.\n[Experiment executors... all mechanical, with higher precision and execution than living people... living people? Two, one of whom is mother... and another person who saved me, is the gene source of FL-218, she told me to call her teacher, age... probably like what FL-218 appears to be... of high status, the name? Lira or Lina, referred to by someone with higher status. Some researchers hate her.]\n[And there was a doctor, teacher called her seelein, responsible for the HP of all test subjects... is female, I haven't seen her face... she's also an outsider... by outsider, I mean she was also a test subject, I don't know what she went through, she appeared suddenly, she dislikes Onifer as well and is one of the teacher's people.]\nAnnotation: There are internal disputes within Onifer, this could be a point of investigation.\n[Other experiment staff and subjects? Never came into contact... test subjects are merely consumables, everyone has their own containment chamber, never meeting... staff hardly ever appears in front of me, all experimental activities are performed by machinery.]\n[The fins and scales are a product of Shogger gene influence, intended to find an ancient city, the city is underwater... the city's name, maybe Lofino, that's how it sounded, I've only vaguely heard it... the mission hasn't started yet... gene combination is not complete enough.]\nAnnotation: This pronunciation sounds familiar, combined with the critical information about an underwater city, it bears similarity to known cities, a useful piece of Information.\n…\n[I've said everything I know, as per the conditions you agreed to in advance, where is Linker... I want to see him.]"
},
	[91211]={ language="Information One: She unexpectedly has a great talent for art.\nInformation Two: Acquired the entire estate of the Rogue family, but 90% was taken by Onifer.\nInformation Three: Once suffered from severe mental illness, now showing signs of improvement."
},
	[91212]={ language="1. One-way Eencryption Communication Device: Leistance's specially allocated secret communicator, only communication initiated by Linker.\n2. Used to collect special scales that fall off her body.\n3. Beauty Magazine: A book subscribed to every issue since meeting Linker.\n4. Polaroid Camera: The latest model of Polaroid camera, convenient for capturing Linker's heroic appearance anytime."
},
	[91213]={ language="Information One: Poor hearing but excellent vision, at two extremes.\nInformation Two: Dislikes dry environments, keeps a humidifier on 24/7.\nInformation Three: Got interested in makeup and dressing up after meeting Linker, currently trying to become Crianca."
},
	[91214]={ language="Rogue Mansion is a century-old building.\nIt is located on the outskirts of Lissugen and was lucky to survive the fierce anchor descent a hundred years ago. It changed hands several times until half a year ago when a young lady from Lod Coalition, Lithe Crianca Rogue, moved in and renamed it Rogue Mansion.\nAs an architectural work from the previous era, Rogue Mansion even has bizarre styles in its carvings—if you observe closely, you might find certain patterns that resemble those of the earliest discovered Shogger.\nMany speculate whether it's a matter of belief or art, suggesting these were elements popular in that era, passionately infused by artists into every aspect of life—yes, not just this building, all relics from that era feature similar patterns and decorations.\n[I can't look, I wanted to copy them... but halfway through, I felt dizzy… I saw monsters, loads of them! Those people were insane to use these things in architecture!] An art critic exclaimed angrily on the show.\n[Good heavens! It's a treasure! The pinnacle of human art! The creator was brilliant! I can't imagine what kind of genius could craft such artistic designs!] Another architect rebutted, even writing to the Lissugen government demanding its protection.\nBoth sides have their supporters, engaging in an ongoing debate, which has yet to reach a conclusion.\n\nWhen Crianca heard about this incident from Linker, her reaction was quite interesting: first confused, then she looked up at the ceiling and corner carvings, before displaying a peculiar expression, and finally laughing uncontrollably in Linker's arms—she claimed she rarely laughed so happily.\n[Without you telling me, I wouldn't have realized because these patterns are everywhere in Onifer.] Crianca picked up the tablet placed aside, opened a drawing app, trying to sketch similar images, [The difference is that most of Onifer's patterns are flat, and upon reflection, they do resemble Shogger in appearance…]\nShe quickly drew several special patterns vividly, which alone could remind one of some similar Shogger.\n[These are patterns inside the containment cabin, which I have seen often, so I paid no attention after moving in, thinking they were just Thaino's most common patterns.]\nLooking at Linker with a hint of apology, she said, [Next time 'Mother' lets me go back, I'll try to document more designs. If Onifer really has connections with that ancient country you mentioned, this might become a breakthrough.]"
},
	[91215]={ language="Information One: Her ear fins are the result of some Shogger gene influence, but publicly claimed to be hearing aids.\nInformation Two: Although planning to pull herself together and live well, she still doesn't like going out."
},
	[91216]={ language="Crianca's room has a newspaper collection.\nIt's a notorious tabloid, with the headline of the current issue showing a gruesome photo: a severely injured middle-aged woman. She is Curd Rogue, the famous movie star born in Burksomi. During a family trip, their car was hit by an out-of-control large truck. Curd's husband, Rogue's senator from Lod Coalition, died on the spot. Curd herself died shortly after being taken to the hospital, and only their daughter Crianca survived by luck.\nIt is said they were trying to escape from paparazzi chasing them from behind when they failed to pay attention to the road situation and couldn't avoid the oncoming truck.\nAfter the accident, the paparazzi immediately photographed the tragic scene and then contacted the nearest hospital, which caused Curd to miss the best time for treatment.\nDuring Lithe Crianca Rogue's hospitalization, despite the strict guard by the Hissrich government, the address of the hospital and her ward number were discovered by Curd's fanatic fans, forcing Lithe Crianca Rogue to transfer hospitals and undergo cosmetic surgery in Uzyanta.\n...\n[…The doctor who arrived at the scene was from Onifer, and by that time Lithe Crianca Rogue was already dead. The person brought to the hospital was actually me… This is the whole process of me, under 'mother's' arrangement, replacing her and becoming the new Crianca, as I told you before. And this newspaper has been trying to find me... planning to use my...] Crianca paused slightly before continuing, [planning to use Crianca's situation as a gimmick to make a lot of money from mom's fans. After the accident, this photo was sold for a fortune by the paparazzi, leading to furious fans storming this newspaper office.]\n[Indeed, 'mother' was involved in this because she wanted to erase all traces of Lithe Crianca Rogue on Taino Star, making my legitimate identity more seamless and easier to take over all assets belonging to Lithe Crianca Rogue and her parents... The proceeds from these things were mostly taken by Onifer for research.]\n[I feel very sorry about Lithe Crianca Rogue's tragedy. As for the cause of the accident, I'm not sure whether Onifer orchestrated all this or if it was just a coincidence.] She closed her eyes, showing a sad expression, [but regardless of which, I, HEL-9415, have become the new Crianca after all this, and will continue to live on this planet under this identity... I read Lithe Crianca Rogue's journal. She liked reading, dancing, and dreamed of one day seeing real daylight. We are completely different people, even our dreams are worlds apart... I am not worthy to become her...]\n[I once thought about letting this identity die completely... Luckily, I truly saw and touched you, you showed me the possibility of resisting Onifer, now I no longer desire death, that day is still far away, I want to live...]\nShe says as she holds Linker's hand, softly rubbing his palm, [I want to live with you, and someday, I want to change my last name to yours, just like they do in Hissrich.]"
},
	[91217]={ language="Information One: She's never drunk alcohol, but under Linker's encouragement, she tried for the first time and got very drunk.\nInformation Two: When emotionally excited or during intense exercise, the scales on her body fall off, but after a while, they return to normal."
},
	[91218]={ language="Real Name: Adenie\nIdentity: Leistance Operator, Knight Selection Contest Candidate\nInterests: Stargazing, Gardening"
},
	[91219]={ language="During the years at Leistance, Adenie never mentioned her past life in Vilatria. Her records all started from when she became an AIMBS Operator. On the day of the divine blood surgery, when Deputy Director Krull Seiber questioned her, she replied to him.\n[Undergoing the surgery means you'll completely lose all traces of Stellar Knights. Are you willing?]\n[I am, it's all for Vilatria.]\n[—From now on, your code name will be Dawn.]\nAfter transforming into Dawn, Adenie never mentioned her homeland again but still cherished every letter from the knights. However, following Danica's advice, she chose silence and never replied, as if she had quietly vanished from the land of Vilatria without a trace.\nUntil the day she went to Vilatria to pick up Linker, a series of shocking news hit Adenie like surging waves. Upon learning of Danica's death, Adenie realized: her fate was woven long ago, and countless lives were sacrificed in pursuit of that unattainable goal. The blood and sins did not disappear when she became an Operator but accumulated into a heavy burden, pushing Adenie to the edge of the abyss along with the so-called [hope.]\nIf it weren't for Linker's presence, if it weren't for that night when she cried out in front of him, Adenie couldn't predict what path she would have taken. Perhaps she would have become a hollow shell filled with resentment, like those who passed.\nDanica once told her that the sword would witness all her experiences. It was once forgotten because of her self-exile, but now it shines again with a sharp glow because of her vow.\nLater, during a mission, Adenie recalled that night, only to smile slightly as she sheathed her sword.\n[Back then, I needed a reason to keep going, and Linker happened to become that, just like the 'coincidence' of being assigned to take him away from Vilatria that first time… all these coincidences molded my new life.]\n[Like unpredictable yet unavoidable fate, it tied my early life to Vilatria, and now… everything will be closely connected with him.]\n[Those tears, those pains, will transform into the strength I need to fight for him and for everything I love.]"
},
	[91220]={ language="Information One: She let go of the grudges from the past and, with her heart pledged to Linker, became a new knight.\nInformation Two: After identifying as [Linker's knight,] no longer accepts any knight titles, and continues to be active as a Leistance cooperation Operator.\nInformation Three: Her new weapon is a modification of the one used during the knight corps period, and due to its unique design, only Linker and a few Star Knights have seen the true form of the weapon."
},
	[91221]={ language="1. Delicate Dried Flowers: Filled with a girl's heartfelt intentions, crafted solely for the one person she's devoted to, one of a kind in the world.\n2. Vilatria's Stellar Knights Medal: A medal that should have been returned to the Knights upon returning to Vilatria, but was ultimately given back to Dawn by Tiya, as the Knight Commander."
},
	[91222]={ language="Information One: Dawn's sword was designed and crafted by Danica, and she often uses swordsmanship as her combat method, while she learned spear techniques at Leistance.\nInformation Two: The letters received at Leistance were all sent by the Knights, but she only replied once before leaving, saying she would return to Vilatria.\nInformation Three: During the selection tournament, she frequently had tutorials with Linker, losing more than winning."
},
	[91223]={ language="During one day of the selection conference, Adenie found you.\n[Want me to be your tutorial partner?]\n[Tiya's not too good at close combat, Flicker's busy with missions, and after thinking about it, you're the best fit for a sparring partner, Linker.] Adenie tossed an unsharpened sword to you.\n[I'm not that great at hand-to-hand combat either, else Isis wouldn't have equipped me with a gun—]\n[You think I don't know your academy scores? Not only did you break all records since the academy was founded, but no one has surpassed you even now... Although I haven't gone on missions with you much, I have memorized your files inside out.] Adenie raised an eyebrow, shoving the sword into your hand.\n[Just accompany me for a bit, I want you to see a different battle style of mine.]\n[Okay, but I have one condition.] You point the sword at Adenie. [The loser has to agree to one request from the winner.]\n[Hah, you think you'll beat me and start making demands? Sure thing, but the one losing will be you.]\nYou were silent for a while, then picked up the sword.\nHalf an hour later, you put down the sword and looked at the knight, who was breathing heavily and kneeling on the ground, resembling a winner. [You really underestimated me... You're swinging weakly, your strikes are sloppy, and your reactions are slow. Is this it?]\n[Ugh, why do you sound so smug like Danica...]\n[But deputy director Seiber and Isis weren't lying to me. Without using Stellaron Resonance, just looking at your physical abilities, you're like a monster.]\n[Thanks for the compliment. But I'm not a devil either, my request is simple.]\n[Take a stroll with me around Stardom, eat and drink, just like an idle ordinary person—and then go back to Asteria's house and sleep well.]\n[...That's it?]\n[That's it. You need to relax a bit, Dawn, you've barely left the tutorial field this whole time, staying too tense and you'll eventually snap.]\n[Aren't you the same? The one more tense than I am... is you.] The knight put away her sword and reverted to the girl full of mischievous warmth.\n[...So you lost to me on purpose?]\n[Who knows, but I've agreed to your request.] Dawn folded her hands behind her back, turned her head to look at you, her smile like morning sunshine.\n[Shall we go, Linker?]"
},
	[91224]={ language="Information One: Once grew a small flower garden in Vilatria, which was abandoned due to leaving. Upon returning, she scattered seeds with Linker, looking forward to the day they bloom.\nInformation Two: Although quite knowledgeable about astrology and constellations, didn't manage to figure out the relationship with Linker, and is thus annoyed."
},
	[91225]={ language="[Leistance News Record\n[Encryption Level: Highest]\n[Extracting Record—]\n...\nMiss Adenie's D-Blood surgery is complete, Deputy Seiber.\nSince Stellaron Resonance is a product of the gene chain, her Stellaron Resonance won't be affected by what you mentioned as [special entity] mental contamination invasion. By the way, if that [special entity] is truly an apostle-level Shogger, another issue arises.\n...Alright, let me explain in detail.\nAdenie... oh, now she should be called Dawn. Although she is isolated from apostle-level Shogger's mental contamination due to the divine blood surgery, you mentioned that in the country called Vilatria, there are several star knights like her... Those knights haven't undergone D-Blood surgery, so how are they facing the mental contamination from apostle-level Shogger?\nPure willpower? That does account for some part of it, but from a more scientific perspective, there must be a fundamental reason.\nYes, exactly... In fact, we've discovered some clues in Dawn's mental consciousness simulation. Just like the D-Blood surgery I just talked about, her sea of consciousness simulated something like a [barrier,] which is more similar to an electromagnetic force field, protecting her mental world from another electromagnetic force field invasion, namely, the mental contamination of apostle-level Shogger.\nPerhaps other star knights are similarly protected by this mysterious [barrier,] but... the barrier in the Dawn Operator's consciousness is very weak, like a thin sheet of paper.\nIf we apply this result to those knights... the situation may not be so optimistic, Deputy Seiber."
},
	[91226]={ language="Information One: After returning to Vilatria, she still loves the nights in Stardom, but prefers the starry sky when there's someone special beside her.\nInformation Two: After a transformation of mind, she no longer hides her love for red roses and later seeks advice from Rose on cultivation methods."
},
	[91227]={ language="Real Name: Shuang\nIdentity: Wandering Taoist of Spark, Yan's senior sister, Frost Jade's junior sister\nInterests: Cooking, Divination"
},
	[91228]={ language="Since Yunzhuan joined Leistance, the chefs in the Leistance logistics department have significantly improved their skills. As a result, many have gained weight to varying degrees, with Linker being the most affected.\nEvery morning at eight, random pastries and drinks appear on Linker's desk.\nAt four in the afternoon, Yunzhuan would knock on Linker's office door with her prepared afternoon tea.\nIf Linker works late occasionally, there would be fruit, milk, or other snacks she personally prepared.\n…………\nThe occupancy rate of Leistance's gym has started to drop.\nEveryone gradually felt a sense of crisis and began to line up to book gym slots.\nThe gym lights often stay on all night, sparking a fitness craze within Leistance.\nOne afternoon on a day off, as Linker emerged from the gym, he saw Yunzhuan waiting at the door with a smile, holding a plate of golden-yellow puff pastries.\n[Soft and crispy, really good!] She picked one up and offered it to Linker's lips, [Want to try?]\n……\n[Yeah!] No one can resist the aroma of pastries. Tasting the freshly baked pastry from Yunzhuan's hand, Linker went back to the office, and the two happily enjoyed another afternoon tea.\n\nGaining weight, losing it through exercise, and enjoying food to gain it back again.\n\nIsn't that a kind of balance."
},
	[91229]={ language="Information One: No dietary restrictions when it comes to eating.\nInformation Two: Skilled in fortune telling, with a unique method that seems a bit unconventional.\nInformation Three: Enjoys experimenting with desserts and feeding Linker regularly."
},
	[91230]={ language="Cookbook: A book with lots of recipes for making delicious food.\nSeasoning Combo: Shuang's secret weapon. It's her trick to make dishes tasty and the key to surviving when eating out.\nTravel Journal: A journal filled with interesting stories from the journey.\nGossip Mirror: A small copper mirror carried around that is said to ward off evil and disaster.\nTalismans And Cinnabar: Tools used for making talismans."
},
	[91231]={ language="Information One: Although she loves sharing, only she can understand the recipes she writes.\nInformation Two: The amulet papers she creates are hot-selling items within Leistance.\nInformation Three: She doesn't like arguing and fighting, but she's not afraid of confrontation."
},
	[91232]={ language="Yunzhuan took a long time to apply for a private residence at Leistance.\nGetting a bigger room was easy, having windows facing east wasn't hard, being close to the Linker office wasn't tricky either, and having the stove in the southern part of the room wasn't a problem. But when these conditions combined, the housing department head almost exploded, angrily and reluctantly knocking on Linker's office—before the room was arranged, Yunzhuan temporarily replenished her energy here.\nFacing the middle-aged woman who sighed and rubbed her forehead, Yunzhuan used her understanding nature and persuasive charm. The matter ended with the head promising to arrange a suitable room for her. Witnesses said the head had a big smile while leaving with a box of Spark specialty snacks, as if encountering a great fortune.\n[Treat people with courtesy~,] Yunzhuan said to Linker, who was equally curious about the situation, as she waved the paper talisman, [I need something from people, naturally I have to reciprocate, it's the way of life.]\nA month later, the girl came with a fruit basket, snacks, and a stack of talisman papers.\n[These are fruits I bought at the market, these are tea leaves I got from my senior sister, and this!] She took out a pack of dried fruits from the bottom of the basket, [These are precious fruits from my hometown, handmade before leaving, all for you to enjoy!]\nThe gifts Yunzhuan brought piled up like a hill on Linker's desk. The girl propped herself against the desk and peeked from behind, [By hometown tradition, when moving into a new home, you invite friends and family, bringing luck and wealth. If an elder can stay for two nights, it would be even better!]\nWith a light tone, she quickly eased Linker's concerns, [It's true! You can ask my senior sister; she'd never deceive you... After much thought, the most suitable person is obviously you, Linker. Asking you is far more effective than those mud statues.]\n[So, what did you say to the Dorm head?] Linker finally asked the question everyone cared about.\n[I just gave her a fortune reading.] Yunzhuan sighed, speaking frankly, [I told her about her recent luck and possible events, and how to resolve them, then gifted a box of snacks. She was thrilled.]\n[Of course, I was thrilled too,] she added, [Someone was enchanted by the great and mysterious Spark culture.]\n[Can Linker help me with this favor?] The focus returned to the original topic, the girl gazed with big, sparkling eyes waiting for Linker's answer.\n[Alright, once I finish this report.]\nUpon Linker's consent, Yunzhuan jumped with joy, [I'll prepare afternoon tea for you~.]\nShe dashed out and then poked her head back in from the door, [It's settled, no backing out!]"
},
	[91233]={ language="Information One: A bit of directionally challenged.\nInformation Two: After spending a long time together, Linker gradually deciphered her writing."
},
	[91234]={ language="Yunzhuan was passionate about everything related to her hometown.\nThe glory of Spark's culture is bright and eternal like stars in the sky. She often boasts about this to her friends, then eagerly talks about everything about Spark.\nSpark civilization is the greatest on Taino star. Yunzhuan avidly and consistently spreads this belief to everyone.\nAfter leaving Spark, her first stop was a land covered with tundra and snow, where temperatures were always low. There, Yunzhuan got the mushrooms she'd been longing for, but before heading home, she received a message from her sect asking her to meet fellow travelers in Lissugen.\nUpon reaching Lissugen, Yunzhuan was greatly impressed by the city with deep historical roots.\nThe abundant historical sites and museum collections fascinated Yunzhuan, and some special recipes she discovered there made her extremely happy. The biggest surprise, of course, was meeting Linker, described in Spark's terms as, [With a unique fate, unmatched in the past five hundred years,] a person whose future cannot be seen even by asking the heavens, drawing Yunzhuan's attention even more.\n\nOn the morning she left Lissugen, Yunzhuan arranged to meet Linker early, nervously inviting him, [Linker, if you get the chance, you must visit Spark.]\n[I represent my hometown, that mysterious and ancient land, welcoming you, and I'm sure you will love it.]\nBefore parting, Yunzhuan once again solemnly reminded.\n[It's okay if you can't come right now. Before you reach there, I'll wait for you, until we meet… this period of waiting is forever.]"
},
	[91235]={ language="Information One: Seems like a recluse, but actually a kid at heart.\nInformation Two: Her ultimate dream is to create a seasoning that makes all food delicious."
},
	[91236]={ language="Real Name: Lux Blore\nIdentity: Weapons Technician\nInterests: Fairy tales, lemonade, cartoons, observing flora and fauna"
},
	[91237]={ language="When Butterfly first stepped onto the Leistance ship, her little toe had an intimate encounter with the automatic door; she accidentally sneezed while receiving water from the staff, spraying everyone... She managed to experience almost every kind of embarrassing moment imaginable.\n[She even mixed up the men's and women's changing rooms. Luckily, only Linker was inside, or it could've been a big problem.]\n[I think her fainting after seeing Linker's bare upper body is already a problem.]\nSurprisingly, Butterfly is excellent at housekeeping. Butterfly can make delicious treats and once became the ship's most popular afternoon tea snack; she's very diligent and keeps her room and the hallway next to it spotless.\nIf you ask her, she'll happily accept cleaning requests. But if you're curious about her room, she'll suddenly block the door, blushing and gesturing for you to stop.\nHer overly cute reactions make a few mischievous AIMBS occasionally come over to [tease] Butterfly, then have her clean their rooms.\nRecommended by Linker, Butterfly accepted a research commission from Leistance. Although her colleagues in the research department were skeptical, Butterfly soon proved her professional skills from her previous work at Divinelight Heavy Tech's Crystal Weapon Department. When Butterfly was engaged in research work, her precise operations and meticulous programming not only ensured she didn't make mistakes but also considered her colleagues' steps.\nWith Butterfly's help, the development of the new batch of Aimbs standard armament for Leistance was significantly accelerated, completing the planned indicators a month in advance.\nAfter completing the research commission and study exchange at Leistance, Butterfly left the ship and returned to Zambra City, restarting her dessert shop while collaborating with the Latif family and the Wanderers Guild in Leistance's name. However, she still sends handmade treats back to Leistance.\nAs for the recipient, everyone can guess with their eyes closed."
},
	[91238]={ language="Information One: Butterfly defected from Divinelight Heavy Tech, but didn't kill any pursuers.\nInformation Two: Has a special preference for lemonade, and reportedly from those who've had AIMBS, Butterfly's lemonade is acidic enough to poison an adult elephant.\nInformation Three: Butterfly claims not to be socially anxious, just has relatively weak social skills. Always rehearses before meeting unfamiliar people."
},
	[91239]={ language="1. Juicer: A juicer specifically for squeezing lemons, assembled by Butterfly herself.\n2. Divinelight Heavy Tech Access Card: The only item she has related to Shenguang Heavy Tech, used to reminisce about her happy days there.\n3. [Big Blue Butterfly] Specimen Ornament: A precious gift found after a long search by someone very, very important in Selevie, always placed by her bedside."
},
	[91240]={ language="Information One: She really likes cartoons and comics that kids enjoy. It's said that her room and bed sheets are so cute they make people uncomfortable.\nInformation Two: Butterfly's exoskeleton weapon is called [Fluttering Moth Type 1.] This name expresses her dislike for Divinelight Heavy Tech, but since Linker liked the name, she started to like it too.\nInformation Three: Butterfly acquired her pastry-making skills from her mother. Her pastries are so delicious that she could make a fortune just by opening a pastry shop."
},
	[91241]={ language="Butterfly, Real Name Lux Blore. She was born into a middle-class family that never worried about food or clothing, and her mother was a professor of Energy at Belsogimi National Defense University. With a good family background and excellent genetic inheritance, Butterfly showed extraordinary intelligence and talent from a young age—by the age of 4, she could already solve her mother's final exam questions.\nBut every genius seems to encounter the same trouble in socializing: due to her outstanding intelligence, Butterfly's words and actions were completely different from those of her peers, making her an [outcast] in the Ravend.\nAfter being teased once, she ran home crying, locked the door, and wrapped herself in a quilt.\nIn the end, Professor Bloor knocked on the door and brought a fairy tale comic, sitting beside her daughter.\n[Little Lux, shall I tell you a story?]\n[Once upon a time, there was a caterpillar with colorful skin. Because its colors were different from the surrounding green-grey caterpillars, it was ridiculed and envied by everyone.]\n[The caterpillar was very sad, but didn't lose heart, because it was striving to become a butterfly just like the other caterpillars.]\n[It worked hard to gnaw leaves, striving to build up its body. Gradually, it found its goal and direction: It wanted to become the shiniest butterfly of all, to fly over mountains and glide in the sky.]\n[It accumulated enough strength; its beautiful body made all the surrounding caterpillars admire and aspire to be like it, but its growing size also attracted the attention of predators. Thus, it kept escaping and escaping...]\n[Then... what happened next?] Attracted by the story, Lux finally poked her messy head out from the quilt.\n[Later, it thought of a way. It fused its silk with leaves to make a protective cocoon. Thanks to this seemingly sturdy and inconspicuous cocoon, it indeed avoided many predators.]\n[But eventually, one day, a fierce bird discovered it.] Professor Bloor noticed her daughter's shivering and gently hugged Lux.\n[Just as the bird was about to peck at the cocoon, suddenly, a butterfly burst in. This butterfly was all black, like an elf of the night.]\n[The black butterfly blocked the bird's beak, protecting the cocoon from being pecked. The bird was very angry and aggressively attacked the black butterfly, trying to eat it.]\n[No way! The black butterfly is protecting the caterpillar!] Out of nowhere, little Lux broke free from her mother's embrace, with clenched fists and eyes suddenly filled with spirit.\nProfessor Blore smiled and lightly pinched her daughter's nose, and continued, [Yes, that's exactly what the caterpillar thought. So it endured intense pain and desperately broke out of the cocoon.]\n[At that moment, the black butterfly witnessed the birth of a miracle: as vast as the ocean, as pure as the sky, a deep blue butterfly fluttered its wings, creating a storm that blew the bird away effortlessly.]\nProfessor Blore looked into her daughter's eyes and peacefully said, [So my little caterpillar, see, you've broken out of your cocoon as well.]\n[Find a goal and strive towards it; only then will you encounter this black butterfly, giving you the strength to break through the cocoon.]"
},
	[91242]={ language="Information One: Before meeting Linker in Zambra City, she wrote a thick stack of papers on what to say, but not a single word was used.\nInformation Two: The inspiration for the first modification of [Fluttering Moth] actually came after meeting Linker."
},
	[91243]={ language="Unlike the vigilance and hostility from Burksomi official channels, Divinelight Heavy Tech showed a great deal of friendliness and trust towards Leistance. Their Anima Crystal Weapon department frequently engaged in academic exchanges with the Leistance Institute. Butterfly learned about Leistance from colleagues who participated in such exchanges.\nHowever, it wasn't until a new order from Rose landed in her hands that she became aware of Linker's existence. It was the first time Butterfly saw Rose so invested in a specific person, which made her also feel a certain anticipation and longing for this Linker mentioned by Rose.\n[Could he be the black butterfly I've been searching for?]\nWhen Linker threw himself into the line of fire to shield her from the armored soldiers, Butterfly was reminded of a scene from a fairy tale her mother used to tell, where the black butterfly collided with the bird's beak. After linking with Linker through the divine blood link, Butterfly became even more convinced that Linker was the hero who would bring purpose to her life and break her out of her cocoon.\nShe found some prized possessions she brought from DivinelightHeavy Tech in her depot, and, using Leistance's technology, personally designed an intelligent AI to assist with the control of the floating cannons, as well as adding a disperser to the exoskeleton on her back to alleviate mental stress... Inspiration kept flowing from her mind.\n[If... If these things can help relieve Linker of some stress, that would be great.] Butterfly murmured to herself with a smile while focused on her modifications, unaware that Rose was standing at the workshop door recording with a mischievous grin on her face.\nAfterward, with Butterfly almost on the verge of tears pleading, Rose finally agreed not to send the recording to Linker."
},
	[91244]={ language="Information One: Butterfly's [unconventional] outfits are actually inspired by learning from Rose. She hopes to dress nicely in front of Linker, but always ends up being teased by friends.\nInformation Two: Butterfly added requests for [cushion filling] and a [3D printer] to the order she submitted to the purchasing department. Later, Isis approved the requests in front of Linker, who showed a fascinating expression."
},
