},
	[112205]={ language=""
},
	[112206]={ language="Following a transmitter with ocean currents, it doesn't seem to belong to this era. As you get closer, you notice the surrounding seawater is rhythmically vibrating—maybe it's not damaged and has been emitting radio waves all along?\nYour mission is to find the source of the unknown signal. How connected might it be to the signal...?"
},
	[112207]={ language="After entering the outskirts of the abandoned ruins, you find the area littered with the wreckage of ships and submarines. Nearby, a small cluster of Void Particles is swirling lightly, seemingly directly connected to the disaster. Of course, at this time, its Energy is almost depleted, no longer posing a threat."
},
	[112208]={ language="In the darkness, you hear footsteps ahead—it doesn't sound robotic. It seems like some huge creature is moving through there. Relying on your past experiences, you quickly determine it must be a Mutant living here, and it will soon be near you. There's no time to hesitate!"
},
	[112209]={ language="On the open ground inside the fort, an escape pod is stuck upside down. Its transparent glass cabin is shattered, and the alarm's red light is still stubbornly flashing, yet it's empty inside—perhaps the former pilot managed to escape? You can almost envision the tragedy it went through. After a brief moment of silence in your heart, you gaze at it, lost in thought."
},
	[112210]={ language="Now you're in the heart of the abandoned city, where robots work methodically, coexisting peacefully with the roaming Mutants, making you feel quite astonished and amazed.\nThis means you need to be extra cautious to avoid getting entangled with them. Just as everything seems to be going smoothly, you suddenly notice something glimmering in the darkness not far away, but nearby, a giant Mutant is sleeping..."
},
	[112211]={ language="You once again noticed that mysterious signal, like sound waves penetrating your cochlea, slightly piercing and accompanied by severe headache. Almost simultaneously, you felt a special fluctuation, and some blurry illusions gradually appeared before your eyes.\nMaybe it's better to take some measures."
},
	[112212]={ language="You walk into a tall building: the ceiling of this room is leaking with a drippy noise, and the place is filled with the smell of rusted metal and sea water. But more than these, what catches your attention is the machine in the center of the room.\nThe screen of the silicon crystal is bright blue, constantly beeping warnings. Based on past experiences, there should be robots here, but as you look around, there's nothing but the machine.\nThe machine starts beeping wildly, and you feel a burst of Stun, while outside, you vaguely hear the sounds of a Mutant."
},
	[112213]={ language="You have no idea how long you've wandered through the ruins. There's no street ahead anymore, nor are there any strangely-behaving robots. In front of you appears a glass house, surrounded by some eerie statues—if analyzed from the perspective of biological science, they should belong to Shogger—you indeed recognize some of them, as you've seen on the battlefield.\nYou cautiously walked in; the glass house is empty except for a large pool in the center, and further back, there are faint sounds of Mutant."
},
	[112214]={ language="You pass by an abandoned laboratory, and a mechanical being sits on a round stool at the door watching you.\n[I am the last remnant of the Infeno Biological Institute.] Its mechanical voice is magnetic, [I was once admired by every citizen as the highest achievement of Inferno Biological Technology research, but I'm about to fail. It's an honor to meet you before my power system fails. Please take a part of me as a historical keepsake.]"
},
	[112215]={ language="A mechanical host stands on a high platform holding a microphone, its steel skin shimmering with sparks, [We need you, for our country, please donate one-tenth of a drop of blood.] \nIt turns its electronic compound eye towards you, [Sir, your left pocket is shining, you will receive satisfactory compensation.]"
},
	[112216]={ language="You tried to start up the abandoned machine, and it immediately emitted a clanging metal sound. The next moment, the glass compartment was filled with capsule balls.\nLooking at the shaky, old machine, you unexpectedly found a metal coin next to it.\nWanna give it a shot?"
},
	[112217]={ language="[I, Thomas Campbell, am the richest and most generous entrepreneur in Infeno; my wealth is the cornerstone of Infino's technological progress.] A face appeared on the electronic screen, speaking formally, [I am committed to eliminating all poverty within the country. Poor people can enjoy my wealth, and wealthy people can also be free from worry because of it.]"
},
	[112218]={ language="[My successors will roam the Taino Star,] shouted a young man with long purple hair. [Many years later, the name Lancelot will thrive, while Campbell will be buried in dust.]\n[History will only remember the Campbell family,] the person across from him replied fiercely. [Your name will decay along with your body.]\nThe arguing pair noticed you.\nThe young man with purple hair looked at you and handed you a blood-stained circuit board.\n[This is the treasure of the Lancelot family. Please help me repair it.]"
},
	[112219]={ language="[Hey, wait up!] The mechanical philosopher with a basket of metal components called out to you, [We were all once exiled beings, but now our nation holds the key to becoming a higher civilization.]\n[I invite you to join our society; you will be the first ordinary human to step into the advanced society of Infeno.]"
},
	[112220]={ language="[We've discovered the gene fragments of a superior civilization!] shouted the scientist in a lab coat excitedly, [This must be the Creator's gift!]\n[Thank the Creator!] He knelt on the ground, his mechanical knee cracked from impact, [What are you waiting for, join me in prayer.]\n[She will take us further.]"
},
	[112221]={ language="You pass by a library, the vine-like totems on the wall make you feel stunned, and a bit nauseous.\nStanding at the door, a mechanical being waves to you enthusiastically, showing you the books in its arms.\n[Infeno's research can no longer progress further.]\n[As you see, I'm just a gatekeeper of this library. Long ago, I was banished here due to disagreeing with the upper echelons.]\n[You would agree with my view, right? Ultimate science will eventually lead to doom.]"
},
	[112222]={ language="[Your Majesty, as a token of your acceptance, I will offer you the secrets of high civilization Technology.] \nThe robed woman said obsequiously. You rubbed your eyes and noticed tendrils of light flowing around feet hidden by her robe. She looked at you, and a one-eyed creature emerged from her collar, both showing the same fierce glance. \n[Stay quiet!] the woman told you."
},
	[112223]={ language="[How can those inferior kingdoms compare with the great Infeno?]\nEmperor Infeno sternly rebuked the envoy from Vilatria, [Tell your pope to stop dreaming about cooperation.]\nThe envoy wanted to say more, but the emperor gave you a look."
},
	[112224]={ language="[Warrior!] The mechanical being pats your shoulder, its alloy skeleton creaking, [I am about to declare war on the Mutants gathered in the wilderness on behalf of the great Infeno Kingdom.]\n[After such a long rest, I feel like my nuts and bolts have rusted.] He raised his arm, and iron filings immediately fell from the mechanical gaps.\n[Find a solution for me, the warriors of Infeno cannot fall just like that.]"
},
	[112225]={ language="You look up and see a crack in the sky, with a huge anchor hanging high, ready to fall at any moment.\nYou look around and find countless residents of Puruis kneeling on the ground, arms raised, muttering prayers for the Creator's protection, but it doesn't slow the anchor's descent.\n[Please guide us to the path of survival.]"
},
	[112226]={ language="[I've been waiting here for over a hundred years,] the vine plant spoke, [Since this city was founded, I've been here. The great Campbell family gave me this mission.] \n[Honored guest, as you can see, they still haven't arrived. If you've seen them, could you tell me about their situation?] \n[Or perhaps, you could go inquire with the Campbell family for me? I will provide you with a token for passage.] \nUnfortunately, the people it awaited have long been lost to history, and you can't help but ponder whether to reveal the truth to it."
},
	[112227]={ language="[To treat infectious diseases and let infected humans live longer, our predecessors created machines, then transplanted the consciousness of every living being onto them. This way, we are no longer afraid of alien life and Taino Star monsters' interference. That's the origin of this procedure.]\nYou glanced at the restraints on your body.\n[Of course, we won't force any resident to accept us,] the mechanical doctor added to you. [The decision is still in your hands. You can choose to accept it, and your consciousness will eternally live with the machine. If you refuse, we respect your choice and feel regretful for it.]"
},
	[112228]={ language="[On that day, we'll enter the newborn Puruis, living eternally by the Creator's side, Infeno's glory will last forever along with the Creator's true name.]\nThe elegantly dressed mechanical woman stood on the stage, passionately speaking, her mechanical body covered in rust. [All the elderly, the young, and the little children will enjoy the same honor as Her Highness, all will gaze upon her brilliance.]\nThe surrounding residents rushed forward eagerly.\n[And you, young sir?] the mechanical being inquired of you."
},
	[112229]={ language="As research intensifies in the city, a large number of Mutants have emerged on the plains east of Puruis, which is not good news for the residents.\nThe city is in a state of panic. After the Elder Council meeting, spearheaded by Duke Campbell, it was decided that the Lancelot family's Elite would lead the charge to eliminate the Mutants outside the city.\nDuke Campbell righteously proclaims the significance of this war to the people, and amidst the cheers, you feel no excitement at all, even sighing in despair—you, who happened to be passing by, got swept into the departing Ravend; the only good news is that you have a slight choice in the mission you'll undertake."
},
	[112230]={ language="Mechanical beings are standing on the street more and more, uniformly looking at you as you cross the road.\nThey're just harmless robots! You think to yourself but can't help speeding up your pace.\nA robot stopped you, its waist part damaged, hunched over like an old man, [Kind young man, please pause for a moment and listen to me.]\n[I'm about to become a discarded metal husk, and soon my companions will end up like me, then all become the majority of mechanical scraps you see, casually piled on the street, but kind guest, please find us some parts.]\nIt points to the distant tower."
},
	[112231]={ language="You passed by the city memorial square and saw the robots working fervently.\nThey were kneeling on the ground, piecing together the mechanical parts on the ground bit by bit, forming patterns that were entangled together. You tried to distinguish them but felt a wave of discomfort, and waves of Stun washed over you, making you almost want to vomit.\nYou stopped a robot next to you that looked like a supervisor for inquiry. It was startled by your question, showing a pixelated question mark on its mechanical face and loudly rebuked your rudeness, saying, [This is the creator's teachings. Once the totem is complete, the great Infeno will transcend the shackles of Taino star and become an even greater civilization.]"
},
	[112232]={ language="[We must ensure fairness.] Duke Campbell tapped the table and emphasized to you again, [I will quickly request the Elder Council to initiate the Taino Currency System plan, to expedite the implementation of the Infino silver Coins, making them the universal currency for trade on the Taino star.]\n[So, dear sir, don't worry about Infino's credibility. Your trust today will bring Uzyanta a very substantial foreign exchange reserve, and Infeno will also benefit from this mineral trade.]"
},
	[112233]={ language="You look towards the western sky—the direction of Puruis. Ever since you and your companions were sent here by Duke Campbell to parry Mutants, you often do this.\nAt this moment, the sky seems to be teetering, something rapidly falling from it, followed by a massive roaring sound—it all happens almost instantly.\nPerhaps you should go back and check, but before setting off, you need to pick up some weapons.\n[Leave everything to the Creator!] the logistics officer flicks away his cigarette butt, [Wanna bet with me? Win and you'll get your weapons, lose and we'll duel.]"
},
	[112234]={ language="The researcher who left home finally returned to his hometown, but he was turned away—because he came back from that nameless place. \nA generous selfless helper lost his home and had to move on.You met him in the wilderness.\n[Please help me.] He reached out to you, [I have no choice but to return to that nameless place, but the parts on my feet can't support me walking back.]"
},
	[112235]={ language="You open your eyes and find yourself strapped to an operating table again.\nA female robot in a white nurse uniform stops beside you. She bends down, and due to the rust on her equipment, the movement is quite difficult.\nShe offers you a gorgeous potion, enticingly colored and sweet-scented, [This contains genes from an extraterrestrial civilization. You are honored to be our first test subject.]\nEven though you know you're just repeating the simulation recorded inside the machine, you can't help but wonder what the consequences of drinking it would be."
},
	[112236]={ language="Several corpses of Infeno merchants were discovered at the Uzyanta border, prompting the Infeno Elder Council to hold the Uzyanta government accountable.\nInfeno's artificial military forces have already arrived in batches at the border between the two nations. You adjust your glasses and carefully read the negotiation treaty on the table. The demands for compensation and future trade are simply unacceptable; Uzyanta cannot afford such costs.\nThe smug expression on the opposing minister's face makes you feel disgusted, and you almost can't resist the urge to punch his ugly nose."
},
	[112237]={ language="The traveler encountered a group of Infeno researchers being attacked by monsters on the road and generously rescued them.\n[Thank you for your heroic intervention.] The lead researcher shook his hand, the damaged mechanical eye glowing with a red alert light, [But you've damaged our experimental items.]\nHis mechanical voice was cold and ruthless, [You are also a human; please uphold your virtues and help us continue our research.]"
},
	[112238]={ language="After deciphering parts of the Creator's genetic fragments, Infeno celebrated nationwide, but in the Elder Council in Puruis City, His Majesty sighed as Chief Administrator of Lancelot and Duke Campbell argued heatedly like two roosters.\n[We must abandon everything and continue researching higher civilizations, deciphering the fragments gifted by the Creator. Only then can Infeno distance itself from humans,] Duke Campbell declared righteously.\n[But before taking that step, Infeno must first eliminate external threats. We cannot abandon research in other areas of Technology,] Chief Administrator loudly retorted.\nThey looked towards His Majesty the Emperor."
},
	[112239]={ language="Three hours have passed since the destruction of Puruis, and Mutants and Shoggers are still pouring out from there continuously. The remaining border guards are exhausted and about to be overwhelmed.\n[Only the last batch of survivors hasn't evacuated yet!] someone shouted loudly, [Hang in there, everyone! For the glory of Infeno!]\n[For the glory of Infeno,] everyone shouted together.\nBut not far away, more Shoggers and Mutants appeared."
},
