	[10000591]={ language="A young nation that encourages innovation and development. Every industry within its borders brims with vitality and dynamism."
},
	[10000592]={ language="A small, multi-faceted alliance whose member states advance hand in hand, sharing both fair winds and storms."
},
	[10000593]={ language="A peculiar region in the continent's far north, shrouded by the Void Expanse. It remains an enigma to this day."
},
	[10000594]={ language="A heavy-industrial northern nation, rich in natural resources. Divinelight Heavy Tech is the lifeblood of its people."
},
	[10000595]={ language="An ancient nation separated by the sea. In the current era, contact with it is only occasional."
},
	[10000596]={ language="A stateless combat organization dedicated to handling Shogger-related incidents. Its headquarters is a massive warship floating in the sky."
},
	[10000597]={ language="An alliance of major powers. The three members share distinct histories and cultures, yet coexist in harmony."
},
	[10000598]={ language="To this day, their origins remain unknown."
},
	[10000599]={ language="A prosperous mercantile republic where commerce is universal, fostering an environment of fierce competition and boundless growth."
},
	[10000600]={ language="An aristocratic state proficient in energy technology, renowned externally for its machinery manufacturing. It stands on the brink of transformation in the new age."
},
	[10000601]={ language="A nation that reveres knowledge and art, a paradise for scholars, and the academic holy land of Taino Star."
},
	[10000602]={ language="A former great power, it reveres nature and is now Taino's largest 'Fortress Greenhouse.'"
},
	[10000603]={ language="Officially the United States of Uzyanta. Clan-based politics prevail here, alongside starkly uneven economic development."
},
	[10000604]={ language="A nation that venerates the stars as its faith, with a rigid internal hierarchy. Many of its secrets remain buried."
},
	[10000605]={ language="An overseas enclave of Joshburg and the location of a Leistance branch office, possessing a degree of autonomy."
},
	[10000606]={ language="Tap blank area to return"
},
	[10000607]={ language="The anchor space of the Omen Star—the 'Divine Kingdom'—has finally descended upon the real world. An all-out war between Leistance and the Apostle-class Shogger has begun. Trapped within the Divine Kingdom alongside Zephyrine, you are caught in an endless cycle of death and rebirth. As fate approaches its end, you face a choice: to forge life from death, or to plummet into the abyss..."
},
	[10000608]={ language="After the battle of Vilatria, a brief peace was yours, only to be shattered by a recurring nightmare. To resolve the instability of the D-Blood Link, you you follow leads from Bureau and journey to the Arctic, arriving at the ancient city shrouded in perpetual snow..."
}
}

return language